ob": 1.2595591887196167e-12}, {"id": 5, "seek": 0, "start": 24.7, "end": 28.42, "text": " We inherently crave that kind of epistemic comfort, I think.", "tokens": [51600, 492, 27993, 46875, 300, 733, 295, 2388, 468, 3438, 3400, 11, 286, 519, 13, 51786], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09126614161900111, "compression_ratio": 1.6394984326018809, "no_speech_prob": 1.2595591887196167e-12}, {"id": 6, "seek": 2842, "start": 28.42, "end": 36.38, "text": " We want the truth to be something we can just, you know, point to, categorize, and lock away as a totally solved problem.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 528, 264, 3494, 281, 312, 746, 321, 393, 445, 11, 291, 458, 11, 935, 281, 11, 19250, 1125, 11, 293, 4017, 1314, 382, 257, 3879, 13041, 1154, 13, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08572704180152016, "compression_ratio": 1.583941605839416, "no_speech_prob": 7.520641553092344e-13}, {"id": 7, "seek": 2842, "start": 36.56, "end": 38.72, "text": " But like, suddenly that x-ray machine is broken.", "tokens": [50772, 583, 411, 11, 5800, 300, 2031, 12, 3458, 3479, 307, 5463, 13, 50880], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08572704180152016, "compression_ratio": 1.583941605839416, "no_speech_prob": 7.520641553092344e-13}, {"id": 8, "seek": 2842, "start": 39.28, "end": 48.38, "text": " You step into the world of, say, neurodevelopment, or these really complex autoimmune diseases, and we're looking at a diagnostic landscape that is just entirely marky.", "tokens": [50908, 509, 1823, 666, 264, 1002, 295, 11, 584, 11, 16499, 35464, 518, 11, 420, 613, 534, 3997, 8399, 49031, 11044, 11, 293, 321, 434, 1237, 412, 257, 27897, 9661, 300, 307, 445, 7696, 1491, 88, 13, 51363], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08572704180152016, "compression_ratio": 1.583941605839416, "no_speech_prob": 7.520641553092344e-13}, {"id": 9, "seek": 2842, "start": 48.46, "end": 48.980000000000004, "text": " Oh, absolutely.", "tokens": [51367, 876, 11, 3122, 13, 51393], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08572704180152016, "compression_ratio": 1.583941605839416, "no_speech_prob": 7.520641553092344e-13}, {"id": 10, "seek": 2842, "start": 49.160000000000004, "end": 53.620000000000005, "text": " You can't just point to a single pixel and say, hey, there is the exact truth.", "tokens": [51402, 509, 393, 380, 445, 935, 281, 257, 2167, 19261, 293, 584, 11, 4177, 11, 456, 307, 264, 1900, 3494, 13, 51625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08572704180152016, "compression_ratio": 1.583941605839416, "no_speech_prob": 7.520641553092344e-13}, {"id": 11, "seek": 5362, "start": 53.62, "end": 63.699999999999996, "text": " Right, and it turns out that terrifying lack of a clean binary x-ray is happening right now, at this very moment, in the documents that you read every single day.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 11, 293, 309, 4523, 484, 300, 18106, 5011, 295, 257, 2541, 17434, 2031, 12, 3458, 307, 2737, 558, 586, 11, 412, 341, 588, 1623, 11, 294, 264, 8512, 300, 291, 1401, 633, 2167, 786, 13, 50869], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07881012057313824, "compression_ratio": 1.6040816326530611, "no_speech_prob": 1.1200139123437869e-12}, {"id": 12, "seek": 5362, "start": 63.839999999999996, "end": 64.94, "text": " Yeah, it really is.", "tokens": [50876, 865, 11, 309, 534, 307, 13, 50931], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07881012057313824, "compression_ratio": 1.6040816326530611, "no_speech_prob": 1.1200139123437869e-12}, {"id": 13, "seek": 5362, "start": 65.16, "end": 74.94, "text": " If a trusted system verifies a fact, and then, you know, an AI rephrases it, or translates it, or summarizes it for you, does the truth actually survive that transformation?", "tokens": [50942, 759, 257, 16034, 1185, 1306, 11221, 257, 1186, 11, 293, 550, 11, 291, 458, 11, 364, 7318, 319, 44598, 1957, 309, 11, 420, 28468, 309, 11, 420, 14611, 5660, 309, 337, 291, 11, 775, 264, 3494, 767, 7867, 300, 9887, 30, 51431], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07881012057313824, "compression_ratio": 1.6040816326530611, "no_speech_prob": 1.1200139123437869e-12}, {"id": 14, "seek": 5362, "start": 75.22, "end": 77.17999999999999, "text": " That is the million-dollar question.", "tokens": [51445, 663, 307, 264, 2459, 12, 40485, 1168, 13, 51543], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07881012057313824, "compression_ratio": 1.6040816326530611, "no_speech_prob": 1.1200139123437869e-12}, {"id": 15, "seek": 7718, "start": 77.18, "end": 78.0, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 534, 307, 13, 50406], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13607961405878483, "compression_ratio": 1.5667752442996743, "no_speech_prob": 1.466481233322603e-12}, {"id": 16, "seek": 7718, "start": 78.32000000000001, "end": 84.76, "text": " So today, we're taking a deep dive into an absolutely massive problem in the world of information infrastructure.", "tokens": [50422, 407, 965, 11, 321, 434, 1940, 257, 2452, 9192, 666, 364, 3122, 5994, 1154, 294, 264, 1002, 295, 1589, 6896, 13, 50744], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13607961405878483, "compression_ratio": 1.5667752442996743, "no_speech_prob": 1.466481233322603e-12}, {"id": 17, "seek": 7718, "start": 85.14, "end": 90.5, "text": " We're exploring this specific, incredibly dense research package called ClaimShift.", "tokens": [50763, 492, 434, 12736, 341, 2685, 11, 6252, 18011, 2132, 7372, 1219, 383, 10970, 7774, 2008, 13, 51031], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13607961405878483, "compression_ratio": 1.5667752442996743, "no_speech_prob": 1.466481233322603e-12}, {"id": 18, "seek": 7718, "start": 90.78, "end": 91.92, "text": " Yeah, it's quite the read.", "tokens": [51045, 865, 11, 309, 311, 1596, 264, 1401, 13, 51102], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13607961405878483, "compression_ratio": 1.5667752442996743, "no_speech_prob": 1.466481233322603e-12}, {"id": 19, "seek": 7718, "start": 92.02000000000001, "end": 92.68, "text": " It's massive.", "tokens": [51107, 467, 311, 5994, 13, 51140], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13607961405878483, "compression_ratio": 1.5667752442996743, "no_speech_prob": 1.466481233322603e-12}, {"id": 20, "seek": 7718, "start": 93.16000000000001, "end": 97.72, "text": " It was authored by an independent researcher named Fliction back in August of 2026.", "tokens": [51164, 467, 390, 6979, 2769, 538, 364, 6695, 21751, 4926, 3235, 4105, 646, 294, 6897, 295, 945, 10880, 13, 51392], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13607961405878483, "compression_ratio": 1.5667752442996743, "no_speech_prob": 1.466481233322603e-12}, {"id": 21, "seek": 7718, "start": 98.32000000000001, "end": 105.94000000000001, "text": " And the goal here is to figure out why the tech industry's current solution to this whole problem is, well, essentially a mathematical illusion.", "tokens": [51422, 400, 264, 3387, 510, 307, 281, 2573, 484, 983, 264, 7553, 3518, 311, 2190, 3827, 281, 341, 1379, 1154, 307, 11, 731, 11, 4476, 257, 18894, 18854, 13, 51803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13607961405878483, "compression_ratio": 1.5667752442996743, "no_speech_prob": 1.466481233322603e-12}, {"id": 22, "seek": 10594, "start": 105.94, "end": 109.5, "text": " It really is the defining epistemic crisis of our time, honestly.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 534, 307, 264, 17827, 2388, 468, 3438, 5869, 295, 527, 565, 11, 6095, 13, 50543], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10071284711853531, "compression_ratio": 1.5865724381625441, "no_speech_prob": 1.5248953358706907e-12}, {"id": 23, "seek": 10594, "start": 109.74, "end": 110.84, "text": " I mean, no pressure, right?", "tokens": [50555, 286, 914, 11, 572, 3321, 11, 558, 30, 50610], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10071284711853531, "compression_ratio": 1.5865724381625441, "no_speech_prob": 1.5248953358706907e-12}, {"id": 24, "seek": 10594, "start": 110.94, "end": 112.14, "text": " Oh, yeah, no pressure at all.", "tokens": [50615, 876, 11, 1338, 11, 572, 3321, 412, 439, 13, 50675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10071284711853531, "compression_ratio": 1.5865724381625441, "no_speech_prob": 1.5248953358706907e-12}, {"id": 25, "seek": 10594, "start": 112.52, "end": 118.32, "text": " But what makes Fliction's work so vital is that it isn't just, you know, a philosophical complaint about AI.", "tokens": [50694, 583, 437, 1669, 3235, 4105, 311, 589, 370, 11707, 307, 300, 309, 1943, 380, 445, 11, 291, 458, 11, 257, 25066, 20100, 466, 7318, 13, 50984], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10071284711853531, "compression_ratio": 1.5865724381625441, "no_speech_prob": 1.5248953358706907e-12}, {"id": 26, "seek": 10594, "start": 118.46, "end": 119.98, "text": " People complain about AI all the time.", "tokens": [50991, 3432, 11024, 466, 7318, 439, 264, 565, 13, 51067], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10071284711853531, "compression_ratio": 1.5865724381625441, "no_speech_prob": 1.5248953358706907e-12}, {"id": 27, "seek": 10594, "start": 120.03999999999999, "end": 120.75999999999999, "text": " Right, exactly.", "tokens": [51070, 1779, 11, 2293, 13, 51106], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10071284711853531, "compression_ratio": 1.5865724381625441, "no_speech_prob": 1.5248953358706907e-12}, {"id": 28, "seek": 10594, "start": 121.02, "end": 127.52, "text": " But this is a rigorous, three-part mathematical teardown and rebuild of how we actually track truth.", "tokens": [51119, 583, 341, 307, 257, 29882, 11, 1045, 12, 6971, 18894, 535, 515, 648, 293, 16877, 295, 577, 321, 767, 2837, 3494, 13, 51444], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10071284711853531, "compression_ratio": 1.5865724381625441, "no_speech_prob": 1.5248953358706907e-12}, {"id": 29, "seek": 10594, "start": 127.64, "end": 130.3, "text": " And we've got three distinct pieces of source material here.", "tokens": [51450, 400, 321, 600, 658, 1045, 10644, 3755, 295, 4009, 2527, 510, 13, 51583], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10071284711853531, "compression_ratio": 1.5865724381625441, "no_speech_prob": 1.5248953358706907e-12}, {"id": 30, "seek": 13030, "start": 130.3, "end": 131.02, "text": " We do.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 360, 13, 50401], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12526115087362436, "compression_ratio": 1.64, "no_speech_prob": 1.7963632968284737e-12}, {"id": 31, "seek": 13030, "start": 131.42000000000002, "end": 137.06, "text": " We're looking at paper one, which establishes the hard mathematical boundaries of what is even possible to verify.", "tokens": [50421, 492, 434, 1237, 412, 3035, 472, 11, 597, 8327, 279, 264, 1152, 18894, 13180, 295, 437, 307, 754, 1944, 281, 16888, 13, 50703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12526115087362436, "compression_ratio": 1.64, "no_speech_prob": 1.7963632968284737e-12}, {"id": 32, "seek": 13030, "start": 137.24, "end": 137.38000000000002, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50712, 1033, 13, 50719], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12526115087362436, "compression_ratio": 1.64, "no_speech_prob": 1.7963632968284737e-12}, {"id": 33, "seek": 13030, "start": 137.58, "end": 143.98000000000002, "text": " Then there is paper two, which designs a completely new software protocol to operate, like, within those boundaries.", "tokens": [50729, 1396, 456, 307, 3035, 732, 11, 597, 11347, 257, 2584, 777, 4722, 10336, 281, 9651, 11, 411, 11, 1951, 729, 13180, 13, 51049], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12526115087362436, "compression_ratio": 1.64, "no_speech_prob": 1.7963632968284737e-12}, {"id": 34, "seek": 13030, "start": 144.10000000000002, "end": 145.3, "text": " Which is super practical.", "tokens": [51055, 3013, 307, 1687, 8496, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12526115087362436, "compression_ratio": 1.64, "no_speech_prob": 1.7963632968284737e-12}, {"id": 35, "seek": 13030, "start": 145.48000000000002, "end": 145.66000000000003, "text": " Very.", "tokens": [51124, 4372, 13, 51133], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12526115087362436, "compression_ratio": 1.64, "no_speech_prob": 1.7963632968284737e-12}, {"id": 36, "seek": 13030, "start": 146.12, "end": 154.64000000000001, "text": " And finally, paper three, which is this open-source GitHub repository where they actually took a mathematical specimen and violently mutated it to prove their protocol works.", "tokens": [51156, 400, 2721, 11, 3035, 1045, 11, 597, 307, 341, 1269, 12, 41676, 23331, 25841, 689, 436, 767, 1890, 257, 18894, 34204, 293, 46728, 5839, 770, 309, 281, 7081, 641, 10336, 1985, 13, 51582], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12526115087362436, "compression_ratio": 1.64, "no_speech_prob": 1.7963632968284737e-12}, {"id": 37, "seek": 15464, "start": 154.64, "end": 155.98, "text": " Okay, let's unpack this.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 26699, 341, 13, 50432], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10131804411076317, "compression_ratio": 1.6113074204946995, "no_speech_prob": 1.9499371735343107e-12}, {"id": 38, "seek": 15464, "start": 156.51999999999998, "end": 164.5, "text": " To really understand why all this heavy math is necessary, we have to start by dismantling the illusion that we are currently living under, right?", "tokens": [50459, 1407, 534, 1223, 983, 439, 341, 4676, 5221, 307, 4818, 11, 321, 362, 281, 722, 538, 30506, 1688, 264, 18854, 300, 321, 366, 4362, 2647, 833, 11, 558, 30, 50858], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10131804411076317, "compression_ratio": 1.6113074204946995, "no_speech_prob": 1.9499371735343107e-12}, {"id": 39, "seek": 15464, "start": 164.67999999999998, "end": 165.0, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50867, 1079, 13, 50883], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10131804411076317, "compression_ratio": 1.6113074204946995, "no_speech_prob": 1.9499371735343107e-12}, {"id": 40, "seek": 15464, "start": 165.5, "end": 167.92, "text": " We have to break down the current paradigm.", "tokens": [50908, 492, 362, 281, 1821, 760, 264, 2190, 24709, 13, 51029], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10131804411076317, "compression_ratio": 1.6113074204946995, "no_speech_prob": 1.9499371735343107e-12}, {"id": 41, "seek": 15464, "start": 168.14, "end": 169.51999999999998, "text": " And I'm talking about watermarks.", "tokens": [51040, 400, 286, 478, 1417, 466, 1281, 37307, 13, 51109], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10131804411076317, "compression_ratio": 1.6113074204946995, "no_speech_prob": 1.9499371735343107e-12}, {"id": 42, "seek": 15464, "start": 169.61999999999998, "end": 173.76, "text": " If you, you know, follow the text space even a little bit, you see this everywhere right now.", "tokens": [51114, 759, 291, 11, 291, 458, 11, 1524, 264, 2487, 1901, 754, 257, 707, 857, 11, 291, 536, 341, 5315, 558, 586, 13, 51321], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10131804411076317, "compression_ratio": 1.6113074204946995, "no_speech_prob": 1.9499371735343107e-12}, {"id": 43, "seek": 15464, "start": 173.76, "end": 175.07999999999998, "text": " Oh, it's inescapable.", "tokens": [51321, 876, 11, 309, 311, 294, 279, 9485, 712, 13, 51387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10131804411076317, "compression_ratio": 1.6113074204946995, "no_speech_prob": 1.9499371735343107e-12}, {"id": 44, "seek": 15464, "start": 175.2, "end": 180.72, "text": " We have these steganographic text watermarks embedded in the actual spacing of words.", "tokens": [51393, 492, 362, 613, 342, 43118, 12295, 2487, 1281, 37307, 16741, 294, 264, 3539, 27739, 295, 2283, 13, 51669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10131804411076317, "compression_ratio": 1.6113074204946995, "no_speech_prob": 1.9499371735343107e-12}, {"id": 45, "seek": 18072, "start": 180.72, "end": 188.62, "text": " We have, like, C2PA content credentials cryptographically sealed into the metadata of images.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 362, 11, 411, 11, 383, 17, 10297, 2701, 27404, 9844, 3108, 984, 21514, 666, 264, 26603, 295, 5267, 13, 50760], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1060190781303074, "compression_ratio": 1.5912162162162162, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856402562491878e-12}, {"id": 46, "seek": 18072, "start": 188.9, "end": 190.32, "text": " Right, the digital provenance industry.", "tokens": [50774, 1779, 11, 264, 4562, 12785, 719, 3518, 13, 50845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1060190781303074, "compression_ratio": 1.5912162162162162, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856402562491878e-12}, {"id": 47, "seek": 18072, "start": 190.62, "end": 190.9, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50860, 865, 13, 50874], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1060190781303074, "compression_ratio": 1.5912162162162162, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856402562491878e-12}, {"id": 48, "seek": 18072, "start": 191.28, "end": 199.06, "text": " It's a billion-dollar industry built on the idea of attaching a digital badge to a file that basically says, this came from a trusted source.", "tokens": [50893, 467, 311, 257, 5218, 12, 40485, 3518, 3094, 322, 264, 1558, 295, 39074, 257, 4562, 25797, 281, 257, 3991, 300, 1936, 1619, 11, 341, 1361, 490, 257, 16034, 4009, 13, 51282], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1060190781303074, "compression_ratio": 1.5912162162162162, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856402562491878e-12}, {"id": 49, "seek": 18072, "start": 199.34, "end": 200.18, "text": " It is everywhere.", "tokens": [51296, 467, 307, 5315, 13, 51338], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1060190781303074, "compression_ratio": 1.5912162162162162, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856402562491878e-12}, {"id": 50, "seek": 18072, "start": 200.64, "end": 205.02, "text": " You've got Adobe, the major camera manufacturers, massive news organizations.", "tokens": [51361, 509, 600, 658, 24862, 11, 264, 2563, 2799, 18455, 11, 5994, 2583, 6150, 13, 51580], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1060190781303074, "compression_ratio": 1.5912162162162162, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856402562491878e-12}, {"id": 51, "seek": 18072, "start": 205.02, "end": 209.72, "text": " They're all rushing to attach these cryptographic anchors to their media.", "tokens": [51580, 814, 434, 439, 25876, 281, 5085, 613, 9844, 12295, 12723, 830, 281, 641, 3021, 13, 51815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1060190781303074, "compression_ratio": 1.5912162162162162, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856402562491878e-12}, {"id": 52, "seek": 18072, "start": 209.72, "end": 210.66, "text": " And they mean well.", "tokens": [51815, 400, 436, 914, 731, 13, 51862], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1060190781303074, "compression_ratio": 1.5912162162162162, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856402562491878e-12}, {"id": 53, "seek": 21072, "start": 210.94, "end": 211.0, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50376, 1779, 13, 50379], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18432777806332237, "compression_ratio": 1.6129032258064515, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783429471906806e-12}, {"id": 54, "seek": 21072, "start": 211.02, "end": 211.68, "text": " Oh, absolutely.", "tokens": [50380, 876, 11, 3122, 13, 50413], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18432777806332237, "compression_ratio": 1.6129032258064515, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783429471906806e-12}, {"id": 55, "seek": 21072, "start": 211.88, "end": 215.35999999999999, "text": " They're doing it with the best of intentions, mostly to fight disinformation.", "tokens": [50423, 814, 434, 884, 309, 365, 264, 1151, 295, 19354, 11, 5240, 281, 2092, 717, 20941, 13, 50597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18432777806332237, "compression_ratio": 1.6129032258064515, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783429471906806e-12}, {"id": 56, "seek": 21072, "start": 216.42, "end": 219.92, "text": " But Flifshin's first paper points out a massive issue with this.", "tokens": [50650, 583, 3235, 351, 2716, 259, 311, 700, 3035, 2793, 484, 257, 5994, 2734, 365, 341, 13, 50825], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18432777806332237, "compression_ratio": 1.6129032258064515, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783429471906806e-12}, {"id": 57, "seek": 21072, "start": 220.04, "end": 220.56, "text": " Which is?", "tokens": [50831, 3013, 307, 30, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18432777806332237, "compression_ratio": 1.6129032258064515, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783429471906806e-12}, {"id": 58, "seek": 21072, "start": 220.64, "end": 230.26, "text": " Well, treating these watermarks as evidence of the continued validity of the information inside the document is a massive structural category error.", "tokens": [50861, 1042, 11, 15083, 613, 1281, 37307, 382, 4467, 295, 264, 7014, 40943, 295, 264, 1589, 1854, 264, 4166, 307, 257, 5994, 15067, 7719, 6713, 13, 51342], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18432777806332237, "compression_ratio": 1.6129032258064515, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783429471906806e-12}, {"id": 59, "seek": 21072, "start": 230.5, "end": 231.38, "text": " A category error.", "tokens": [51354, 316, 7719, 6713, 13, 51398], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18432777806332237, "compression_ratio": 1.6129032258064515, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783429471906806e-12}, {"id": 60, "seek": 21072, "start": 231.38, "end": 236.86, "text": " Okay, I want to really dig into the mechanics of that because it sounds counterintuitive at first.", "tokens": [51398, 1033, 11, 286, 528, 281, 534, 2528, 666, 264, 12939, 295, 300, 570, 309, 3263, 5682, 686, 48314, 412, 700, 13, 51672], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18432777806332237, "compression_ratio": 1.6129032258064515, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783429471906806e-12}, {"id": 61, "seek": 21072, "start": 237.24, "end": 237.56, "text": " It does.", "tokens": [51691, 467, 775, 13, 51707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18432777806332237, "compression_ratio": 1.6129032258064515, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783429471906806e-12}, {"id": 62, "seek": 23756, "start": 237.56, "end": 244.68, "text": " Like, if I have a cryptographically secure watermark on a document, doesn't that inherently mean the document itself is secure?", "tokens": [50365, 1743, 11, 498, 286, 362, 257, 9844, 3108, 984, 7144, 1281, 5638, 322, 257, 4166, 11, 1177, 380, 300, 27993, 914, 264, 4166, 2564, 307, 7144, 30, 50721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1018555736541748, "compression_ratio": 1.465648854961832, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813162190612574e-12}, {"id": 63, "seek": 23756, "start": 244.84, "end": 247.18, "text": " No, it means the lineage of the document is secure.", "tokens": [50729, 883, 11, 309, 1355, 264, 38257, 295, 264, 4166, 307, 7144, 13, 50846], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1018555736541748, "compression_ratio": 1.465648854961832, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813162190612574e-12}, {"id": 64, "seek": 23756, "start": 247.34, "end": 247.78, "text": " The lineage.", "tokens": [50854, 440, 38257, 13, 50876], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1018555736541748, "compression_ratio": 1.465648854961832, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813162190612574e-12}, {"id": 65, "seek": 24778, "start": 247.78, "end": 248.26, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20409632565682395, "compression_ratio": 1.4055944055944056, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465504732917415e-12}, {"id": 66, "seek": 24778, "start": 248.26, "end": 249.66, "text": " It means the pointer is intact.", "tokens": [50389, 467, 1355, 264, 23918, 307, 23493, 13, 50459], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20409632565682395, "compression_ratio": 1.4055944055944056, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465504732917415e-12}, {"id": 67, "seek": 24778, "start": 249.9, "end": 255.72, "text": " But the paper is so explicit here, the persistence of a pointer cannot stand in for the validity of the claim it points to.", "tokens": [50471, 583, 264, 3035, 307, 370, 13691, 510, 11, 264, 37617, 295, 257, 23918, 2644, 1463, 294, 337, 264, 40943, 295, 264, 3932, 309, 2793, 281, 13, 50762], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20409632565682395, "compression_ratio": 1.4055944055944056, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465504732917415e-12}, {"id": 68, "seek": 24778, "start": 256.02, "end": 256.42, "text": " Okay, wait.", "tokens": [50777, 1033, 11, 1699, 13, 50797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20409632565682395, "compression_ratio": 1.4055944055944056, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465504732917415e-12}, {"id": 69, "seek": 24778, "start": 256.56, "end": 257.44, "text": " Explain that a bit more.", "tokens": [50804, 39574, 300, 257, 857, 544, 13, 50848], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20409632565682395, "compression_ratio": 1.4055944055944056, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465504732917415e-12}, {"id": 70, "seek": 25744, "start": 257.44, "end": 269.7, "text": " So, a C2PA credential or a robust nano publication, all it really proves is that the digital artifact you are looking at traces its ancestry back to an earlier verified artifact.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 257, 383, 17, 10297, 22034, 420, 257, 13956, 30129, 19953, 11, 439, 309, 534, 25019, 307, 300, 264, 4562, 34806, 291, 366, 1237, 412, 26076, 1080, 44729, 646, 281, 364, 3071, 31197, 34806, 13, 50978], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13705750703811645, "compression_ratio": 1.328358208955224, "no_speech_prob": 1.3142695482262767e-12}, {"id": 71, "seek": 26970, "start": 269.7, "end": 270.92, "text": " Like a birth certificate.", "tokens": [50365, 1743, 257, 3965, 15953, 13, 50426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10401270939753605, "compression_ratio": 1.5654008438818565, "no_speech_prob": 1.4102997198880973e-12}, {"id": 72, "seek": 26970, "start": 271.14, "end": 272.32, "text": " It's a perfect way to look at it.", "tokens": [50437, 467, 311, 257, 2176, 636, 281, 574, 412, 309, 13, 50496], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10401270939753605, "compression_ratio": 1.5654008438818565, "no_speech_prob": 1.4102997198880973e-12}, {"id": 73, "seek": 26970, "start": 272.56, "end": 283.76, "text": " It proves the file was born in the right hospital, but it tells you absolutely nothing about whether the semantic meaning, the actual truth of the words on the page, survived whatever transformation happened between there and here.", "tokens": [50508, 467, 25019, 264, 3991, 390, 4232, 294, 264, 558, 4530, 11, 457, 309, 5112, 291, 3122, 1825, 466, 1968, 264, 47982, 3620, 11, 264, 3539, 3494, 295, 264, 2283, 322, 264, 3028, 11, 14433, 2035, 9887, 2011, 1296, 456, 293, 510, 13, 51068], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10401270939753605, "compression_ratio": 1.5654008438818565, "no_speech_prob": 1.4102997198880973e-12}, {"id": 74, "seek": 26970, "start": 283.86, "end": 286.03999999999996, "text": " Okay, this makes me think of, like, a recipe.", "tokens": [51073, 1033, 11, 341, 1669, 385, 519, 295, 11, 411, 11, 257, 6782, 13, 51182], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10401270939753605, "compression_ratio": 1.5654008438818565, "no_speech_prob": 1.4102997198880973e-12}, {"id": 75, "seek": 26970, "start": 286.3, "end": 287.53999999999996, "text": " Okay, I like where this is going.", "tokens": [51195, 1033, 11, 286, 411, 689, 341, 307, 516, 13, 51257], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10401270939753605, "compression_ratio": 1.5654008438818565, "no_speech_prob": 1.4102997198880973e-12}, {"id": 76, "seek": 28754, "start": 287.54, "end": 295.78000000000003, "text": " Let's say I have a master baker's award-winning recipe for chocolate cake, and the baker signs it with an unbreakable cryptographic seal.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 311, 584, 286, 362, 257, 4505, 48148, 311, 7130, 12, 32960, 6782, 337, 6215, 5908, 11, 293, 264, 48148, 7880, 309, 365, 364, 517, 13225, 712, 9844, 12295, 12185, 13, 50777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1399044672648112, "compression_ratio": 1.6360294117647058, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191869030123373e-12}, {"id": 77, "seek": 28754, "start": 296.32, "end": 298.38, "text": " The provenance is flawless.", "tokens": [50804, 440, 12785, 719, 307, 45693, 13, 50907], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1399044672648112, "compression_ratio": 1.6360294117647058, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191869030123373e-12}, {"id": 78, "seek": 28754, "start": 298.82, "end": 299.16, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50929, 1779, 13, 50946], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1399044672648112, "compression_ratio": 1.6360294117647058, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191869030123373e-12}, {"id": 79, "seek": 28754, "start": 299.52000000000004, "end": 300.46000000000004, "text": " Unquestionable origin.", "tokens": [50964, 1156, 20343, 313, 712, 4957, 13, 51011], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1399044672648112, "compression_ratio": 1.6360294117647058, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191869030123373e-12}, {"id": 80, "seek": 28754, "start": 300.70000000000005, "end": 303.04, "text": " Now, I decide to transform that recipe.", "tokens": [51023, 823, 11, 286, 4536, 281, 4088, 300, 6782, 13, 51140], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1399044672648112, "compression_ratio": 1.6360294117647058, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191869030123373e-12}, {"id": 81, "seek": 28754, "start": 303.62, "end": 309.76, "text": " I take the text, and I swap out the instruction to use a metal baking pan, and I write in glass baking pan instead.", "tokens": [51169, 286, 747, 264, 2487, 11, 293, 286, 18135, 484, 264, 10951, 281, 764, 257, 5760, 12102, 2462, 11, 293, 286, 2464, 294, 4276, 12102, 2462, 2602, 13, 51476], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1399044672648112, "compression_ratio": 1.6360294117647058, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191869030123373e-12}, {"id": 82, "seek": 28754, "start": 310.08000000000004, "end": 310.34000000000003, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51492, 1033, 13, 51505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1399044672648112, "compression_ratio": 1.6360294117647058, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191869030123373e-12}, {"id": 83, "seek": 28754, "start": 310.46000000000004, "end": 313.34000000000003, "text": " The cryptographic signature just passes right along, right?", "tokens": [51511, 440, 9844, 12295, 13397, 445, 11335, 558, 2051, 11, 558, 30, 51655], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1399044672648112, "compression_ratio": 1.6360294117647058, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191869030123373e-12}, {"id": 84, "seek": 28754, "start": 313.58000000000004, "end": 314.98, "text": " The lineage is still there.", "tokens": [51667, 440, 38257, 307, 920, 456, 13, 51737], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1399044672648112, "compression_ratio": 1.6360294117647058, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191869030123373e-12}, {"id": 85, "seek": 31498, "start": 314.98, "end": 318.02000000000004, "text": " Yep, the software just sees a mild edit and preserves the badge.", "tokens": [50365, 7010, 11, 264, 4722, 445, 8194, 257, 15154, 8129, 293, 1183, 9054, 264, 25797, 13, 50517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12350481131981159, "compression_ratio": 1.5622775800711743, "no_speech_prob": 1.345928034822419e-12}, {"id": 86, "seek": 31498, "start": 318.34000000000003, "end": 321.04, "text": " And, honestly, the cake is probably still fine.", "tokens": [50533, 400, 11, 6095, 11, 264, 5908, 307, 1391, 920, 2489, 13, 50668], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12350481131981159, "compression_ratio": 1.5622775800711743, "no_speech_prob": 1.345928034822419e-12}, {"id": 87, "seek": 31498, "start": 321.44, "end": 326.44, "text": " The core semantic meaning, how to make a chocolate cake, basically survived the transformation.", "tokens": [50688, 440, 4965, 47982, 3620, 11, 577, 281, 652, 257, 6215, 5908, 11, 1936, 14433, 264, 9887, 13, 50938], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12350481131981159, "compression_ratio": 1.5622775800711743, "no_speech_prob": 1.345928034822419e-12}, {"id": 88, "seek": 31498, "start": 326.74, "end": 327.54, "text": " You'll still get a cake.", "tokens": [50953, 509, 603, 920, 483, 257, 5908, 13, 50993], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12350481131981159, "compression_ratio": 1.5622775800711743, "no_speech_prob": 1.345928034822419e-12}, {"id": 89, "seek": 31498, "start": 327.68, "end": 331.52000000000004, "text": " But what if, instead of the pan, I decide to swap out the sugar for salt?", "tokens": [51000, 583, 437, 498, 11, 2602, 295, 264, 2462, 11, 286, 4536, 281, 18135, 484, 264, 5076, 337, 5139, 30, 51192], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12350481131981159, "compression_ratio": 1.5622775800711743, "no_speech_prob": 1.345928034822419e-12}, {"id": 90, "seek": 31498, "start": 331.6, "end": 331.96000000000004, "text": " Oh, well.", "tokens": [51196, 876, 11, 731, 13, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12350481131981159, "compression_ratio": 1.5622775800711743, "no_speech_prob": 1.345928034822419e-12}, {"id": 91, "seek": 31498, "start": 332.26, "end": 335.72, "text": " The cryptographic signature behaves exactly the same way.", "tokens": [51229, 440, 9844, 12295, 13397, 36896, 2293, 264, 912, 636, 13, 51402], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12350481131981159, "compression_ratio": 1.5622775800711743, "no_speech_prob": 1.345928034822419e-12}, {"id": 92, "seek": 31498, "start": 335.8, "end": 336.04, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51406, 1779, 13, 51418], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12350481131981159, "compression_ratio": 1.5622775800711743, "no_speech_prob": 1.345928034822419e-12}, {"id": 93, "seek": 31498, "start": 336.38, "end": 339.32, "text": " The watermark perfectly traces back to the master baker.", "tokens": [51435, 440, 1281, 5638, 6239, 26076, 646, 281, 264, 4505, 48148, 13, 51582], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12350481131981159, "compression_ratio": 1.5622775800711743, "no_speech_prob": 1.345928034822419e-12}, {"id": 94, "seek": 33932, "start": 339.32, "end": 346.02, "text": " The provenance tool lights up green and says, verified, this originated from the master baker.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 12785, 719, 2290, 5811, 493, 3092, 293, 1619, 11, 31197, 11, 341, 31129, 490, 264, 4505, 48148, 13, 50700], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16267924241616694, "compression_ratio": 1.45, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980730194015136e-12}, {"id": 95, "seek": 33932, "start": 346.4, "end": 349.78, "text": " It tells us we're still in the exact same digital kitchen.", "tokens": [50719, 467, 5112, 505, 321, 434, 920, 294, 264, 1900, 912, 4562, 6525, 13, 50888], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16267924241616694, "compression_ratio": 1.45, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980730194015136e-12}, {"id": 96, "seek": 33932, "start": 350.21999999999997, "end": 351.4, "text": " But the cake is now poison.", "tokens": [50910, 583, 264, 5908, 307, 586, 10836, 13, 50969], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16267924241616694, "compression_ratio": 1.45, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980730194015136e-12}, {"id": 97, "seek": 33932, "start": 351.88, "end": 352.36, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50993, 7587, 13, 51017], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16267924241616694, "compression_ratio": 1.45, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980730194015136e-12}, {"id": 98, "seek": 33932, "start": 352.84, "end": 357.94, "text": " The watermark survived perfectly fine, but the edible truth of the recipe was completely destroyed.", "tokens": [51041, 440, 1281, 5638, 14433, 6239, 2489, 11, 457, 264, 30666, 3494, 295, 264, 6782, 390, 2584, 8937, 13, 51296], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16267924241616694, "compression_ratio": 1.45, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980730194015136e-12}, {"id": 99, "seek": 35794, "start": 357.94, "end": 365.74, "text": " And that, right there, is the exact vulnerability we face when we let AI systems transform verified documents.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 300, 11, 558, 456, 11, 307, 264, 1900, 24210, 321, 1851, 562, 321, 718, 7318, 3652, 4088, 31197, 8512, 13, 50755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12933928749778054, "compression_ratio": 1.4965034965034965, "no_speech_prob": 1.2790957529262847e-12}, {"id": 100, "seek": 35794, "start": 365.9, "end": 369.92, "text": " Because the AI doesn't know what sugar or salt is, conceptually.", "tokens": [50763, 1436, 264, 7318, 1177, 380, 458, 437, 5076, 420, 5139, 307, 11, 3410, 671, 13, 50964], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12933928749778054, "compression_ratio": 1.4965034965034965, "no_speech_prob": 1.2790957529262847e-12}, {"id": 101, "seek": 35794, "start": 370.06, "end": 371.72, "text": " No, it's just predicting tokens.", "tokens": [50971, 883, 11, 309, 311, 445, 32884, 22667, 13, 51054], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12933928749778054, "compression_ratio": 1.4965034965034965, "no_speech_prob": 1.2790957529262847e-12}, {"id": 102, "seek": 35794, "start": 371.88, "end": 375.32, "text": " You might have a heavily vetted, peer-reviewed financial report.", "tokens": [51062, 509, 1062, 362, 257, 10950, 371, 46508, 11, 15108, 12, 265, 1759, 292, 4669, 2275, 13, 51234], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12933928749778054, "compression_ratio": 1.4965034965034965, "no_speech_prob": 1.2790957529262847e-12}, {"id": 103, "seek": 35794, "start": 375.8, "end": 380.64, "text": " You feed it into a large language model and say, hey, summarize this for a non-technical audience.", "tokens": [51258, 509, 3154, 309, 666, 257, 2416, 2856, 2316, 293, 584, 11, 4177, 11, 20858, 341, 337, 257, 2107, 12, 29113, 804, 4034, 13, 51500], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12933928749778054, "compression_ratio": 1.4965034965034965, "no_speech_prob": 1.2790957529262847e-12}, {"id": 104, "seek": 35794, "start": 380.68, "end": 382.46, "text": " Which people do literally every single day.", "tokens": [51502, 3013, 561, 360, 3736, 633, 2167, 786, 13, 51591], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12933928749778054, "compression_ratio": 1.4965034965034965, "no_speech_prob": 1.2790957529262847e-12}, {"id": 105, "seek": 35794, "start": 382.82, "end": 383.3, "text": " Constantly.", "tokens": [51609, 8574, 3627, 13, 51633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12933928749778054, "compression_ratio": 1.4965034965034965, "no_speech_prob": 1.2790957529262847e-12}, {"id": 106, "seek": 38330, "start": 383.3, "end": 388.22, "text": " And the software environment might preserve the cryptographic watermark.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 4722, 2823, 1062, 15665, 264, 9844, 12295, 1281, 5638, 13, 50611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13002557020920974, "compression_ratio": 1.626865671641791, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039913538004602e-12}, {"id": 107, "seek": 38330, "start": 388.34000000000003, "end": 394.04, "text": " It might append a little note that says, summarized by AI, originating from verified source.", "tokens": [50617, 467, 1062, 34116, 257, 707, 3637, 300, 1619, 11, 14611, 1602, 538, 7318, 11, 4957, 990, 490, 31197, 4009, 13, 50902], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13002557020920974, "compression_ratio": 1.626865671641791, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039913538004602e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 38330, "start": 394.22, "end": 394.32, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50911, 1779, 13, 50916], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13002557020920974, "compression_ratio": 1.626865671641791, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039913538004602e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 38330, "start": 394.66, "end": 409.34000000000003, "text": " But if the AI subtly hallucinates or, say, it misinterprets a critical risk factor, reversing the entire thrust of the financial advice, the watermark will still proudly declare the document is verified.", "tokens": [50933, 583, 498, 264, 7318, 7257, 356, 35212, 259, 1024, 420, 11, 584, 11, 309, 3346, 5106, 3712, 1373, 257, 4924, 3148, 5952, 11, 14582, 278, 264, 2302, 24030, 295, 264, 4669, 5192, 11, 264, 1281, 5638, 486, 920, 33522, 19710, 264, 4166, 307, 31197, 13, 51667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13002557020920974, "compression_ratio": 1.626865671641791, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039913538004602e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 38330, "start": 409.7, "end": 411.94, "text": " Because it's still pointing to the hospital it was born in.", "tokens": [51685, 1436, 309, 311, 920, 12166, 281, 264, 4530, 309, 390, 4232, 294, 13, 51797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13002557020920974, "compression_ratio": 1.626865671641791, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039913538004602e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 41194, "start": 411.94, "end": 415.04, "text": " Exactly. We are completely conflating the container with the payload.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 492, 366, 2584, 1497, 75, 990, 264, 10129, 365, 264, 30918, 13, 50520], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12050750167281539, "compression_ratio": 1.68955223880597, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130298272950093e-12}, {"id": 112, "seek": 41194, "start": 415.38, "end": 421.78, "text": " What's fascinating to me is that other industries actually solved this exact conceptual problem decades ago.", "tokens": [50537, 708, 311, 10343, 281, 385, 307, 300, 661, 13284, 767, 13041, 341, 1900, 24106, 1154, 7878, 2057, 13, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12050750167281539, "compression_ratio": 1.68955223880597, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130298272950093e-12}, {"id": 113, "seek": 41194, "start": 422.18, "end": 425.48, "text": " What's fascinating here is how often tech forgets the past.", "tokens": [50877, 708, 311, 10343, 510, 307, 577, 2049, 7553, 2870, 82, 264, 1791, 13, 51042], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12050750167281539, "compression_ratio": 1.68955223880597, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130298272950093e-12}, {"id": 114, "seek": 41194, "start": 425.7, "end": 425.88, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51053, 865, 13, 51062], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12050750167281539, "compression_ratio": 1.68955223880597, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130298272950093e-12}, {"id": 115, "seek": 41194, "start": 426.04, "end": 428.58, "text": " The paper mentions legal sotation systems, actually.", "tokens": [51070, 440, 3035, 23844, 5089, 262, 310, 399, 3652, 11, 767, 13, 51197], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12050750167281539, "compression_ratio": 1.68955223880597, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130298272950093e-12}, {"id": 116, "seek": 41194, "start": 428.64, "end": 431.86, "text": " Right. Which immediately brings to mind things like shepherdizing a legal case.", "tokens": [51200, 1779, 13, 3013, 4258, 5607, 281, 1575, 721, 411, 402, 21676, 67, 3319, 257, 5089, 1389, 13, 51361], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12050750167281539, "compression_ratio": 1.68955223880597, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130298272950093e-12}, {"id": 117, "seek": 41194, "start": 432.02, "end": 439.1, "text": " Like, lawyers don't just point to an old physical case book and say, look, this piece of paper physically exists, therefore I win the argument.", "tokens": [51369, 1743, 11, 16219, 500, 380, 445, 935, 281, 364, 1331, 4001, 1389, 1446, 293, 584, 11, 574, 11, 341, 2522, 295, 3035, 9762, 8198, 11, 4412, 286, 1942, 264, 6770, 13, 51723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12050750167281539, "compression_ratio": 1.68955223880597, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130298272950093e-12}, {"id": 118, "seek": 41194, "start": 439.44, "end": 441.54, "text": " No. Any judge would throw them out of court.", "tokens": [51740, 883, 13, 2639, 6995, 576, 3507, 552, 484, 295, 4753, 13, 51845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12050750167281539, "compression_ratio": 1.68955223880597, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130298272950093e-12}, {"id": 119, "seek": 44154, "start": 441.54, "end": 441.88, "text": " Mm-hmm.", "tokens": [50365, 8266, 12, 10250, 13, 50382], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17889504493037356, "compression_ratio": 1.458937198067633, "no_speech_prob": 1.72793116620662e-12}, {"id": 120, "seek": 44154, "start": 442.14000000000004, "end": 446.72, "text": " The legal profession has understood the difference between a pointer and a payload for over a century.", "tokens": [50395, 440, 5089, 7032, 575, 7320, 264, 2649, 1296, 257, 23918, 293, 257, 30918, 337, 670, 257, 4901, 13, 50624], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17889504493037356, "compression_ratio": 1.458937198067633, "no_speech_prob": 1.72793116620662e-12}, {"id": 121, "seek": 44154, "start": 446.98, "end": 447.0, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50637, 865, 13, 50638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17889504493037356, "compression_ratio": 1.458937198067633, "no_speech_prob": 1.72793116620662e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 44154, "start": 447.1, "end": 456.3, "text": " If a lawyer cites a Supreme Court case from 1980, the physical, literal existence of that 1980 document is not what matters at all.", "tokens": [50643, 759, 257, 11613, 269, 3324, 257, 11032, 7873, 1389, 490, 13626, 11, 264, 4001, 11, 20411, 9123, 295, 300, 13626, 4166, 307, 406, 437, 7001, 412, 439, 13, 51103], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17889504493037356, "compression_ratio": 1.458937198067633, "no_speech_prob": 1.72793116620662e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 44154, "start": 456.5, "end": 458.86, "text": " What matters is if the law is still the law.", "tokens": [51113, 708, 7001, 307, 498, 264, 2101, 307, 920, 264, 2101, 13, 51231], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17889504493037356, "compression_ratio": 1.458937198067633, "no_speech_prob": 1.72793116620662e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 44154, "start": 459.24, "end": 459.72, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51250, 7587, 13, 51274], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17889504493037356, "compression_ratio": 1.458937198067633, "no_speech_prob": 1.72793116620662e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 45972, "start": 459.72, "end": 464.38000000000005, "text": " What matters is the semantic validity of its legal holding in the present day.", "tokens": [50365, 708, 7001, 307, 264, 47982, 40943, 295, 1080, 5089, 5061, 294, 264, 1974, 786, 13, 50598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24711060523986816, "compression_ratio": 1.3952095808383234, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555044011004605e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 45972, "start": 464.5, "end": 464.78000000000003, "text": " Mm-hmm.", "tokens": [50604, 8266, 12, 10250, 13, 50618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24711060523986816, "compression_ratio": 1.3952095808383234, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555044011004605e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 45972, "start": 464.86, "end": 468.1, "text": " Has that 1980 case been distinguished by a later court?", "tokens": [50622, 8646, 300, 13626, 1389, 668, 21702, 538, 257, 1780, 4753, 30, 50784], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24711060523986816, "compression_ratio": 1.3952095808383234, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555044011004605e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 45972, "start": 468.3, "end": 468.6, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50794, 1779, 13, 50809], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24711060523986816, "compression_ratio": 1.3952095808383234, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555044011004605e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 45972, "start": 468.82000000000005, "end": 471.64000000000004, "text": " Has its core logic been criticized by other judges?", "tokens": [50820, 8646, 1080, 4965, 9952, 668, 28011, 538, 661, 14449, 30, 50961], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24711060523986816, "compression_ratio": 1.3952095808383234, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555044011004605e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 45972, "start": 472.28000000000003, "end": 474.04, "text": " Has it been outright overruled?", "tokens": [50993, 8646, 309, 668, 35189, 670, 35972, 292, 30, 51081], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24711060523986816, "compression_ratio": 1.3952095808383234, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555044011004605e-12}, {"id": 131, "seek": 47404, "start": 474.04, "end": 482.94, "text": " Systems like shepherds citations were built specifically to track the semantic health of a claim over time and across entirely new contests.", "tokens": [50365, 27059, 411, 402, 21676, 16063, 4814, 763, 645, 3094, 4682, 281, 2837, 264, 47982, 1585, 295, 257, 3932, 670, 565, 293, 2108, 7696, 777, 660, 4409, 13, 50810], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19398795404741842, "compression_ratio": 1.2962962962962963, "no_speech_prob": 2.1676007343207626e-12}, {"id": 132, "seek": 48294, "start": 482.94, "end": 486.68, "text": " So the support doesn't just persist automatically just because the text exists?", "tokens": [50365, 407, 264, 1406, 1177, 380, 445, 13233, 6772, 445, 570, 264, 2487, 8198, 30, 50552], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1450235875447591, "compression_ratio": 1.475, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179333906298556e-12}, {"id": 133, "seek": 48294, "start": 486.86, "end": 487.08, "text": " No.", "tokens": [50561, 883, 13, 50572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1450235875447591, "compression_ratio": 1.475, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179333906298556e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 48294, "start": 487.28, "end": 490.8, "text": " The legal meaning has to be rigorously, continuously reestablished.", "tokens": [50582, 440, 5089, 3620, 575, 281, 312, 42191, 5098, 11, 15684, 319, 33542, 4173, 13, 50758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1450235875447591, "compression_ratio": 1.475, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179333906298556e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 48294, "start": 491.04, "end": 493.58, "text": " And Fliction also points to software engineering, right?", "tokens": [50770, 400, 3235, 4105, 611, 2793, 281, 4722, 7043, 11, 558, 30, 50897], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1450235875447591, "compression_ratio": 1.475, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179333906298556e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 48294, "start": 493.96, "end": 496.02, "text": " Specifically this concept of proof repair.", "tokens": [50916, 26058, 341, 3410, 295, 8177, 10535, 13, 51019], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1450235875447591, "compression_ratio": 1.475, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179333906298556e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 48294, "start": 496.24, "end": 496.4, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51030, 865, 13, 51038], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1450235875447591, "compression_ratio": 1.475, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179333906298556e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 48294, "start": 496.5, "end": 498.08, "text": " Proof repair is a huge parallel here.", "tokens": [51043, 1705, 2670, 10535, 307, 257, 2603, 8952, 510, 13, 51122], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1450235875447591, "compression_ratio": 1.475, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179333906298556e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 49808, "start": 498.08, "end": 506.18, "text": " Like if I write a piece of code and mathematically prove it is completely secure, no bugs, and then three months later I update one tiny library dependency in that code.", "tokens": [50365, 1743, 498, 286, 2464, 257, 2522, 295, 3089, 293, 44003, 7081, 309, 307, 2584, 7144, 11, 572, 15120, 11, 293, 550, 1045, 2493, 1780, 286, 5623, 472, 5870, 6405, 33621, 294, 300, 3089, 13, 50770], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1264629442829731, "compression_ratio": 1.7431506849315068, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977475840786795e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 49808, "start": 506.24, "end": 507.02, "text": " Just a version bump.", "tokens": [50773, 1449, 257, 3037, 9961, 13, 50812], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1264629442829731, "compression_ratio": 1.7431506849315068, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977475840786795e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 49808, "start": 507.3, "end": 507.52, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50826, 1779, 13, 50837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1264629442829731, "compression_ratio": 1.7431506849315068, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977475840786795e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 49808, "start": 507.62, "end": 508.35999999999996, "text": " Just a version bump.", "tokens": [50842, 1449, 257, 3037, 9961, 13, 50879], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1264629442829731, "compression_ratio": 1.7431506849315068, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977475840786795e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 49808, "start": 508.47999999999996, "end": 509.62, "text": " The code file still exists.", "tokens": [50885, 440, 3089, 3991, 920, 8198, 13, 50942], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1264629442829731, "compression_ratio": 1.7431506849315068, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977475840786795e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 49808, "start": 509.96, "end": 511.65999999999997, "text": " The file name is exactly the same.", "tokens": [50959, 440, 3991, 1315, 307, 2293, 264, 912, 13, 51044], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1264629442829731, "compression_ratio": 1.7431506849315068, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977475840786795e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 49808, "start": 512.18, "end": 518.3199999999999, "text": " But the mathematical proof of security is now entirely void until I prove that this specific update didn't break the logic.", "tokens": [51070, 583, 264, 18894, 8177, 295, 3825, 307, 586, 7696, 22009, 1826, 286, 7081, 300, 341, 2685, 5623, 994, 380, 1821, 264, 9952, 13, 51377], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1264629442829731, "compression_ratio": 1.7431506849315068, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977475840786795e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 49808, "start": 518.52, "end": 518.98, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51387, 48746, 736, 13, 51410], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1264629442829731, "compression_ratio": 1.7431506849315068, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977475840786795e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 49808, "start": 519.4399999999999, "end": 523.34, "text": " The persistence of the artifact simply does not guarantee the persistence of the properties.", "tokens": [51433, 440, 37617, 295, 264, 34806, 2935, 775, 406, 10815, 264, 37617, 295, 264, 7221, 13, 51628], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1264629442829731, "compression_ratio": 1.7431506849315068, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977475840786795e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 52334, "start": 523.34, "end": 535.1, "text": " So, okay, if we accept that watermarks and provenance chains cannot actually verify the truth of a transformed document, we are left with this massive void.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 1392, 11, 498, 321, 3241, 300, 1281, 37307, 293, 12785, 719, 12626, 2644, 767, 16888, 264, 3494, 295, 257, 16894, 4166, 11, 321, 366, 1411, 365, 341, 5994, 22009, 13, 50953], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07361828127214985, "compression_ratio": 1.6233766233766234, "no_speech_prob": 2.0683533011323085e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 52334, "start": 535.7, "end": 538.14, "text": " Like how do we actually verify it then?", "tokens": [50983, 1743, 577, 360, 321, 767, 16888, 309, 550, 30, 51105], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07361828127214985, "compression_ratio": 1.6233766233766234, "no_speech_prob": 2.0683533011323085e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 52334, "start": 538.22, "end": 542.2, "text": " Well, the obvious Silicon Valley solution to this is to just throw more compute at it.", "tokens": [51109, 1042, 11, 264, 6322, 25351, 10666, 3827, 281, 341, 307, 281, 445, 3507, 544, 14722, 412, 309, 13, 51308], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07361828127214985, "compression_ratio": 1.6233766233766234, "no_speech_prob": 2.0683533011323085e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 52334, "start": 542.26, "end": 542.4, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51311, 1779, 13, 51318], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07361828127214985, "compression_ratio": 1.6233766233766234, "no_speech_prob": 2.0683533011323085e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 52334, "start": 542.48, "end": 544.6800000000001, "text": " Let me play devil's advocate for the tech industry here.", "tokens": [51322, 961, 385, 862, 13297, 311, 14608, 337, 264, 7553, 3518, 510, 13, 51432], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07361828127214985, "compression_ratio": 1.6233766233766234, "no_speech_prob": 2.0683533011323085e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 52334, "start": 544.98, "end": 551.2, "text": " If the watermark can't read the text to see if the meaning survived, why don't we just build an automated semantic checker AI?", "tokens": [51447, 759, 264, 1281, 5638, 393, 380, 1401, 264, 2487, 281, 536, 498, 264, 3620, 14433, 11, 983, 500, 380, 321, 445, 1322, 364, 18473, 47982, 1520, 260, 7318, 30, 51758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07361828127214985, "compression_ratio": 1.6233766233766234, "no_speech_prob": 2.0683533011323085e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 52334, "start": 551.4200000000001, "end": 552.6600000000001, "text": " A giant semantic checker.", "tokens": [51769, 316, 7410, 47982, 1520, 260, 13, 51831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07361828127214985, "compression_ratio": 1.6233766233766234, "no_speech_prob": 2.0683533011323085e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 55266, "start": 552.66, "end": 552.9399999999999, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 13, 50379], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13809498596191405, "compression_ratio": 1.6835016835016836, "no_speech_prob": 2.1005948716568135e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 55266, "start": 553.12, "end": 555.76, "text": " Like we have trillion parameter models now.", "tokens": [50388, 1743, 321, 362, 18723, 13075, 5245, 586, 13, 50520], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13809498596191405, "compression_ratio": 1.6835016835016836, "no_speech_prob": 2.1005948716568135e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 55266, "start": 556.12, "end": 559.52, "text": " We have models that can pass the bar exam and write complex code.", "tokens": [50538, 492, 362, 5245, 300, 393, 1320, 264, 2159, 1139, 293, 2464, 3997, 3089, 13, 50708], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13809498596191405, "compression_ratio": 1.6835016835016836, "no_speech_prob": 2.1005948716568135e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 55266, "start": 560.0, "end": 572.66, "text": " Surely we can just build a massive neural network, feed it the original verified text, feed it the new AI summarized text, and have it output a definitive universal green check mark if the underlying meaning is exactly the same.", "tokens": [50732, 29803, 321, 393, 445, 1322, 257, 5994, 18161, 3209, 11, 3154, 309, 264, 3380, 31197, 2487, 11, 3154, 309, 264, 777, 7318, 14611, 1602, 2487, 11, 293, 362, 309, 5598, 257, 28152, 11455, 3092, 1520, 1491, 498, 264, 14217, 3620, 307, 2293, 264, 912, 13, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13809498596191405, "compression_ratio": 1.6835016835016836, "no_speech_prob": 2.1005948716568135e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 55266, "start": 572.9599999999999, "end": 577.4399999999999, "text": " I mean, it is the most intuitive, seductive solution imaginable.", "tokens": [51380, 286, 914, 11, 309, 307, 264, 881, 21769, 11, 9643, 11130, 488, 3827, 23427, 712, 13, 51604], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13809498596191405, "compression_ratio": 1.6835016835016836, "no_speech_prob": 2.1005948716568135e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 55266, "start": 577.52, "end": 578.86, "text": " It sounds totally doable.", "tokens": [51608, 467, 3263, 3879, 41183, 13, 51675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13809498596191405, "compression_ratio": 1.6835016835016836, "no_speech_prob": 2.1005948716568135e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 55266, "start": 578.98, "end": 579.4399999999999, "text": " It does.", "tokens": [51681, 467, 775, 13, 51704], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13809498596191405, "compression_ratio": 1.6835016835016836, "no_speech_prob": 2.1005948716568135e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 55266, "start": 579.74, "end": 581.38, "text": " It's also mathematically impossible.", "tokens": [51719, 467, 311, 611, 44003, 6243, 13, 51801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13809498596191405, "compression_ratio": 1.6835016835016836, "no_speech_prob": 2.1005948716568135e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 55266, "start": 581.38, "end": 581.62, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51801, 1779, 13, 51813], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13809498596191405, "compression_ratio": 1.6835016835016836, "no_speech_prob": 2.1005948716568135e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 55266, "start": 581.6999999999999, "end": 582.1, "text": " Impossible.", "tokens": [51817, 36808, 13, 51837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13809498596191405, "compression_ratio": 1.6835016835016836, "no_speech_prob": 2.1005948716568135e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 58210, "start": 582.5600000000001, "end": 582.98, "text": " Completely.", "tokens": [50388, 39978, 13, 50409], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24270842796148256, "compression_ratio": 1.3881278538812785, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182114884870981e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 58210, "start": 583.12, "end": 583.3000000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50416, 1779, 13, 50425], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24270842796148256, "compression_ratio": 1.3881278538812785, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182114884870981e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 58210, "start": 583.3000000000001, "end": 591.86, "text": " And that brings us to the core of Paper One, where Flictian builds an impenetrable mathematical wall against this entire idea.", "tokens": [50425, 400, 300, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 4965, 295, 24990, 1485, 11, 689, 3235, 985, 952, 15182, 364, 704, 268, 302, 424, 638, 18894, 2929, 1970, 341, 2302, 1558, 13, 50853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24270842796148256, "compression_ratio": 1.3881278538812785, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182114884870981e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 58210, "start": 592.0600000000001, "end": 592.28, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50863, 3153, 13, 50874], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24270842796148256, "compression_ratio": 1.3881278538812785, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182114884870981e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 58210, "start": 592.44, "end": 592.62, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50882, 1033, 13, 50891], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24270842796148256, "compression_ratio": 1.3881278538812785, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182114884870981e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 58210, "start": 593.16, "end": 597.86, "text": " A universal automated semantic checker isn't just difficult to build.", "tokens": [50918, 316, 11455, 18473, 47982, 1520, 260, 1943, 380, 445, 2252, 281, 1322, 13, 51153], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24270842796148256, "compression_ratio": 1.3881278538812785, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182114884870981e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 58210, "start": 598.2, "end": 601.78, "text": " It isn't just, you know, waiting for NVIDIA to release a slightly better GPU.", "tokens": [51170, 467, 1943, 380, 445, 11, 291, 458, 11, 3806, 337, 426, 3958, 6914, 281, 4374, 257, 4748, 1101, 18407, 13, 51349], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24270842796148256, "compression_ratio": 1.3881278538812785, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182114884870981e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 60178, "start": 601.78, "end": 606.9399999999999, "text": " It is fundamentally, theoretically impossible to create in general.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 17879, 11, 29400, 6243, 281, 1884, 294, 2674, 13, 50623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23470141840916053, "compression_ratio": 1.4797297297297298, "no_speech_prob": 3.370304686375891e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 60178, "start": 606.9399999999999, "end": 607.3399999999999, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50623, 1033, 13, 50643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23470141840916053, "compression_ratio": 1.4797297297297298, "no_speech_prob": 3.370304686375891e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 60178, "start": 607.3399999999999, "end": 614.04, "text": " I want to really dig into this because telling the AI industry that something is mathematically impossible is a massive claim.", "tokens": [50643, 286, 528, 281, 534, 2528, 666, 341, 570, 3585, 264, 7318, 3518, 300, 746, 307, 44003, 6243, 307, 257, 5994, 3932, 13, 50978], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23470141840916053, "compression_ratio": 1.4797297297297298, "no_speech_prob": 3.370304686375891e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 60178, "start": 614.04, "end": 615.3, "text": " It's a huge claim.", "tokens": [50978, 467, 311, 257, 2603, 3932, 13, 51041], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23470141840916053, "compression_ratio": 1.4797297297297298, "no_speech_prob": 3.370304686375891e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 61530, "start": 615.3, "end": 620.9, "text": " How does Fliction actually prove that an AI can never universally check if two pieces of text mean the same thing?", "tokens": [50365, 1012, 775, 3235, 4105, 767, 7081, 300, 364, 7318, 393, 1128, 43995, 1520, 498, 732, 3755, 295, 2487, 914, 264, 912, 551, 30, 50645], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09223059888155956, "compression_ratio": 1.4794520547945205, "no_speech_prob": 2.69783999827522e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 61530, "start": 620.9, "end": 626.5, "text": " Well, to do this, Fliction in first has to formalize what we actually mean by meaning the same thing.", "tokens": [50645, 1042, 11, 281, 360, 341, 11, 3235, 4105, 294, 700, 575, 281, 9860, 1125, 437, 321, 767, 914, 538, 3620, 264, 912, 551, 13, 50925], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09223059888155956, "compression_ratio": 1.4794520547945205, "no_speech_prob": 2.69783999827522e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 62650, "start": 626.5, "end": 628.02, "text": " Because language is messy.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 2856, 307, 16191, 13, 50441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2807891785152375, "compression_ratio": 1.50625, "no_speech_prob": 3.153266493402529e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 62650, "start": 628.28, "end": 628.74, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50454, 7587, 13, 50477], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2807891785152375, "compression_ratio": 1.50625, "no_speech_prob": 3.153266493402529e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 62650, "start": 629.2, "end": 630.96, "text": " In natural language, meaning is fuzzy.", "tokens": [50500, 682, 3303, 2856, 11, 3620, 307, 34710, 13, 50588], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2807891785152375, "compression_ratio": 1.50625, "no_speech_prob": 3.153266493402529e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 62650, "start": 631.26, "end": 633.76, "text": " But mathematically, we define this as correspondence.", "tokens": [50603, 583, 44003, 11, 321, 6964, 341, 382, 38135, 13, 50728], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2807891785152375, "compression_ratio": 1.50625, "no_speech_prob": 3.153266493402529e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 62650, "start": 634.26, "end": 634.82, "text": " Correspondence.", "tokens": [50753, 3925, 6663, 655, 13, 50781], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2807891785152375, "compression_ratio": 1.50625, "no_speech_prob": 3.153266493402529e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 62650, "start": 634.88, "end": 635.08, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50784, 1079, 13, 50794], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2807891785152375, "compression_ratio": 1.50625, "no_speech_prob": 3.153266493402529e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 62650, "start": 635.26, "end": 640.2, "text": " Correspondence is mutual semantic entailment between a claim and its transformed successor.", "tokens": [50803, 3925, 6663, 655, 307, 16917, 47982, 948, 864, 518, 1296, 257, 3932, 293, 1080, 16894, 31864, 13, 51050], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2807891785152375, "compression_ratio": 1.50625, "no_speech_prob": 3.153266493402529e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 64020, "start": 640.2, "end": 640.84, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 13, 50397], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15780095886765866, "compression_ratio": 1.751004016064257, "no_speech_prob": 1.768896986352464e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 64020, "start": 641.0400000000001, "end": 650.0600000000001, "text": " Mutual semantic entailment, meaning the original claim mathematically entails the new claim, and the new claim mathematically entails the original claim.", "tokens": [50407, 18517, 901, 47982, 948, 864, 518, 11, 3620, 264, 3380, 3932, 44003, 50133, 264, 777, 3932, 11, 293, 264, 777, 3932, 44003, 50133, 264, 3380, 3932, 13, 50858], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15780095886765866, "compression_ratio": 1.751004016064257, "no_speech_prob": 1.768896986352464e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 64020, "start": 650.1800000000001, "end": 650.46, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50864, 1079, 13, 50878], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15780095886765866, "compression_ratio": 1.751004016064257, "no_speech_prob": 1.768896986352464e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 64020, "start": 650.86, "end": 652.58, "text": " They are a logical two-way street.", "tokens": [50898, 814, 366, 257, 14978, 732, 12, 676, 4838, 13, 50984], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15780095886765866, "compression_ratio": 1.751004016064257, "no_speech_prob": 1.768896986352464e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 64020, "start": 652.74, "end": 653.1, "text": " Got it.", "tokens": [50992, 5803, 309, 13, 51010], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15780095886765866, "compression_ratio": 1.751004016064257, "no_speech_prob": 1.768896986352464e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 64020, "start": 653.34, "end": 658.1, "text": " So if one is true, the other is inescapably true in the exact same structures.", "tokens": [51022, 407, 498, 472, 307, 2074, 11, 264, 661, 307, 294, 279, 9485, 1188, 2074, 294, 264, 1900, 912, 9227, 13, 51260], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15780095886765866, "compression_ratio": 1.751004016064257, "no_speech_prob": 1.768896986352464e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 64020, "start": 658.5600000000001, "end": 658.86, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51283, 1779, 13, 51298], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15780095886765866, "compression_ratio": 1.751004016064257, "no_speech_prob": 1.768896986352464e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 64020, "start": 659.08, "end": 666.7800000000001, "text": " And to model whether a computer can universally decide if this mutual entailment actually exists, the paper relies on first-order logic.", "tokens": [51309, 400, 281, 2316, 1968, 257, 3820, 393, 43995, 4536, 498, 341, 16917, 948, 864, 518, 767, 8198, 11, 264, 3035, 30910, 322, 700, 12, 4687, 9952, 13, 51694], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15780095886765866, "compression_ratio": 1.751004016064257, "no_speech_prob": 1.768896986352464e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 64020, "start": 666.9200000000001, "end": 667.12, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51701, 1033, 13, 51711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15780095886765866, "compression_ratio": 1.751004016064257, "no_speech_prob": 1.768896986352464e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 66712, "start": 667.12, "end": 674.86, "text": " Specifically, they define a language over a signature, what's called the signature of the set containing P, Q, and S.", "tokens": [50365, 26058, 11, 436, 6964, 257, 2856, 670, 257, 13397, 11, 437, 311, 1219, 264, 13397, 295, 264, 992, 19273, 430, 11, 1249, 11, 293, 318, 13, 50752], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.137135678388941, "compression_ratio": 1.6492537313432836, "no_speech_prob": 2.1846040601514183e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 66712, "start": 674.96, "end": 676.76, "text": " P, Q, and S. Okay. I'm with you.", "tokens": [50757, 430, 11, 1249, 11, 293, 318, 13, 1033, 13, 286, 478, 365, 291, 13, 50847], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.137135678388941, "compression_ratio": 1.6492537313432836, "no_speech_prob": 2.1846040601514183e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 66712, "start": 676.86, "end": 680.4, "text": " In this set, P and Q are unary relation symbols.", "tokens": [50852, 682, 341, 992, 11, 430, 293, 1249, 366, 517, 822, 9721, 16944, 13, 51029], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.137135678388941, "compression_ratio": 1.6492537313432836, "no_speech_prob": 2.1846040601514183e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 66712, "start": 680.5600000000001, "end": 681.84, "text": " Unary meaning one.", "tokens": [51037, 1156, 822, 3620, 472, 13, 51101], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.137135678388941, "compression_ratio": 1.6492537313432836, "no_speech_prob": 2.1846040601514183e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 66712, "start": 682.02, "end": 682.46, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51110, 7587, 13, 51132], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.137135678388941, "compression_ratio": 1.6492537313432836, "no_speech_prob": 2.1846040601514183e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 66712, "start": 683.04, "end": 687.84, "text": " This means they take one argument, they describe a property of a single isolated object.", "tokens": [51161, 639, 1355, 436, 747, 472, 6770, 11, 436, 6786, 257, 4707, 295, 257, 2167, 14621, 2657, 13, 51401], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.137135678388941, "compression_ratio": 1.6492537313432836, "no_speech_prob": 2.1846040601514183e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 66712, "start": 688.0600000000001, "end": 691.94, "text": " Think of them like the statements X is blue or Y is a prime number.", "tokens": [51412, 6557, 295, 552, 411, 264, 12363, 1783, 307, 3344, 420, 398, 307, 257, 5835, 1230, 13, 51606], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.137135678388941, "compression_ratio": 1.6492537313432836, "no_speech_prob": 2.1846040601514183e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 66712, "start": 692.02, "end": 693.62, "text": " Okay. Single properties. That makes sense.", "tokens": [51610, 1033, 13, 31248, 7221, 13, 663, 1669, 2020, 13, 51690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.137135678388941, "compression_ratio": 1.6492537313432836, "no_speech_prob": 2.1846040601514183e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 66712, "start": 693.7, "end": 694.32, "text": " And what is S?", "tokens": [51694, 400, 437, 307, 318, 30, 51725], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.137135678388941, "compression_ratio": 1.6492537313432836, "no_speech_prob": 2.1846040601514183e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 69432, "start": 694.32, "end": 697.2800000000001, "text": " S is a relation symbol with an arity of at least two.", "tokens": [50365, 318, 307, 257, 9721, 5986, 365, 364, 594, 507, 295, 412, 1935, 732, 13, 50513], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1258373682477833, "compression_ratio": 1.6483050847457628, "no_speech_prob": 1.383365752678778e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 69432, "start": 697.48, "end": 699.86, "text": " Arity. That's the number of arguments it takes.", "tokens": [50523, 1587, 507, 13, 663, 311, 264, 1230, 295, 12869, 309, 2516, 13, 50642], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1258373682477833, "compression_ratio": 1.6483050847457628, "no_speech_prob": 1.383365752678778e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 69432, "start": 700.0600000000001, "end": 701.86, "text": " Yes. Arity just means the number of arguments.", "tokens": [50652, 1079, 13, 1587, 507, 445, 1355, 264, 1230, 295, 12869, 13, 50742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1258373682477833, "compression_ratio": 1.6483050847457628, "no_speech_prob": 1.383365752678778e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 69432, "start": 702.1, "end": 706.4200000000001, "text": " Because the arity is two or more, S describes a relationship between objects.", "tokens": [50754, 1436, 264, 594, 507, 307, 732, 420, 544, 11, 318, 15626, 257, 2480, 1296, 6565, 13, 50970], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1258373682477833, "compression_ratio": 1.6483050847457628, "no_speech_prob": 1.383365752678778e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 69432, "start": 706.58, "end": 706.9200000000001, "text": " Ah.", "tokens": [50978, 2438, 13, 50995], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1258373682477833, "compression_ratio": 1.6483050847457628, "no_speech_prob": 1.383365752678778e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 69432, "start": 707.1600000000001, "end": 713.58, "text": " So think of a statement like X is greater than Y, or X caused Y, or X is connected to Y.", "tokens": [51007, 407, 519, 295, 257, 5629, 411, 1783, 307, 5044, 813, 398, 11, 420, 1783, 7008, 398, 11, 420, 1783, 307, 4582, 281, 398, 13, 51328], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1258373682477833, "compression_ratio": 1.6483050847457628, "no_speech_prob": 1.383365752678778e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 69432, "start": 713.74, "end": 714.9200000000001, "text": " Right. So it's linking them.", "tokens": [51336, 1779, 13, 407, 309, 311, 25775, 552, 13, 51395], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1258373682477833, "compression_ratio": 1.6483050847457628, "no_speech_prob": 1.383365752678778e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 69432, "start": 715.1, "end": 717.0, "text": " But why is that distinction so critical?", "tokens": [51404, 583, 983, 307, 300, 16844, 370, 4924, 30, 51499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1258373682477833, "compression_ratio": 1.6483050847457628, "no_speech_prob": 1.383365752678778e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 71700, "start": 717.0, "end": 722.66, "text": " Why does the math suddenly care if we are talking about one object versus how two objects relate to each other?", "tokens": [50365, 1545, 775, 264, 5221, 5800, 1127, 498, 321, 366, 1417, 466, 472, 2657, 5717, 577, 732, 6565, 10961, 281, 1184, 661, 30, 50648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1435450315475464, "compression_ratio": 1.578512396694215, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724421768669282e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 71700, "start": 723.36, "end": 725.6, "text": " Because of the exponential branching it creates in logic.", "tokens": [50683, 1436, 295, 264, 21510, 9819, 278, 309, 7829, 294, 9952, 13, 50795], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1435450315475464, "compression_ratio": 1.578512396694215, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724421768669282e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 71700, "start": 726.48, "end": 733.78, "text": " If you only have a language made entirely of unary predicates, just a long list of single objects and their isolated properties,", "tokens": [50839, 759, 291, 787, 362, 257, 2856, 1027, 7696, 295, 517, 822, 47336, 1024, 11, 445, 257, 938, 1329, 295, 2167, 6565, 293, 641, 14621, 7221, 11, 51204], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1435450315475464, "compression_ratio": 1.578512396694215, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724421768669282e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 71700, "start": 734.46, "end": 736.56, "text": " first order logic is actually decidable.", "tokens": [51238, 700, 1668, 9952, 307, 767, 21937, 712, 13, 51343], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1435450315475464, "compression_ratio": 1.578512396694215, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724421768669282e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 71700, "start": 736.74, "end": 738.78, "text": " Decidable meaning a computer can solve it.", "tokens": [51352, 12427, 38089, 3620, 257, 3820, 393, 5039, 309, 13, 51454], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1435450315475464, "compression_ratio": 1.578512396694215, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724421768669282e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 73878, "start": 738.78, "end": 743.74, "text": " Exactly. A mathematician named Leopold Lohenheim proved this back in 1915.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 316, 48281, 4926, 1456, 404, 2641, 441, 1445, 268, 18673, 14617, 341, 646, 294, 1294, 5211, 13, 50613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14612743258476257, "compression_ratio": 1.343915343915344, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130223463000192e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 73878, "start": 744.3, "end": 745.62, "text": " It's known as the monadic fragment.", "tokens": [50641, 467, 311, 2570, 382, 264, 1108, 43341, 26424, 13, 50707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14612743258476257, "compression_ratio": 1.343915343915344, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130223463000192e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 73878, "start": 746.52, "end": 751.62, "text": " A computer can systematically check every isolated property because the objects don't interact.", "tokens": [50752, 316, 3820, 393, 39531, 1520, 633, 14621, 4707, 570, 264, 6565, 500, 380, 4648, 13, 51007], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14612743258476257, "compression_ratio": 1.343915343915344, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130223463000192e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 73878, "start": 751.78, "end": 753.8, "text": " Right. They are just in their own little lanes.", "tokens": [51015, 1779, 13, 814, 366, 445, 294, 641, 1065, 707, 25397, 13, 51116], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14612743258476257, "compression_ratio": 1.343915343915344, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130223463000192e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 75380, "start": 753.8, "end": 761.0799999999999, "text": " Exactly. But the absolute second you introduce a relationarity to, the moment you allow objects to relate to one another,", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 583, 264, 8236, 1150, 291, 5366, 257, 9721, 17409, 281, 11, 264, 1623, 291, 2089, 6565, 281, 10961, 281, 472, 1071, 11, 50729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13082705169427591, "compression_ratio": 1.585139318885449, "no_speech_prob": 1.4668365263745264e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 75380, "start": 761.54, "end": 765.9399999999999, "text": " the language becomes expressive enough to describe complex, overlapping structures.", "tokens": [50752, 264, 2856, 3643, 40189, 1547, 281, 6786, 3997, 11, 33535, 9227, 13, 50972], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13082705169427591, "compression_ratio": 1.585139318885449, "no_speech_prob": 1.4668365263745264e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 75380, "start": 766.0999999999999, "end": 766.9599999999999, "text": " And that breaks it.", "tokens": [50980, 400, 300, 9857, 309, 13, 51023], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13082705169427591, "compression_ratio": 1.585139318885449, "no_speech_prob": 1.4668365263745264e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 75380, "start": 767.02, "end": 769.04, "text": " That expressiveness triggers Church's theorem.", "tokens": [51026, 663, 5109, 8477, 22827, 7882, 311, 20904, 13, 51127], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13082705169427591, "compression_ratio": 1.585139318885449, "no_speech_prob": 1.4668365263745264e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 75380, "start": 769.42, "end": 772.7199999999999, "text": " Alonzo Church, the mathematician who worked alongside Alan Turing.", "tokens": [51146, 967, 266, 4765, 7882, 11, 264, 48281, 567, 2732, 12385, 16442, 314, 1345, 13, 51311], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13082705169427591, "compression_ratio": 1.585139318885449, "no_speech_prob": 1.4668365263745264e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 75380, "start": 773.04, "end": 773.56, "text": " You got it.", "tokens": [51327, 509, 658, 309, 13, 51353], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13082705169427591, "compression_ratio": 1.585139318885449, "no_speech_prob": 1.4668365263745264e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 75380, "start": 774.24, "end": 780.9399999999999, "text": " Church's theorem, which was published in 1936, states that the validity problem for first order logic is undecidable.", "tokens": [51387, 7882, 311, 20904, 11, 597, 390, 6572, 294, 1294, 11309, 11, 4368, 300, 264, 40943, 1154, 337, 700, 1668, 9952, 307, 674, 3045, 38089, 13, 51722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13082705169427591, "compression_ratio": 1.585139318885449, "no_speech_prob": 1.4668365263745264e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 75380, "start": 781.0999999999999, "end": 782.8399999999999, "text": " Okay. Can you put that in a visual for me?", "tokens": [51730, 1033, 13, 1664, 291, 829, 300, 294, 257, 5056, 337, 385, 30, 51817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13082705169427591, "compression_ratio": 1.585139318885449, "no_speech_prob": 1.4668365263745264e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 78284, "start": 782.84, "end": 789.6600000000001, "text": " Yeah. Imagine a maze. If you are in that monadic fragment, the unary one, the maze is fixed.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 13, 11739, 257, 33032, 13, 759, 291, 366, 294, 300, 1108, 43341, 26424, 11, 264, 517, 822, 472, 11, 264, 33032, 307, 6806, 13, 50706], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10161720058782314, "compression_ratio": 1.5901639344262295, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491506731926674e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 78284, "start": 790.2, "end": 797.08, "text": " A computer can just run a simple algorithm, trace the walls, and eventually find the exit, or definitively prove there isn't one.", "tokens": [50733, 316, 3820, 393, 445, 1190, 257, 2199, 9284, 11, 13508, 264, 7920, 11, 293, 4728, 915, 264, 11043, 11, 420, 28152, 356, 7081, 456, 1943, 380, 472, 13, 51077], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10161720058782314, "compression_ratio": 1.5901639344262295, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491506731926674e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 78284, "start": 797.22, "end": 799.32, "text": " It might take a while, but it's guaranteed to finish.", "tokens": [51084, 467, 1062, 747, 257, 1339, 11, 457, 309, 311, 18031, 281, 2413, 13, 51189], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10161720058782314, "compression_ratio": 1.5901639344262295, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491506731926674e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 78284, "start": 799.5400000000001, "end": 807.26, "text": " Exactly. But when you introduce relations of arity 2 or more, the maze can essentially shift its own walls based on where you stand.", "tokens": [51200, 7587, 13, 583, 562, 291, 5366, 2299, 295, 594, 507, 568, 420, 544, 11, 264, 33032, 393, 4476, 5513, 1080, 1065, 7920, 2361, 322, 689, 291, 1463, 13, 51586], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10161720058782314, "compression_ratio": 1.5901639344262295, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491506731926674e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 78284, "start": 807.32, "end": 807.76, "text": " Whoa.", "tokens": [51589, 7521, 13, 51611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10161720058782314, "compression_ratio": 1.5901639344262295, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491506731926674e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 78284, "start": 807.76, "end": 811.4200000000001, "text": " The connections between the nodes create infinite, undecidable loops.", "tokens": [51611, 440, 9271, 1296, 264, 13891, 1884, 13785, 11, 674, 3045, 38089, 16121, 13, 51794], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10161720058782314, "compression_ratio": 1.5901639344262295, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491506731926674e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 81142, "start": 811.42, "end": 816.64, "text": " There is simply no single finite algorithm, no matter how powerful the computer is,", "tokens": [50365, 821, 307, 2935, 572, 2167, 19362, 9284, 11, 572, 1871, 577, 4005, 264, 3820, 307, 11, 50626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1052395502726237, "compression_ratio": 1.4642857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325139382001528e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 81142, "start": 817.02, "end": 824.4399999999999, "text": " that can look at any arbitrary or mathematical statement in this relational language and universally calculate whether it is true in all cases.", "tokens": [50645, 300, 393, 574, 412, 604, 23211, 420, 18894, 5629, 294, 341, 38444, 2856, 293, 43995, 8873, 1968, 309, 307, 2074, 294, 439, 3331, 13, 51016], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1052395502726237, "compression_ratio": 1.4642857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325139382001528e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 81142, "start": 824.66, "end": 831.54, "text": " So how does Fliction connect Church's theorem from 1936 to, you know, a modern AI trying to summarize a PDF today?", "tokens": [51027, 407, 577, 775, 3235, 4105, 1745, 7882, 311, 20904, 490, 1294, 11309, 281, 11, 291, 458, 11, 257, 4363, 7318, 1382, 281, 20858, 257, 17752, 965, 30, 51371], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1052395502726237, "compression_ratio": 1.4642857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325139382001528e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 81142, "start": 831.66, "end": 833.36, "text": " Through a classic proof by contradiction.", "tokens": [51377, 8927, 257, 7230, 8177, 538, 34937, 13, 51462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1052395502726237, "compression_ratio": 1.4642857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325139382001528e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 81142, "start": 833.52, "end": 834.4, "text": " Okay. Walk me through it.", "tokens": [51470, 1033, 13, 10818, 385, 807, 309, 13, 51514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1052395502726237, "compression_ratio": 1.4642857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325139382001528e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 83440, "start": 834.4, "end": 839.06, "text": " Fliction says, let's pretend your Silicon Valley tech bro is completely right.", "tokens": [50365, 3235, 4105, 1619, 11, 718, 311, 11865, 428, 25351, 10666, 7553, 2006, 307, 2584, 558, 13, 50598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13841094499752846, "compression_ratio": 1.5288461538461537, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839893636847679e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 83440, "start": 839.72, "end": 844.6999999999999, "text": " Let's pretend you could build a perfect, universal, automated semantic checker.", "tokens": [50631, 961, 311, 11865, 291, 727, 1322, 257, 2176, 11, 11455, 11, 18473, 47982, 1520, 260, 13, 50880], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13841094499752846, "compression_ratio": 1.5288461538461537, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839893636847679e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 83440, "start": 844.8, "end": 845.66, "text": " The ultimate AI.", "tokens": [50885, 440, 9705, 7318, 13, 50928], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13841094499752846, "compression_ratio": 1.5288461538461537, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839893636847679e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 83440, "start": 846.1, "end": 851.06, "text": " Right. A magic black box that takes two statements and universally decides if they correspond.", "tokens": [50950, 1779, 13, 316, 5585, 2211, 2424, 300, 2516, 732, 12363, 293, 43995, 14898, 498, 436, 6805, 13, 51198], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13841094499752846, "compression_ratio": 1.5288461538461537, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839893636847679e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 83440, "start": 851.62, "end": 853.0, "text": " Let's call this the decider.", "tokens": [51226, 961, 311, 818, 341, 264, 979, 1438, 13, 51295], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13841094499752846, "compression_ratio": 1.5288461538461537, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839893636847679e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 83440, "start": 853.18, "end": 854.28, "text": " Okay. The decider.", "tokens": [51304, 1033, 13, 440, 979, 1438, 13, 51359], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13841094499752846, "compression_ratio": 1.5288461538461537, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839893636847679e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 85428, "start": 854.28, "end": 862.14, "text": " Fliction shows mathematically that if this decider actually existed, you could use it to solve the validity problem for first-order logic.", "tokens": [50365, 3235, 4105, 3110, 44003, 300, 498, 341, 979, 1438, 767, 13135, 11, 291, 727, 764, 309, 281, 5039, 264, 40943, 1154, 337, 700, 12, 4687, 9952, 13, 50758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17669240563316682, "compression_ratio": 1.6845878136200716, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043226859843718e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 85428, "start": 862.6, "end": 866.12, "text": " You could literally use it to map the unmappable maze.", "tokens": [50781, 509, 727, 3736, 764, 309, 281, 4471, 264, 517, 1696, 427, 712, 33032, 13, 50957], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17669240563316682, "compression_ratio": 1.6845878136200716, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043226859843718e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 85428, "start": 866.28, "end": 868.9, "text": " But Church already proved that mapping the maze is impossible.", "tokens": [50965, 583, 7882, 1217, 14617, 300, 18350, 264, 33032, 307, 6243, 13, 51096], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17669240563316682, "compression_ratio": 1.6845878136200716, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043226859843718e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 85428, "start": 869.16, "end": 872.02, "text": " Exactly. It creates a total logical paradox.", "tokens": [51109, 7587, 13, 467, 7829, 257, 3217, 14978, 26221, 13, 51252], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17669240563316682, "compression_ratio": 1.6845878136200716, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043226859843718e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 85428, "start": 872.38, "end": 876.38, "text": " If the universal semantic checker exists, it breaks a fundamental law of mathematics.", "tokens": [51270, 759, 264, 11455, 47982, 1520, 260, 8198, 11, 309, 9857, 257, 8088, 2101, 295, 18666, 13, 51470], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17669240563316682, "compression_ratio": 1.6845878136200716, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043226859843718e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 85428, "start": 876.5799999999999, "end": 877.0, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51480, 3153, 13, 51501], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17669240563316682, "compression_ratio": 1.6845878136200716, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043226859843718e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 85428, "start": 877.66, "end": 881.38, "text": " Therefore, the universal semantic checker cannot exist. Period.", "tokens": [51534, 7504, 11, 264, 11455, 47982, 1520, 260, 2644, 2514, 13, 34976, 13, 51720], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17669240563316682, "compression_ratio": 1.6845878136200716, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043226859843718e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 85428, "start": 881.54, "end": 882.52, "text": " That is wild.", "tokens": [51728, 663, 307, 4868, 13, 51777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17669240563316682, "compression_ratio": 1.6845878136200716, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043226859843718e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 88252, "start": 882.52, "end": 895.64, "text": " Any system, whether it's a simple Python script or a massive hundred billion parameter LLM that claims to universally and perfectly certify that a paraphrased text means the exact same thing as the original, is fundamentally lying.", "tokens": [50365, 2639, 1185, 11, 1968, 309, 311, 257, 2199, 15329, 5755, 420, 257, 5994, 3262, 5218, 13075, 441, 43, 44, 300, 9441, 281, 43995, 293, 6239, 5351, 2505, 300, 257, 36992, 1703, 1937, 2487, 1355, 264, 1900, 912, 551, 382, 264, 3380, 11, 307, 17879, 8493, 13, 51021], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09290221885398582, "compression_ratio": 1.6219931271477663, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039710792198347e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 88252, "start": 895.74, "end": 897.04, "text": " Because it mathematically has to be.", "tokens": [51026, 1436, 309, 44003, 575, 281, 312, 13, 51091], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09290221885398582, "compression_ratio": 1.6219931271477663, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039710792198347e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 88252, "start": 897.38, "end": 904.36, "text": " Yes. It is either incomplete, it's unsound, or it's secretly restricting the language it's using.", "tokens": [51108, 1079, 13, 467, 307, 2139, 31709, 11, 309, 311, 2693, 554, 11, 420, 309, 311, 22611, 1472, 37714, 264, 2856, 309, 311, 1228, 13, 51457], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09290221885398582, "compression_ratio": 1.6219931271477663, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039710792198347e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 88252, "start": 905.1999999999999, "end": 909.52, "text": " A general purpose semantic equivalence function is a mathematical fantasy.", "tokens": [51499, 316, 2674, 4334, 47982, 9052, 655, 2445, 307, 257, 18894, 13861, 13, 51715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09290221885398582, "compression_ratio": 1.6219931271477663, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039710792198347e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 88252, "start": 909.68, "end": 911.0799999999999, "text": " It will eventually hit a wall.", "tokens": [51723, 467, 486, 4728, 2045, 257, 2929, 13, 51793], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09290221885398582, "compression_ratio": 1.6219931271477663, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039710792198347e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 91108, "start": 911.08, "end": 915.5200000000001, "text": " It will eventually hit a complex relational structure where it is forced to guess.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 486, 4728, 2045, 257, 3997, 38444, 3877, 689, 309, 307, 7579, 281, 2041, 13, 50587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1087774675945903, "compression_ratio": 1.5748031496062993, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895667165004678e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 91108, "start": 916.0600000000001, "end": 919.32, "text": " And because it is guessing, it will eventually be wrong.", "tokens": [50614, 400, 570, 309, 307, 17939, 11, 309, 486, 4728, 312, 2085, 13, 50777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1087774675945903, "compression_ratio": 1.5748031496062993, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895667165004678e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 91108, "start": 919.6800000000001, "end": 922.0400000000001, "text": " This is a staggering realization, honestly.", "tokens": [50795, 639, 307, 257, 42974, 25138, 11, 6095, 13, 50913], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1087774675945903, "compression_ratio": 1.5748031496062993, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895667165004678e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 91108, "start": 922.4000000000001, "end": 934.44, "text": " We are currently rushing to build an entire future information ecosystem on the absolute assumption that AI can compress, summarize, and translate human knowledge without losing the truth.", "tokens": [50931, 492, 366, 4362, 25876, 281, 1322, 364, 2302, 2027, 1589, 11311, 322, 264, 8236, 15302, 300, 7318, 393, 14778, 11, 20858, 11, 293, 13799, 1952, 3601, 1553, 7027, 264, 3494, 13, 51533], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1087774675945903, "compression_ratio": 1.5748031496062993, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895667165004678e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 91108, "start": 934.62, "end": 935.94, "text": " Yeah, that's a whole pitch.", "tokens": [51542, 865, 11, 300, 311, 257, 1379, 7293, 13, 51608], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1087774675945903, "compression_ratio": 1.5748031496062993, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895667165004678e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 93594, "start": 935.94, "end": 940.3800000000001, "text": " And this paper just definitively proved that a machine can never universally guarantee that.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 341, 3035, 445, 28152, 356, 14617, 300, 257, 3479, 393, 1128, 43995, 10815, 300, 13, 50587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1366962377841656, "compression_ratio": 1.5598455598455598, "no_speech_prob": 1.825044672679188e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 93594, "start": 940.7600000000001, "end": 942.58, "text": " So are we completely doomed here?", "tokens": [50606, 407, 366, 321, 2584, 33847, 510, 30, 50697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1366962377841656, "compression_ratio": 1.5598455598455598, "no_speech_prob": 1.825044672679188e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 93594, "start": 942.8000000000001, "end": 943.24, "text": " Well, no.", "tokens": [50708, 1042, 11, 572, 13, 50730], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1366962377841656, "compression_ratio": 1.5598455598455598, "no_speech_prob": 1.825044672679188e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 93594, "start": 943.34, "end": 949.0, "text": " If a universal checker is mathematically impossible, do we just give up on verifying transformed documents entirely?", "tokens": [50735, 759, 257, 11455, 1520, 260, 307, 44003, 6243, 11, 360, 321, 445, 976, 493, 322, 1306, 5489, 16894, 8512, 7696, 30, 51018], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1366962377841656, "compression_ratio": 1.5598455598455598, "no_speech_prob": 1.825044672679188e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 93594, "start": 949.24, "end": 949.7800000000001, "text": " Not at all.", "tokens": [51030, 1726, 412, 439, 13, 51057], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1366962377841656, "compression_ratio": 1.5598455598455598, "no_speech_prob": 1.825044672679188e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 93594, "start": 949.84, "end": 952.82, "text": " And this is where Paper Eye pivots from, like, destruction to construction.", "tokens": [51060, 400, 341, 307, 689, 24990, 21603, 280, 592, 1971, 490, 11, 411, 11, 13563, 281, 6435, 13, 51209], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1366962377841656, "compression_ratio": 1.5598455598455598, "no_speech_prob": 1.825044672679188e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 93594, "start": 953.1400000000001, "end": 954.3800000000001, "text": " It actually offers a lifeline.", "tokens": [51225, 467, 767, 7736, 257, 4545, 5440, 13, 51287], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1366962377841656, "compression_ratio": 1.5598455598455598, "no_speech_prob": 1.825044672679188e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 93594, "start": 954.46, "end": 955.58, "text": " Okay, good. We need a lifeline.", "tokens": [51291, 1033, 11, 665, 13, 492, 643, 257, 4545, 5440, 13, 51347], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1366962377841656, "compression_ratio": 1.5598455598455598, "no_speech_prob": 1.825044672679188e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 95558, "start": 955.58, "end": 958.5, "text": " The math says we cannot universally check everything.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 5221, 1619, 321, 2644, 43995, 1520, 1203, 13, 50511], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1310613864176982, "compression_ratio": 1.5188679245283019, "no_speech_prob": 1.7275493102014705e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 95558, "start": 958.86, "end": 962.9200000000001, "text": " But what if we severely restrict the types of transformations we are looking at?", "tokens": [50529, 583, 437, 498, 321, 26271, 7694, 264, 3467, 295, 34852, 321, 366, 1237, 412, 30, 50732], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1310613864176982, "compression_ratio": 1.5188679245283019, "no_speech_prob": 1.7275493102014705e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 95558, "start": 963.0600000000001, "end": 963.8000000000001, "text": " Restrict them how?", "tokens": [50739, 13094, 3740, 552, 577, 30, 50776], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1310613864176982, "compression_ratio": 1.5188679245283019, "no_speech_prob": 1.7275493102014705e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 95558, "start": 964.0200000000001, "end": 974.86, "text": " What if we don't let the AI completely rewrite the paragraph in, you know, the style of Shakespeare, but instead we limit it to very specific, highly structured shifts?", "tokens": [50787, 708, 498, 321, 500, 380, 718, 264, 7318, 2584, 28132, 264, 18865, 294, 11, 291, 458, 11, 264, 3758, 295, 22825, 11, 457, 2602, 321, 4948, 309, 281, 588, 2685, 11, 5405, 18519, 19201, 30, 51329], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1310613864176982, "compression_ratio": 1.5188679245283019, "no_speech_prob": 1.7275493102014705e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 97486, "start": 974.86, "end": 979.5, "text": " This leads to what Fliction calls the certified rewrite fragment.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 6689, 281, 437, 3235, 4105, 5498, 264, 18580, 28132, 26424, 13, 50597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12981719970703126, "compression_ratio": 1.7137809187279152, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191861440708165e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 97486, "start": 979.66, "end": 982.52, "text": " Okay, so certified rewrite fragment, the safe zone.", "tokens": [50605, 1033, 11, 370, 18580, 28132, 26424, 11, 264, 3273, 6668, 13, 50748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12981719970703126, "compression_ratio": 1.7137809187279152, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191861440708165e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 97486, "start": 982.8000000000001, "end": 985.04, "text": " What does it take to actually get into this safe zone?", "tokens": [50762, 708, 775, 309, 747, 281, 767, 483, 666, 341, 3273, 6668, 30, 50874], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12981719970703126, "compression_ratio": 1.7137809187279152, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191861440708165e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 97486, "start": 985.7, "end": 996.8000000000001, "text": " So to guarantee correspondence, a machine can perfectly check the transformation if we limit ourselves to a bounded class of transformations generated by a terminating and confluent rewrite system.", "tokens": [50907, 407, 281, 10815, 38135, 11, 257, 3479, 393, 6239, 1520, 264, 9887, 498, 321, 4948, 4175, 281, 257, 37498, 1508, 295, 34852, 10833, 538, 257, 1433, 8205, 293, 1497, 43518, 28132, 1185, 13, 51462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12981719970703126, "compression_ratio": 1.7137809187279152, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191861440708165e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 97486, "start": 996.84, "end": 998.22, "text": " Okay, that's a lot of math words.", "tokens": [51464, 1033, 11, 300, 311, 257, 688, 295, 5221, 2283, 13, 51533], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12981719970703126, "compression_ratio": 1.7137809187279152, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191861440708165e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 97486, "start": 998.28, "end": 999.12, "text": " Let's break that down.", "tokens": [51536, 961, 311, 1821, 300, 760, 13, 51578], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12981719970703126, "compression_ratio": 1.7137809187279152, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191861440708165e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 97486, "start": 999.86, "end": 1002.5, "text": " Terminating means we avoid the infinite loop, right?", "tokens": [51615, 19835, 8205, 1355, 321, 5042, 264, 13785, 6367, 11, 558, 30, 51747], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12981719970703126, "compression_ratio": 1.7137809187279152, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191861440708165e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 97486, "start": 1002.52, "end": 1002.8000000000001, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51748, 1079, 13, 51762], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12981719970703126, "compression_ratio": 1.7137809187279152, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191861440708165e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 100280, "start": 1002.8, "end": 1005.62, "text": " The transformation rules eventually have to stop applying.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 9887, 4474, 4728, 362, 281, 1590, 9275, 13, 50506], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14068280855814616, "compression_ratio": 1.6258278145695364, "no_speech_prob": 1.868605530724876e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 100280, "start": 1005.9599999999999, "end": 1010.76, "text": " It doesn't just infinitely swap the word happy for glad and then glad back to happy forever.", "tokens": [50523, 467, 1177, 380, 445, 36227, 18135, 264, 1349, 2055, 337, 5404, 293, 550, 5404, 646, 281, 2055, 5680, 13, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14068280855814616, "compression_ratio": 1.6258278145695364, "no_speech_prob": 1.868605530724876e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 100280, "start": 1010.8599999999999, "end": 1012.42, "text": " Exactly. It reaches an end state.", "tokens": [50768, 7587, 13, 467, 14235, 364, 917, 1785, 13, 50846], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14068280855814616, "compression_ratio": 1.6258278145695364, "no_speech_prob": 1.868605530724876e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 100280, "start": 1012.5, "end": 1015.76, "text": " But confluence is the tricky part. That's Newman's Lemma, right?", "tokens": [50850, 583, 1497, 40432, 307, 264, 12414, 644, 13, 663, 311, 49377, 311, 16905, 1696, 11, 558, 30, 51013], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14068280855814616, "compression_ratio": 1.6258278145695364, "no_speech_prob": 1.868605530724876e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 100280, "start": 1015.8599999999999, "end": 1016.3199999999999, "text": " Thought on.", "tokens": [51018, 23058, 322, 13, 51041], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14068280855814616, "compression_ratio": 1.6258278145695364, "no_speech_prob": 1.868605530724876e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 100280, "start": 1016.64, "end": 1021.28, "text": " Getting to that unique normal form, regardless of the path you take, yes.", "tokens": [51057, 13674, 281, 300, 3845, 2710, 1254, 11, 10060, 295, 264, 3100, 291, 747, 11, 2086, 13, 51289], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14068280855814616, "compression_ratio": 1.6258278145695364, "no_speech_prob": 1.868605530724876e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 100280, "start": 1022.16, "end": 1030.8799999999999, "text": " Newman's Lemma states that if a rewrite system is terminating and it is locally confluent, meaning if you take one step in two different valid directions,", "tokens": [51333, 49377, 311, 16905, 1696, 4368, 300, 498, 257, 28132, 1185, 307, 1433, 8205, 293, 309, 307, 16143, 1497, 43518, 11, 3620, 498, 291, 747, 472, 1823, 294, 732, 819, 7363, 11095, 11, 51769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14068280855814616, "compression_ratio": 1.6258278145695364, "no_speech_prob": 1.868605530724876e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 103088, "start": 1030.88, "end": 1037.0800000000002, "text": " you can eventually merge those paths back together, then the system is globally confluent.", "tokens": [50365, 291, 393, 4728, 22183, 729, 14518, 646, 1214, 11, 550, 264, 1185, 307, 18958, 1497, 43518, 13, 50675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18719303607940674, "compression_ratio": 1.3727810650887573, "no_speech_prob": 1.5421203810456197e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 103088, "start": 1037.2, "end": 1037.46, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50681, 1033, 13, 50694], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18719303607940674, "compression_ratio": 1.3727810650887573, "no_speech_prob": 1.5421203810456197e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 103088, "start": 1037.7600000000002, "end": 1039.68, "text": " It guarantees a unique normal form.", "tokens": [50709, 467, 32567, 257, 3845, 2710, 1254, 13, 50805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18719303607940674, "compression_ratio": 1.3727810650887573, "no_speech_prob": 1.5421203810456197e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 103088, "start": 1039.88, "end": 1046.64, "text": " The way I visualize this is like cleaning up a really messy algebraic equation in high school math.", "tokens": [50815, 440, 636, 286, 23273, 341, 307, 411, 8924, 493, 257, 534, 16191, 21989, 299, 5367, 294, 1090, 1395, 5221, 13, 51153], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18719303607940674, "compression_ratio": 1.3727810650887573, "no_speech_prob": 1.5421203810456197e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 104664, "start": 1046.64, "end": 1048.26, "text": " Oh, that's a great analogy.", "tokens": [50365, 876, 11, 300, 311, 257, 869, 21663, 13, 50446], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1378892000983743, "compression_ratio": 1.6244343891402715, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127013140367462e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 104664, "start": 1048.26, "end": 1054.8600000000001, "text": " Right. Let's say you have an equation with variables, deep sets of parentheses, and negative signs scattered everywhere.", "tokens": [50446, 1779, 13, 961, 311, 584, 291, 362, 364, 5367, 365, 9102, 11, 2452, 6352, 295, 34153, 11, 293, 3671, 7880, 21986, 5315, 13, 50776], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1378892000983743, "compression_ratio": 1.6244343891402715, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127013140367462e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 104664, "start": 1055.0800000000002, "end": 1057.5400000000002, "text": " You have a strict set of algebraic rules.", "tokens": [50787, 509, 362, 257, 10910, 992, 295, 21989, 299, 4474, 13, 50910], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1378892000983743, "compression_ratio": 1.6244343891402715, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127013140367462e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 104664, "start": 1057.68, "end": 1057.8200000000002, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50917, 1779, 13, 50924], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1378892000983743, "compression_ratio": 1.6244343891402715, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127013140367462e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 104664, "start": 1058.1000000000001, "end": 1066.0200000000002, "text": " Whether I choose to multiply the variables first or distribute the negative sign first or group the terms first, it really doesn't matter what sequence I choose.", "tokens": [50938, 8503, 286, 2826, 281, 12972, 264, 9102, 700, 420, 20594, 264, 3671, 1465, 700, 420, 1594, 264, 2115, 700, 11, 309, 534, 1177, 380, 1871, 437, 8310, 286, 2826, 13, 51334], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1378892000983743, "compression_ratio": 1.6244343891402715, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127013140367462e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 106602, "start": 1066.02, "end": 1067.08, "text": " As long as you follow the rules.", "tokens": [50365, 1018, 938, 382, 291, 1524, 264, 4474, 13, 50418], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09247789754495993, "compression_ratio": 1.603960396039604, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733205954691746e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 106602, "start": 1067.22, "end": 1076.86, "text": " Exactly. As long as I strictly follow those algebraic rules, the equation will steadily collapse down until I reach the exact same simplified answer at the bottom of the page as the person sitting next to me.", "tokens": [50425, 7587, 13, 1018, 938, 382, 286, 20792, 1524, 729, 21989, 299, 4474, 11, 264, 5367, 486, 36129, 15584, 760, 1826, 286, 2524, 264, 1900, 912, 26335, 1867, 412, 264, 2767, 295, 264, 3028, 382, 264, 954, 3798, 958, 281, 385, 13, 50907], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09247789754495993, "compression_ratio": 1.603960396039604, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733205954691746e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 106602, "start": 1076.94, "end": 1077.58, "text": " That is perfect.", "tokens": [50911, 663, 307, 2176, 13, 50943], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09247789754495993, "compression_ratio": 1.603960396039604, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733205954691746e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 106602, "start": 1077.72, "end": 1081.0, "text": " And that fully simplified, irreducible answer is our normal form.", "tokens": [50950, 400, 300, 4498, 26335, 11, 16014, 769, 32128, 1867, 307, 527, 2710, 1254, 13, 51114], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09247789754495993, "compression_ratio": 1.603960396039604, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733205954691746e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 108100, "start": 1081.0, "end": 1099.0, "text": " And if we take that algebra analogy, what Fliction is saying is that if the original text and the new AI transformed text both boil down to the exact same normal form, using these strict algebraic style rules, then we can mathematically perfectly guarantee that they possess mutual semantic entailment.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 498, 321, 747, 300, 21989, 21663, 11, 437, 3235, 4105, 307, 1566, 307, 300, 498, 264, 3380, 2487, 293, 264, 777, 7318, 16894, 2487, 1293, 13329, 760, 281, 264, 1900, 912, 2710, 1254, 11, 1228, 613, 10910, 21989, 299, 3758, 4474, 11, 550, 321, 393, 44003, 6239, 10815, 300, 436, 17490, 16917, 47982, 948, 864, 518, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1004747814602322, "compression_ratio": 1.6928571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.356277611920531e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 108100, "start": 1099.7, "end": 1101.18, "text": " Meaning the meaning is identical.", "tokens": [51300, 19948, 264, 3620, 307, 14800, 13, 51374], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1004747814602322, "compression_ratio": 1.6928571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.356277611920531e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 108100, "start": 1101.82, "end": 1102.3, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51406, 7587, 13, 51430], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1004747814602322, "compression_ratio": 1.6928571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.356277611920531e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 108100, "start": 1102.44, "end": 1108.98, "text": " But wait, algebra is just numbers? What kind of text transformations actually fit into this super strict mathematical safe zone?", "tokens": [51437, 583, 1699, 11, 21989, 307, 445, 3547, 30, 708, 733, 295, 2487, 34852, 767, 3318, 666, 341, 1687, 10910, 18894, 3273, 6668, 30, 51764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1004747814602322, "compression_ratio": 1.6928571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.356277611920531e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 110898, "start": 1108.98, "end": 1114.3600000000001, "text": " The paper provides specific examples of these benign transformations that make up the certified fragment.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3035, 6417, 2685, 5110, 295, 613, 3271, 788, 34852, 300, 652, 493, 264, 18580, 26424, 13, 50634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11075339998517718, "compression_ratio": 1.6741214057507987, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684885894777124e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 110898, "start": 1114.92, "end": 1117.94, "text": " The first is alpha renaming of bound variables.", "tokens": [50662, 440, 700, 307, 8961, 8124, 5184, 295, 5472, 9102, 13, 50813], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11075339998517718, "compression_ratio": 1.6741214057507987, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684885894777124e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 110898, "start": 1118.24, "end": 1121.2, "text": " Alpha renaming, right. So changing the label without changing the logic.", "tokens": [50828, 20588, 8124, 5184, 11, 558, 13, 407, 4473, 264, 7645, 1553, 4473, 264, 9952, 13, 50976], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11075339998517718, "compression_ratio": 1.6741214057507987, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684885894777124e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 110898, "start": 1121.3600000000001, "end": 1130.28, "text": " Exactly. If I have a mathematical proof that says for all X, X is greater than zero, and the AI rewrites it to say for all Y, Y is greater than zero.", "tokens": [50984, 7587, 13, 759, 286, 362, 257, 18894, 8177, 300, 1619, 337, 439, 1783, 11, 1783, 307, 5044, 813, 4018, 11, 293, 264, 7318, 319, 86, 30931, 309, 281, 584, 337, 439, 398, 11, 398, 307, 5044, 813, 4018, 13, 51430], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11075339998517718, "compression_ratio": 1.6741214057507987, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684885894777124e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 110898, "start": 1130.38, "end": 1135.04, "text": " The text is lexically different. Like the actual byte data on the hard drive has changed.", "tokens": [51435, 440, 2487, 307, 476, 87, 984, 819, 13, 1743, 264, 3539, 40846, 1412, 322, 264, 1152, 3332, 575, 3105, 13, 51668], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11075339998517718, "compression_ratio": 1.6741214057507987, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684885894777124e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 110898, "start": 1135.1200000000001, "end": 1137.16, "text": " Right, but the logical structure is completely untouched.", "tokens": [51672, 1779, 11, 457, 264, 14978, 3877, 307, 2584, 1701, 36740, 13, 51774], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11075339998517718, "compression_ratio": 1.6741214057507987, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684885894777124e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 113716, "start": 1137.16, "end": 1139.96, "text": " Which is lexically substantial, but semantically inert.", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 307, 476, 87, 984, 16726, 11, 457, 4361, 49505, 25832, 13, 50505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18268577339722938, "compression_ratio": 1.550420168067227, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111185294544807e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 113716, "start": 1140.28, "end": 1147.3200000000002, "text": " Precisely. Another example in the fragment is the reordering of conjuncts and disjuncts, utilizing associativity and commutativity.", "tokens": [50521, 48746, 736, 13, 3996, 1365, 294, 264, 26424, 307, 264, 319, 765, 1794, 295, 18244, 349, 82, 293, 717, 10010, 349, 82, 11, 26775, 4180, 30142, 293, 800, 325, 30142, 13, 50873], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18268577339722938, "compression_ratio": 1.550420168067227, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111185294544807e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 113716, "start": 1147.64, "end": 1150.0600000000002, "text": " So changing A and B to B and A.", "tokens": [50889, 407, 4473, 316, 293, 363, 281, 363, 293, 316, 13, 51010], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18268577339722938, "compression_ratio": 1.550420168067227, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111185294544807e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 113716, "start": 1150.16, "end": 1156.02, "text": " Yes. The machine can perfectly verify that those mean the same thing. Another one is double negation elimination.", "tokens": [51015, 1079, 13, 440, 3479, 393, 6239, 16888, 300, 729, 914, 264, 912, 551, 13, 3996, 472, 307, 3834, 2485, 399, 29224, 13, 51308], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18268577339722938, "compression_ratio": 1.550420168067227, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111185294544807e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 113716, "start": 1156.42, "end": 1157.5400000000002, "text": " Okay, give me a little bit of that.", "tokens": [51328, 1033, 11, 976, 385, 257, 707, 857, 295, 300, 13, 51384], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18268577339722938, "compression_ratio": 1.550420168067227, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111185294544807e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 115754, "start": 1157.54, "end": 1166.12, "text": " If the text originally said, it is not the case that the system is not vulnerable, and the AI summarizes it down to the system is vulnerable.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 264, 2487, 7993, 848, 11, 309, 307, 406, 264, 1389, 300, 264, 1185, 307, 406, 10955, 11, 293, 264, 7318, 14611, 5660, 309, 760, 281, 264, 1185, 307, 10955, 13, 50794], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12074235507420131, "compression_ratio": 1.4931506849315068, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810576790124657e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 115754, "start": 1166.48, "end": 1171.8799999999999, "text": " Ah, okay. The certified rewrite fragment can handle that flawlessly.", "tokens": [50812, 2438, 11, 1392, 13, 440, 18580, 28132, 26424, 393, 4813, 300, 13717, 12048, 13, 51082], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12074235507420131, "compression_ratio": 1.4931506849315068, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810576790124657e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 115754, "start": 1172.18, "end": 1172.6599999999999, "text": " It can.", "tokens": [51097, 467, 393, 13, 51121], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12074235507420131, "compression_ratio": 1.4931506849315068, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810576790124657e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 117266, "start": 1172.66, "end": 1189.26, "text": " Okay, so these are incredibly structural, almost grammatical shifts. They are safe, but, I mean, they are also incredibly narrow.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 370, 613, 366, 6252, 15067, 11, 1920, 17570, 267, 804, 19201, 13, 814, 366, 3273, 11, 457, 11, 286, 914, 11, 436, 366, 611, 6252, 9432, 13, 51195], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1366203835136012, "compression_ratio": 1.290909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956219856337993e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 117266, "start": 1189.46, "end": 1189.94, "text": " Very narrow.", "tokens": [51205, 4372, 9432, 13, 51229], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1366203835136012, "compression_ratio": 1.290909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956219856337993e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 118994, "start": 1189.94, "end": 1196.22, "text": " Out in the real world, an AI summarizer is going to try to do much more complex things than just eliminating double negatives.", "tokens": [50365, 5925, 294, 264, 957, 1002, 11, 364, 7318, 14611, 6545, 307, 516, 281, 853, 281, 360, 709, 544, 3997, 721, 813, 445, 31203, 3834, 40019, 13, 50679], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11471697235107423, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617126511603297e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 118994, "start": 1196.52, "end": 1199.98, "text": " It's going to try to synthesize entire pages of dense data.", "tokens": [50694, 467, 311, 516, 281, 853, 281, 26617, 1125, 2302, 7183, 295, 18011, 1412, 13, 50867], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11471697235107423, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617126511603297e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 118994, "start": 1200.1000000000001, "end": 1200.8200000000002, "text": " Of course it is.", "tokens": [50873, 2720, 1164, 309, 307, 13, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11471697235107423, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617126511603297e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 118994, "start": 1200.92, "end": 1210.02, "text": " So if our machines can only perfectly check things inside that strict, tiny algebraic boundary, our systems need a way to honestly report when they are out of their depth.", "tokens": [50914, 407, 498, 527, 8379, 393, 787, 6239, 1520, 721, 1854, 300, 10910, 11, 5870, 21989, 299, 12866, 11, 527, 3652, 643, 257, 636, 281, 6095, 2275, 562, 436, 366, 484, 295, 641, 7161, 13, 51369], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11471697235107423, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617126511603297e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 118994, "start": 1210.3400000000001, "end": 1212.16, "text": " They can't just pretend everything is fine.", "tokens": [51385, 814, 393, 380, 445, 11865, 1203, 307, 2489, 13, 51476], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11471697235107423, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617126511603297e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 118994, "start": 1212.26, "end": 1216.6000000000001, "text": " This is arguably the most critical design principle of the entire claim shift architecture.", "tokens": [51481, 639, 307, 26771, 264, 881, 4924, 1715, 8665, 295, 264, 2302, 3932, 5513, 9482, 13, 51698], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11471697235107423, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617126511603297e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 118994, "start": 1216.9, "end": 1217.9, "text": " Because of Church's theorem.", "tokens": [51713, 1436, 295, 7882, 311, 20904, 13, 51763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11471697235107423, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617126511603297e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 121790, "start": 1217.9, "end": 1224.18, "text": " Exactly. Because we know from Church's theorem that the system can't solve everything and must never pretend that it can.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 1436, 321, 458, 490, 7882, 311, 20904, 300, 264, 1185, 393, 380, 5039, 1203, 293, 1633, 1128, 11865, 300, 309, 393, 13, 50679], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12009782611199145, "compression_ratio": 1.562937062937063, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815693802685328e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 121790, "start": 1224.5, "end": 1224.7800000000002, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50695, 1779, 13, 50709], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12009782611199145, "compression_ratio": 1.562937062937063, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815693802685328e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 121790, "start": 1224.98, "end": 1231.3000000000002, "text": " If you build a system that only outputs true or false, it will inevitably lie when it encounters complexity.", "tokens": [50719, 759, 291, 1322, 257, 1185, 300, 787, 23930, 2074, 420, 7908, 11, 309, 486, 28171, 4544, 562, 309, 26310, 14024, 13, 51035], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12009782611199145, "compression_ratio": 1.562937062937063, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815693802685328e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 121790, "start": 1231.98, "end": 1239.44, "text": " So the sources propose a strictly three-valued logic output for any system attempting to check a transformation.", "tokens": [51069, 407, 264, 7139, 17421, 257, 20792, 1045, 12, 3337, 5827, 9952, 5598, 337, 604, 1185, 22001, 281, 1520, 257, 9887, 13, 51442], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12009782611199145, "compression_ratio": 1.562937062937063, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815693802685328e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 121790, "start": 1240.0, "end": 1242.2, "text": " Okay. Three values. Walk me through them.", "tokens": [51470, 1033, 13, 6244, 4190, 13, 10818, 385, 807, 552, 13, 51580], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12009782611199145, "compression_ratio": 1.562937062937063, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815693802685328e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 121790, "start": 1242.3000000000002, "end": 1244.92, "text": " Yes. Value number one is preserved.", "tokens": [51585, 1079, 13, 39352, 1230, 472, 307, 22242, 13, 51716], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12009782611199145, "compression_ratio": 1.562937062937063, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815693802685328e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 121790, "start": 1245.22, "end": 1246.0600000000002, "text": " Meaning it worked.", "tokens": [51731, 19948, 309, 2732, 13, 51773], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12009782611199145, "compression_ratio": 1.562937062937063, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815693802685328e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 124606, "start": 1246.06, "end": 1250.54, "text": " Meaning the transformation fell entirely inside our strict mathematical safe zone.", "tokens": [50365, 19948, 264, 9887, 5696, 7696, 1854, 527, 10910, 18894, 3273, 6668, 13, 50589], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13273272671542324, "compression_ratio": 1.6540084388185654, "no_speech_prob": 1.2992354588015065e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 124606, "start": 1250.8999999999999, "end": 1257.22, "text": " The system ran the rewrite rules, the normal forms matched, and the machine guarantees mutual semantic entailment.", "tokens": [50607, 440, 1185, 5872, 264, 28132, 4474, 11, 264, 2710, 6422, 21447, 11, 293, 264, 3479, 32567, 16917, 47982, 948, 864, 518, 13, 50923], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13273272671542324, "compression_ratio": 1.6540084388185654, "no_speech_prob": 1.2992354588015065e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 124606, "start": 1257.34, "end": 1260.6399999999999, "text": " The meaning is flawlessly preserved. That's the gold standard.", "tokens": [50929, 440, 3620, 307, 13717, 12048, 22242, 13, 663, 311, 264, 3821, 3832, 13, 51094], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13273272671542324, "compression_ratio": 1.6540084388185654, "no_speech_prob": 1.2992354588015065e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 124606, "start": 1260.76, "end": 1261.1799999999998, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51100, 7587, 13, 51121], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13273272671542324, "compression_ratio": 1.6540084388185654, "no_speech_prob": 1.2992354588015065e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 124606, "start": 1261.36, "end": 1262.46, "text": " What's the second value?", "tokens": [51130, 708, 311, 264, 1150, 2158, 30, 51185], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13273272671542324, "compression_ratio": 1.6540084388185654, "no_speech_prob": 1.2992354588015065e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 124606, "start": 1262.74, "end": 1264.86, "text": " Value number two is not preserved under.", "tokens": [51199, 39352, 1230, 732, 307, 406, 22242, 833, 13, 51305], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13273272671542324, "compression_ratio": 1.6540084388185654, "no_speech_prob": 1.2992354588015065e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 124606, "start": 1265.52, "end": 1268.96, "text": " The R stands for the specific set of rewrite rules used.", "tokens": [51338, 440, 497, 7382, 337, 264, 2685, 992, 295, 28132, 4474, 1143, 13, 51510], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13273272671542324, "compression_ratio": 1.6540084388185654, "no_speech_prob": 1.2992354588015065e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 126896, "start": 1268.96, "end": 1271.22, "text": " Okay. So it ran the rules, and?", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 13, 407, 309, 5872, 264, 4474, 11, 293, 30, 50478], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1626444207616599, "compression_ratio": 1.5777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.9503487366789862e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 126896, "start": 1271.3600000000001, "end": 1278.76, "text": " This means the transformation fell inside our mathematical safe zone, the system checked it, and it definitively found that the meaning fundamentally changed.", "tokens": [50485, 639, 1355, 264, 9887, 5696, 1854, 527, 18894, 3273, 6668, 11, 264, 1185, 10033, 309, 11, 293, 309, 28152, 356, 1352, 300, 264, 3620, 17879, 3105, 13, 50855], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1626444207616599, "compression_ratio": 1.5777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.9503487366789862e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 126896, "start": 1278.92, "end": 1280.4, "text": " The normal forms do not match.", "tokens": [50863, 440, 2710, 6422, 360, 406, 2995, 13, 50937], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1626444207616599, "compression_ratio": 1.5777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.9503487366789862e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 126896, "start": 1280.46, "end": 1282.2, "text": " Right. The semantic meaning is broken.", "tokens": [50940, 1779, 13, 440, 47982, 3620, 307, 5463, 13, 51027], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1626444207616599, "compression_ratio": 1.5777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.9503487366789862e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 126896, "start": 1282.44, "end": 1287.52, "text": " So this is the recipe where we swapped sugar for salt. The machine actively caught the poison.", "tokens": [51039, 407, 341, 307, 264, 6782, 689, 321, 50011, 5076, 337, 5139, 13, 440, 3479, 13022, 5415, 264, 10836, 13, 51293], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1626444207616599, "compression_ratio": 1.5777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.9503487366789862e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 128752, "start": 1287.52, "end": 1288.8799999999999, "text": " Exactly. It caught the lie.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 467, 5415, 264, 4544, 13, 50433], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15967987360579244, "compression_ratio": 1.5206611570247934, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234906214523948e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 128752, "start": 1289.32, "end": 1294.22, "text": " But what about the third value? Because that's where the vast majority of AI summaries are going to land.", "tokens": [50455, 583, 437, 466, 264, 2636, 2158, 30, 1436, 300, 311, 689, 264, 8369, 6286, 295, 7318, 8367, 4889, 366, 516, 281, 2117, 13, 50700], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15967987360579244, "compression_ratio": 1.5206611570247934, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234906214523948e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 128752, "start": 1294.36, "end": 1297.9, "text": " Without a doubt. Value number three is outside certified fragment.", "tokens": [50707, 9129, 257, 6385, 13, 39352, 1230, 1045, 307, 2380, 18580, 26424, 13, 50884], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15967987360579244, "compression_ratio": 1.5206611570247934, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234906214523948e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 128752, "start": 1298.1, "end": 1299.06, "text": " Outside the fragment.", "tokens": [50894, 28218, 264, 26424, 13, 50942], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15967987360579244, "compression_ratio": 1.5206611570247934, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234906214523948e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 128752, "start": 1299.3799999999999, "end": 1306.32, "text": " This means the transformation is simply too complex, too relational, or too novel for the automated system to judge.", "tokens": [50958, 639, 1355, 264, 9887, 307, 2935, 886, 3997, 11, 886, 38444, 11, 420, 886, 7613, 337, 264, 18473, 1185, 281, 6995, 13, 51305], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15967987360579244, "compression_ratio": 1.5206611570247934, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234906214523948e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 128752, "start": 1306.68, "end": 1308.8799999999999, "text": " So it's basically giving up.", "tokens": [51323, 407, 309, 311, 1936, 2902, 493, 13, 51433], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15967987360579244, "compression_ratio": 1.5206611570247934, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234906214523948e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 130888, "start": 1308.88, "end": 1323.5600000000002, "text": " It's not saying the new text is false. It's not saying the new text is true. It is a machine honestly throwing its hands up and saying, I am a finite algorithm, and this semantic comparison is beyond my mathematical capacity to evaluate.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 406, 1566, 264, 777, 2487, 307, 7908, 13, 467, 311, 406, 1566, 264, 777, 2487, 307, 2074, 13, 467, 307, 257, 3479, 6095, 10238, 1080, 2377, 493, 293, 1566, 11, 286, 669, 257, 19362, 9284, 11, 293, 341, 47982, 9660, 307, 4399, 452, 18894, 6042, 281, 13059, 13, 51099], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06315866488854861, "compression_ratio": 1.71900826446281, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684872884351054e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 130888, "start": 1323.9, "end": 1332.16, "text": " I love that. It brings us right back to the x-ray analogy from the start. It's the machine saying, the tissue is too dense, I can't give you a clear diagnosis.", "tokens": [51116, 286, 959, 300, 13, 467, 5607, 505, 558, 646, 281, 264, 2031, 12, 3458, 21663, 490, 264, 722, 13, 467, 311, 264, 3479, 1566, 11, 264, 12404, 307, 886, 18011, 11, 286, 393, 380, 976, 291, 257, 1850, 15217, 13, 51529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06315866488854861, "compression_ratio": 1.71900826446281, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684872884351054e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 130888, "start": 1332.4, "end": 1333.2800000000002, "text": " That's exactly it.", "tokens": [51541, 663, 311, 2293, 309, 13, 51585], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06315866488854861, "compression_ratio": 1.71900826446281, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684872884351054e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 133328, "start": 1333.28, "end": 1340.24, "text": " So if the system spits out outside certified fragment, that doesn't necessarily mean the AI summarizer hallucinated or lied.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 498, 264, 1185, 637, 1208, 484, 2380, 18580, 26424, 11, 300, 1177, 380, 4725, 914, 264, 7318, 14611, 6545, 35212, 5410, 420, 20101, 13, 50713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07796713022085336, "compression_ratio": 1.7606837606837606, "no_speech_prob": 1.2595651518315654e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 133328, "start": 1340.24, "end": 1353.16, "text": " Not at all. As Fliction states in the text, and I honestly think this is a principle that should be carved into the walls of every tech company right now, failure of certification is not certification of failure.", "tokens": [50713, 1726, 412, 439, 13, 1018, 3235, 4105, 4368, 294, 264, 2487, 11, 293, 286, 6095, 519, 341, 307, 257, 8665, 300, 820, 312, 28613, 666, 264, 7920, 295, 633, 7553, 2237, 558, 586, 11, 7763, 295, 21775, 307, 406, 21775, 295, 7763, 13, 51359], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07796713022085336, "compression_ratio": 1.7606837606837606, "no_speech_prob": 1.2595651518315654e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 133328, "start": 1353.3799999999999, "end": 1358.28, "text": " Failure of certification is not certification of failure. That is so good.", "tokens": [51370, 39094, 540, 295, 21775, 307, 406, 21775, 295, 7763, 13, 663, 307, 370, 665, 13, 51615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07796713022085336, "compression_ratio": 1.7606837606837606, "no_speech_prob": 1.2595651518315654e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 135828, "start": 1358.28, "end": 1365.2, "text": " It's crucial. Just because the automated system failed to prove that the meaning is preserved does not mean the meaning was destroyed.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 11462, 13, 1449, 570, 264, 18473, 1185, 7612, 281, 7081, 300, 264, 3620, 307, 22242, 775, 406, 914, 264, 3620, 390, 8937, 13, 50711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.058913102856388795, "compression_ratio": 1.6160990712074303, "no_speech_prob": 1.444135067606156e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 135828, "start": 1365.48, "end": 1371.26, "text": " Maybe the AI did a brilliant, completely accurate, profound summary of the article.", "tokens": [50725, 2704, 264, 7318, 630, 257, 10248, 11, 2584, 8559, 11, 14382, 12691, 295, 264, 7222, 13, 51014], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.058913102856388795, "compression_ratio": 1.6160990712074303, "no_speech_prob": 1.444135067606156e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 135828, "start": 1371.3799999999999, "end": 1379.3, "text": " Right. But it used vocabulary and relational structures so novel that the basic rewrite rules couldn't map it back to the original normal form.", "tokens": [51020, 1779, 13, 583, 309, 1143, 19864, 293, 38444, 9227, 370, 7613, 300, 264, 3875, 28132, 4474, 2809, 380, 4471, 309, 646, 281, 264, 3380, 2710, 1254, 13, 51416], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.058913102856388795, "compression_ratio": 1.6160990712074303, "no_speech_prob": 1.444135067606156e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 135828, "start": 1379.52, "end": 1387.16, "text": " Okay, that makes sense. But practically speaking, what happens when a document hits that third value? Does the whole verification process just die right there?", "tokens": [51427, 1033, 11, 300, 1669, 2020, 13, 583, 15667, 4124, 11, 437, 2314, 562, 257, 4166, 8664, 300, 2636, 2158, 30, 4402, 264, 1379, 30206, 1399, 445, 978, 558, 456, 30, 51809], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.058913102856388795, "compression_ratio": 1.6160990712074303, "no_speech_prob": 1.444135067606156e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 138716, "start": 1387.16, "end": 1390.88, "text": " No, it acts as a routing mechanism. It defines a boundary of applicability.", "tokens": [50365, 883, 11, 309, 10672, 382, 257, 32722, 7513, 13, 467, 23122, 257, 12866, 295, 2580, 2310, 13, 50551], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1310800097205422, "compression_ratio": 1.6711111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.8533828985423106e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 138716, "start": 1390.94, "end": 1391.8600000000001, "text": " A routing mechanism.", "tokens": [50554, 316, 32722, 7513, 13, 50600], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1310800097205422, "compression_ratio": 1.6711111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.8533828985423106e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 138716, "start": 1391.96, "end": 1396.94, "text": " Yeah. When the system hits outside certified fragment, it flags the transformation and routes the problem.", "tokens": [50605, 865, 13, 1133, 264, 1185, 8664, 2380, 18580, 26424, 11, 309, 23265, 264, 9887, 293, 18242, 264, 1154, 13, 50854], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1310800097205422, "compression_ratio": 1.6711111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.8533828985423106e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 138716, "start": 1396.98, "end": 1397.78, "text": " Where does it route it?", "tokens": [50856, 2305, 775, 309, 7955, 309, 30, 50896], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1310800097205422, "compression_ratio": 1.6711111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.8533828985423106e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 138716, "start": 1398.1200000000001, "end": 1401.22, "text": " Maybe it routes it to a human expert for manual review.", "tokens": [50913, 2704, 309, 18242, 309, 281, 257, 1952, 5844, 337, 9688, 3131, 13, 51068], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1310800097205422, "compression_ratio": 1.6711111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.8533828985423106e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 138716, "start": 1401.72, "end": 1407.5600000000002, "text": " Or maybe it routes it to a completely different computationally massive formal proof method.", "tokens": [51093, 1610, 1310, 309, 18242, 309, 281, 257, 2584, 819, 24903, 379, 5994, 9860, 8177, 3170, 13, 51385], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1310800097205422, "compression_ratio": 1.6711111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.8533828985423106e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 140756, "start": 1407.56, "end": 1423.4199999999998, "text": " But the absolute cardinal sin in this architecture, the thing that corrupts the entire epistemic structure, is silently converting an outside certified fragment into a default negative, or worse, a default positive.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 8236, 2920, 2071, 3343, 294, 341, 9482, 11, 264, 551, 300, 17366, 82, 264, 2302, 2388, 468, 3438, 3877, 11, 307, 40087, 29942, 364, 2380, 18580, 26424, 666, 257, 7576, 3671, 11, 420, 5324, 11, 257, 7576, 3353, 13, 51158], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10460846145431717, "compression_ratio": 1.576036866359447, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077925445335707e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 140756, "start": 1423.56, "end": 1424.82, "text": " Just sweeping it under the rug.", "tokens": [51165, 1449, 33285, 309, 833, 264, 18329, 13, 51228], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10460846145431717, "compression_ratio": 1.576036866359447, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077925445335707e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 140756, "start": 1425.1399999999999, "end": 1431.54, "text": " Exactly. If the machine doesn't know, it must visibly permanently record that it doesn't know.", "tokens": [51244, 7587, 13, 759, 264, 3479, 1177, 380, 458, 11, 309, 1633, 1452, 3545, 24042, 2136, 300, 309, 1177, 380, 458, 13, 51564], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10460846145431717, "compression_ratio": 1.576036866359447, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077925445335707e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 143154, "start": 1431.54, "end": 1446.22, "text": " Okay, the theory here is incredibly rigorous. We've established the category error of watermarks, we've hit the hard wall of Church's theorem, and we've found a narrow safe zone with a three-valued logic system to keep the machines honest.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 264, 5261, 510, 307, 6252, 29882, 13, 492, 600, 7545, 264, 7719, 6713, 295, 1281, 37307, 11, 321, 600, 2045, 264, 1152, 2929, 295, 7882, 311, 20904, 11, 293, 321, 600, 1352, 257, 9432, 3273, 6668, 365, 257, 1045, 12, 3337, 5827, 9952, 1185, 281, 1066, 264, 8379, 3245, 13, 51099], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05574102401733398, "compression_ratio": 1.550185873605948, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617368288687762e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 143154, "start": 1446.42, "end": 1447.1399999999999, "text": " It's a lot of theory.", "tokens": [51109, 467, 311, 257, 688, 295, 5261, 13, 51145], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05574102401733398, "compression_ratio": 1.550185873605948, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617368288687762e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 143154, "start": 1447.32, "end": 1453.76, "text": " It is, but theory is just math on a whiteboard. How do we actually build software that obeys these strict limits out in the wild?", "tokens": [51154, 467, 307, 11, 457, 5261, 307, 445, 5221, 322, 257, 2418, 3787, 13, 1012, 360, 321, 767, 1322, 4722, 300, 36346, 749, 613, 10910, 10406, 484, 294, 264, 4868, 30, 51476], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05574102401733398, "compression_ratio": 1.550185873605948, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617368288687762e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 143154, "start": 1453.92, "end": 1455.04, "text": " That is the big question.", "tokens": [51484, 663, 307, 264, 955, 1168, 13, 51540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05574102401733398, "compression_ratio": 1.550185873605948, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617368288687762e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 145504, "start": 1455.04, "end": 1461.06, "text": " How do we build a filing cabinet for this? Because a normal PDF doesn't naturally support three-valued logic routing.", "tokens": [50365, 1012, 360, 321, 1322, 257, 26854, 15188, 337, 341, 30, 1436, 257, 2710, 17752, 1177, 380, 8195, 1406, 1045, 12, 3337, 5827, 9952, 32722, 13, 50666], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08702979716219643, "compression_ratio": 1.617910447761194, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404740642139479e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 145504, "start": 1461.22, "end": 1465.12, "text": " No, it doesn't. And this brings us to Paper 2, the Manifest Protocol.", "tokens": [50674, 883, 11, 309, 1177, 380, 13, 400, 341, 5607, 505, 281, 24990, 568, 11, 264, 2458, 351, 377, 48753, 13, 50869], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08702979716219643, "compression_ratio": 1.617910447761194, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404740642139479e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 145504, "start": 1465.36, "end": 1467.08, "text": " Okay, here's where it gets really interesting.", "tokens": [50881, 1033, 11, 510, 311, 689, 309, 2170, 534, 1880, 13, 50967], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08702979716219643, "compression_ratio": 1.617910447761194, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404740642139479e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 145504, "start": 1467.2, "end": 1474.02, "text": " Yes. Paper 2 takes all this Lochte logic and forces it into a practical, implementable software architecture.", "tokens": [50973, 1079, 13, 24990, 568, 2516, 439, 341, 6130, 10553, 9952, 293, 5874, 309, 666, 257, 8496, 11, 4445, 712, 4722, 9482, 13, 51314], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08702979716219643, "compression_ratio": 1.617910447761194, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404740642139479e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 145504, "start": 1474.1399999999999, "end": 1475.7, "text": " Because you have to actually build the thing.", "tokens": [51320, 1436, 291, 362, 281, 767, 1322, 264, 551, 13, 51398], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08702979716219643, "compression_ratio": 1.617910447761194, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404740642139479e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 145504, "start": 1475.94, "end": 1484.78, "text": " Right. How do you track a document, track its AI transformations, and track its verification status over time without accidentally conflating them all?", "tokens": [51410, 1779, 13, 1012, 360, 291, 2837, 257, 4166, 11, 2837, 1080, 7318, 34852, 11, 293, 2837, 1080, 30206, 6558, 670, 565, 1553, 15715, 1497, 75, 990, 552, 439, 30, 51852], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08702979716219643, "compression_ratio": 1.617910447761194, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404740642139479e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 148478, "start": 1485.06, "end": 1485.84, "text": " How do they do it?", "tokens": [50379, 1012, 360, 436, 360, 309, 30, 50418], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18154023398815747, "compression_ratio": 1.7166666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759182575378563e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 148478, "start": 1486.16, "end": 1491.24, "text": " To do this, the protocol physically separates the system into three distinct layers.", "tokens": [50434, 1407, 360, 341, 11, 264, 10336, 9762, 34149, 264, 1185, 666, 1045, 10644, 7914, 13, 50688], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18154023398815747, "compression_ratio": 1.7166666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759182575378563e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 148478, "start": 1491.3799999999999, "end": 1492.94, "text": " Okay, break those layers down for me.", "tokens": [50695, 1033, 11, 1821, 729, 7914, 760, 337, 385, 13, 50773], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18154023398815747, "compression_ratio": 1.7166666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759182575378563e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 148478, "start": 1493.06, "end": 1494.74, "text": " Layer 1 is the artifact.", "tokens": [50779, 35166, 502, 307, 264, 34806, 13, 50863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18154023398815747, "compression_ratio": 1.7166666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759182575378563e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 148478, "start": 1494.92, "end": 1495.46, "text": " The artifact.", "tokens": [50872, 440, 34806, 13, 50899], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18154023398815747, "compression_ratio": 1.7166666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759182575378563e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 148478, "start": 1495.46, "end": 1502.16, "text": " This is the document itself. The PDF, the webpage, the raw text file of the AI summary you were reading.", "tokens": [50899, 639, 307, 264, 4166, 2564, 13, 440, 17752, 11, 264, 37852, 11, 264, 8936, 2487, 3991, 295, 264, 7318, 12691, 291, 645, 3760, 13, 51234], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18154023398815747, "compression_ratio": 1.7166666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759182575378563e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 148478, "start": 1502.28, "end": 1503.66, "text": " Got it. The actual thing.", "tokens": [51240, 5803, 309, 13, 440, 3539, 551, 13, 51309], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18154023398815747, "compression_ratio": 1.7166666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759182575378563e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 148478, "start": 1503.8999999999999, "end": 1505.3999999999999, "text": " Layer 2 is the robust commitment.", "tokens": [51321, 35166, 568, 307, 264, 13956, 8371, 13, 51396], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18154023398815747, "compression_ratio": 1.7166666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759182575378563e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 148478, "start": 1505.52, "end": 1506.58, "text": " And that's the watermark, right?", "tokens": [51402, 400, 300, 311, 264, 1281, 5638, 11, 558, 30, 51455], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18154023398815747, "compression_ratio": 1.7166666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759182575378563e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 148478, "start": 1506.68, "end": 1513.08, "text": " Exactly. This is the watermark, the C2PA credential, the steganographic pointer, embedded directly into the artifact.", "tokens": [51460, 7587, 13, 639, 307, 264, 1281, 5638, 11, 264, 383, 17, 10297, 22034, 11, 264, 342, 43118, 12295, 23918, 11, 16741, 3838, 666, 264, 34806, 13, 51780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18154023398815747, "compression_ratio": 1.7166666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759182575378563e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 148478, "start": 1513.28, "end": 1514.22, "text": " Okay, and layer 3.", "tokens": [51790, 1033, 11, 293, 4583, 805, 13, 51837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18154023398815747, "compression_ratio": 1.7166666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759182575378563e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 151422, "start": 1514.22, "end": 1516.5, "text": " Layer 3 is the signed manifest.", "tokens": [50365, 35166, 805, 307, 264, 8175, 10067, 13, 50479], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13779590975853703, "compression_ratio": 1.6023622047244095, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610256564965955e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 151422, "start": 1516.98, "end": 1525.9, "text": " This is a completely separate, append-only cryptographic document stored elsewhere that actually holds all the claims, the relationships, and the verification history.", "tokens": [50503, 639, 307, 257, 2584, 4994, 11, 34116, 12, 25202, 9844, 12295, 4166, 12187, 14517, 300, 767, 9190, 439, 264, 9441, 11, 264, 6159, 11, 293, 264, 30206, 2503, 13, 50949], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13779590975853703, "compression_ratio": 1.6023622047244095, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610256564965955e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 151422, "start": 1526.1000000000001, "end": 1529.48, "text": " So the watermark doesn't actually contain the proof of truth?", "tokens": [50959, 407, 264, 1281, 5638, 1177, 380, 767, 5304, 264, 8177, 295, 3494, 30, 51128], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13779590975853703, "compression_ratio": 1.6023622047244095, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610256564965955e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 151422, "start": 1530.02, "end": 1531.0, "text": " No, not at all.", "tokens": [51155, 883, 11, 406, 412, 439, 13, 51204], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13779590975853703, "compression_ratio": 1.6023622047244095, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610256564965955e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 151422, "start": 1531.1000000000001, "end": 1537.64, "text": " The watermark is just a digital license plate pointing you to the manifest, which is the actual DMV database holding the records.", "tokens": [51209, 440, 1281, 5638, 307, 445, 257, 4562, 10476, 5924, 12166, 291, 281, 264, 10067, 11, 597, 307, 264, 3539, 15322, 53, 8149, 5061, 264, 7724, 13, 51536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13779590975853703, "compression_ratio": 1.6023622047244095, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610256564965955e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 153764, "start": 1537.64, "end": 1550.92, "text": " Precisely. Because a scholarly document, or say a complex legal filing, might contain hundreds of individual claims and a massive interwoven dependency graph.", "tokens": [50365, 48746, 736, 13, 1436, 257, 39589, 4166, 11, 420, 584, 257, 3997, 5089, 26854, 11, 1062, 5304, 6779, 295, 2609, 9441, 293, 257, 5994, 728, 6120, 553, 33621, 4295, 13, 51029], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08449816270308061, "compression_ratio": 1.3876404494382022, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782112166267236e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 153764, "start": 1551.0400000000002, "end": 1556.64, "text": " Right. You couldn't possibly embed all of that complex logic into a tiny text watermark.", "tokens": [51035, 1779, 13, 509, 2809, 380, 6264, 12240, 439, 295, 300, 3997, 9952, 666, 257, 5870, 2487, 1281, 5638, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08449816270308061, "compression_ratio": 1.3876404494382022, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782112166267236e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 155664, "start": 1556.64, "end": 1557.92, "text": " It would break the file.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 576, 1821, 264, 3991, 13, 50429], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11579289087435095, "compression_ratio": 1.537037037037037, "no_speech_prob": 1.61061333540935e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 155664, "start": 1557.92, "end": 1559.4, "text": " The pointer just points.", "tokens": [50429, 440, 23918, 445, 2793, 13, 50503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11579289087435095, "compression_ratio": 1.537037037037037, "no_speech_prob": 1.61061333540935e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 155664, "start": 1559.5400000000002, "end": 1568.8200000000002, "text": " And the manifest doesn't just hold the data. This is the part that I think is brilliant. It actively rejects conflated signatures. It enforces strict cryptographic roles.", "tokens": [50510, 400, 264, 10067, 1177, 380, 445, 1797, 264, 1412, 13, 639, 307, 264, 644, 300, 286, 519, 307, 10248, 13, 467, 13022, 8248, 82, 1497, 38539, 32322, 13, 467, 25495, 887, 10910, 9844, 12295, 9604, 13, 50974], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11579289087435095, "compression_ratio": 1.537037037037037, "no_speech_prob": 1.61061333540935e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 155664, "start": 1568.98, "end": 1575.5800000000002, "text": " Right. Up until now, if you saw a digital signature on a document, you usually just assumed a monolithic trust.", "tokens": [50982, 1779, 13, 5858, 1826, 586, 11, 498, 291, 1866, 257, 4562, 13397, 322, 257, 4166, 11, 291, 2673, 445, 15895, 257, 1108, 42878, 3361, 13, 51312], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11579289087435095, "compression_ratio": 1.537037037037037, "no_speech_prob": 1.61061333540935e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 157558, "start": 1575.58, "end": 1576.9399999999998, "text": " Oh, they signed it. It's good.", "tokens": [50365, 876, 11, 436, 8175, 309, 13, 467, 311, 665, 13, 50433], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13701523145039876, "compression_ratio": 1.6199261992619927, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983220606405335e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 157558, "start": 1577.12, "end": 1580.8799999999999, "text": " Yeah. We thought, okay, the person who signed this wrote it, they checked it, and they stand by it.", "tokens": [50442, 865, 13, 492, 1194, 11, 1392, 11, 264, 954, 567, 8175, 341, 4114, 309, 11, 436, 10033, 309, 11, 293, 436, 1463, 538, 309, 13, 50630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13701523145039876, "compression_ratio": 1.6199261992619927, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983220606405335e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 157558, "start": 1581.0, "end": 1581.1799999999998, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50636, 1779, 13, 50645], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13701523145039876, "compression_ratio": 1.6199261992619927, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983220606405335e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 157558, "start": 1581.52, "end": 1585.6399999999999, "text": " The manifest protocol shatters that monolithic trust into three distinct pieces.", "tokens": [50662, 440, 10067, 10336, 402, 37690, 300, 1108, 42878, 3361, 666, 1045, 10644, 3755, 13, 50868], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13701523145039876, "compression_ratio": 1.6199261992619927, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983220606405335e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 157558, "start": 1585.76, "end": 1586.78, "text": " Okay. What's piece number one?", "tokens": [50874, 1033, 13, 708, 311, 2522, 1230, 472, 30, 50925], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13701523145039876, "compression_ratio": 1.6199261992619927, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983220606405335e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 157558, "start": 1586.9199999999998, "end": 1591.6399999999999, "text": " Signature rule one is the assertion signature. This simply means I'm making this claim.", "tokens": [50932, 13515, 1503, 4978, 472, 307, 264, 19810, 313, 13397, 13, 639, 2935, 1355, 286, 478, 1455, 341, 3932, 13, 51168], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13701523145039876, "compression_ratio": 1.6199261992619927, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983220606405335e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 157558, "start": 1591.84, "end": 1592.1, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51178, 1033, 13, 51191], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13701523145039876, "compression_ratio": 1.6199261992619927, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983220606405335e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 157558, "start": 1592.6599999999999, "end": 1597.6, "text": " And it is crucial to note that under this protocol, authorship is not generation.", "tokens": [51219, 400, 309, 307, 11462, 281, 3637, 300, 833, 341, 10336, 11, 6979, 14752, 307, 406, 5125, 13, 51466], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13701523145039876, "compression_ratio": 1.6199261992619927, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983220606405335e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 157558, "start": 1598.02, "end": 1598.5, "text": " Meaning what?", "tokens": [51487, 19948, 437, 30, 51511], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13701523145039876, "compression_ratio": 1.6199261992619927, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983220606405335e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 159850, "start": 1598.5, "end": 1608.52, "text": " If I use an LLM to generate a paragraph of financial analysis, and I sign it with my assertion signature, I am taking human responsibility for asserting it.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 286, 764, 364, 441, 43, 44, 281, 8460, 257, 18865, 295, 4669, 5215, 11, 293, 286, 1465, 309, 365, 452, 19810, 313, 13397, 11, 286, 669, 1940, 1952, 6357, 337, 1256, 27187, 309, 13, 50866], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10270853553499494, "compression_ratio": 1.7777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496123485613355e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 159850, "start": 1608.6, "end": 1611.62, "text": " The fact that a machine generated the pixels is secondary.", "tokens": [50870, 440, 1186, 300, 257, 3479, 10833, 264, 18668, 307, 11396, 13, 51021], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10270853553499494, "compression_ratio": 1.7777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496123485613355e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 159850, "start": 1611.94, "end": 1616.88, "text": " Exactly. The fact that an AI wrote it is secondary to the fact that I am asserting it as truth.", "tokens": [51037, 7587, 13, 440, 1186, 300, 364, 7318, 4114, 309, 307, 11396, 281, 264, 1186, 300, 286, 669, 1256, 27187, 309, 382, 3494, 13, 51284], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10270853553499494, "compression_ratio": 1.7777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496123485613355e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 159850, "start": 1617.08, "end": 1620.68, "text": " Okay. Assertion. I am making the claim. What is the second rule?", "tokens": [51294, 1033, 13, 6281, 911, 313, 13, 286, 669, 1455, 264, 3932, 13, 708, 307, 264, 1150, 4978, 30, 51474], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10270853553499494, "compression_ratio": 1.7777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496123485613355e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 159850, "start": 1621.32, "end": 1623.7, "text": " Signature rule two is the verification signature.", "tokens": [51506, 13515, 1503, 4978, 732, 307, 264, 30206, 13397, 13, 51625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10270853553499494, "compression_ratio": 1.7777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496123485613355e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 159850, "start": 1623.84, "end": 1624.06, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51632, 1033, 13, 51643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10270853553499494, "compression_ratio": 1.7777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496123485613355e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 162406, "start": 1624.06, "end": 1630.04, "text": " This states, I used method X to check this claim, and here is the mathematical or empirical result.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 4368, 11, 286, 1143, 3170, 1783, 281, 1520, 341, 3932, 11, 293, 510, 307, 264, 18894, 420, 31886, 1874, 13, 50664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11638171212715015, "compression_ratio": 1.6216216216216217, "no_speech_prob": 1.3147406340702217e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 162406, "start": 1630.32, "end": 1632.3999999999999, "text": " Okay. So explicitly names the method.", "tokens": [50678, 1033, 13, 407, 20803, 5288, 264, 3170, 13, 50782], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11638171212715015, "compression_ratio": 1.6216216216216217, "no_speech_prob": 1.3147406340702217e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 162406, "start": 1632.52, "end": 1639.26, "text": " Yes. This embodies the core epistemic principle that verification is not absolute universal truth.", "tokens": [50788, 1079, 13, 639, 4605, 6087, 264, 4965, 2388, 468, 3438, 8665, 300, 30206, 307, 406, 8236, 11455, 3494, 13, 51125], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11638171212715015, "compression_ratio": 1.6216216216216217, "no_speech_prob": 1.3147406340702217e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 162406, "start": 1639.54, "end": 1641.02, "text": " It is strictly method relative.", "tokens": [51139, 467, 307, 20792, 3170, 4972, 13, 51213], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11638171212715015, "compression_ratio": 1.6216216216216217, "no_speech_prob": 1.3147406340702217e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 162406, "start": 1641.52, "end": 1645.1599999999999, "text": " Right. The signature doesn't just say true. It says how it was checked.", "tokens": [51238, 1779, 13, 440, 13397, 1177, 380, 445, 584, 2074, 13, 467, 1619, 577, 309, 390, 10033, 13, 51420], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11638171212715015, "compression_ratio": 1.6216216216216217, "no_speech_prob": 1.3147406340702217e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 162406, "start": 1645.3, "end": 1652.72, "text": " Maybe it was checked by the lean foreproof assistant, or a reproducible Python data pipeline, or a double-blind human peer review protocol.", "tokens": [51427, 2704, 309, 390, 10033, 538, 264, 11659, 2091, 15690, 10994, 11, 420, 257, 11408, 32128, 15329, 1412, 15517, 11, 420, 257, 3834, 12, 47494, 1952, 15108, 3131, 10336, 13, 51798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11638171212715015, "compression_ratio": 1.6216216216216217, "no_speech_prob": 1.3147406340702217e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 165272, "start": 1652.72, "end": 1656.84, "text": " So I can assert a claim without having the skills to verify it myself.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 286, 393, 19810, 257, 3932, 1553, 1419, 264, 3942, 281, 16888, 309, 2059, 13, 50571], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18692268559962144, "compression_ratio": 1.6082474226804124, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363671485539188e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 165272, "start": 1657.02, "end": 1657.24, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50580, 1079, 13, 50591], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18692268559962144, "compression_ratio": 1.6082474226804124, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363671485539188e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 165272, "start": 1657.44, "end": 1661.74, "text": " And a completely separate entity can verify it without taking responsibility for asserting it.", "tokens": [50601, 400, 257, 2584, 4994, 13977, 393, 16888, 309, 1553, 1940, 6357, 337, 1256, 27187, 309, 13, 50816], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18692268559962144, "compression_ratio": 1.6082474226804124, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363671485539188e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 165272, "start": 1661.84, "end": 1663.04, "text": " Exactly. They are decoupled.", "tokens": [50821, 7587, 13, 814, 366, 979, 263, 15551, 13, 50881], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18692268559962144, "compression_ratio": 1.6082474226804124, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363671485539188e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 165272, "start": 1663.22, "end": 1664.04, "text": " And the third rule?", "tokens": [50890, 400, 264, 2636, 4978, 30, 50931], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18692268559962144, "compression_ratio": 1.6082474226804124, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363671485539188e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 165272, "start": 1664.3, "end": 1667.08, "text": " The third rule is the transformation attestation.", "tokens": [50944, 440, 2636, 4978, 307, 264, 9887, 951, 377, 399, 13, 51083], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18692268559962144, "compression_ratio": 1.6082474226804124, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363671485539188e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 165272, "start": 1667.22, "end": 1667.88, "text": " The transformation.", "tokens": [51090, 440, 9887, 13, 51123], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18692268559962144, "compression_ratio": 1.6082474226804124, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363671485539188e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 165272, "start": 1668.32, "end": 1669.38, "text": " This signature states,", "tokens": [51145, 639, 13397, 4368, 11, 51198], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18692268559962144, "compression_ratio": 1.6082474226804124, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363671485539188e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 166938, "start": 1669.38, "end": 1686.0400000000002, "text": " This is the critical signature that bridges the gap between the original document and the AI summarized version.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 307, 264, 4924, 13397, 300, 21114, 264, 7417, 1296, 264, 3380, 4166, 293, 264, 7318, 14611, 1602, 3037, 13, 51198], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12638615644895113, "compression_ratio": 1.3333333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.7754352675536378e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 166938, "start": 1686.16, "end": 1687.0600000000002, "text": " It is the bridge.", "tokens": [51204, 467, 307, 264, 7283, 13, 51249], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12638615644895113, "compression_ratio": 1.3333333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.7754352675536378e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 166938, "start": 1687.18, "end": 1688.8600000000001, "text": " It's exactly like buying a house.", "tokens": [51255, 467, 311, 2293, 411, 6382, 257, 1782, 13, 51339], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12638615644895113, "compression_ratio": 1.3333333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.7754352675536378e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 166938, "start": 1688.94, "end": 1690.7, "text": " Oh, I like this. Go on.", "tokens": [51343, 876, 11, 286, 411, 341, 13, 1037, 322, 13, 51431], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12638615644895113, "compression_ratio": 1.3333333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.7754352675536378e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 169070, "start": 1690.7, "end": 1695.1000000000001, "text": " The assertion signature is the seller writing the real estate listing, saying,", "tokens": [50365, 440, 19810, 313, 13397, 307, 264, 23600, 3579, 264, 957, 9749, 22161, 11, 1566, 11, 50585], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18950668334960938, "compression_ratio": 1.75, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488054411373243e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 169070, "start": 1695.28, "end": 1695.94, "text": " This house is great.", "tokens": [50594, 639, 1782, 307, 869, 13, 50627], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18950668334960938, "compression_ratio": 1.75, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488054411373243e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 169070, "start": 1696.3, "end": 1697.46, "text": " The foundation is perfect.", "tokens": [50645, 440, 7030, 307, 2176, 13, 50703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18950668334960938, "compression_ratio": 1.75, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488054411373243e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 169070, "start": 1697.5800000000002, "end": 1698.66, "text": " It has three bedrooms.", "tokens": [50709, 467, 575, 1045, 39955, 13, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18950668334960938, "compression_ratio": 1.75, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488054411373243e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 169070, "start": 1698.9, "end": 1701.0800000000002, "text": " They are asserting the claim to the market.", "tokens": [50775, 814, 366, 1256, 27187, 264, 3932, 281, 264, 2142, 13, 50884], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18950668334960938, "compression_ratio": 1.75, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488054411373243e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 169070, "start": 1701.7, "end": 1706.22, "text": " The verification signature is the independent structural engineer coming in and saying,", "tokens": [50915, 440, 30206, 13397, 307, 264, 6695, 15067, 11403, 1348, 294, 293, 1566, 11, 51141], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18950668334960938, "compression_ratio": 1.75, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488054411373243e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 169070, "start": 1706.88, "end": 1713.38, "text": " I ran a specific set of stress tests on the foundation, and based on my specific method, it is solid.", "tokens": [51174, 286, 5872, 257, 2685, 992, 295, 4244, 6921, 322, 264, 7030, 11, 293, 2361, 322, 452, 2685, 3170, 11, 309, 307, 5100, 13, 51499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18950668334960938, "compression_ratio": 1.75, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488054411373243e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 169070, "start": 1713.82, "end": 1714.7, "text": " Okay. And the transformation?", "tokens": [51521, 1033, 13, 400, 264, 9887, 30, 51565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18950668334960938, "compression_ratio": 1.75, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488054411373243e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 171470, "start": 1714.7, "end": 1722.14, "text": " The transformation attestation is the municipal appraiser coming in five years later after you've knocked down a wall to remodel the kitchen and saying,", "tokens": [50365, 440, 9887, 951, 377, 399, 307, 264, 27177, 724, 424, 6694, 1348, 294, 1732, 924, 1780, 934, 291, 600, 16914, 760, 257, 2929, 281, 890, 41147, 264, 6525, 293, 1566, 11, 50737], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1211538314819336, "compression_ratio": 1.66, "no_speech_prob": 1.662134622645861e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 171470, "start": 1722.52, "end": 1727.32, "text": " After the structural transformation, it is still fundamentally the same property functioning safely.", "tokens": [50756, 2381, 264, 15067, 9887, 11, 309, 307, 920, 17879, 264, 912, 4707, 18483, 11750, 13, 50996], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1211538314819336, "compression_ratio": 1.66, "no_speech_prob": 1.662134622645861e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 171470, "start": 1727.78, "end": 1729.3, "text": " That is exactly how it works.", "tokens": [51019, 663, 307, 2293, 577, 309, 1985, 13, 51095], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1211538314819336, "compression_ratio": 1.66, "no_speech_prob": 1.662134622645861e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 171470, "start": 1729.8400000000001, "end": 1736.46, "text": " And taking that house analogy further, if the seller tries to be the inspector, you are walking into a trap.", "tokens": [51122, 400, 1940, 300, 1782, 21663, 3052, 11, 498, 264, 23600, 9898, 281, 312, 264, 34564, 11, 291, 366, 4494, 666, 257, 11487, 13, 51453], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1211538314819336, "compression_ratio": 1.66, "no_speech_prob": 1.662134622645861e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 171470, "start": 1736.64, "end": 1738.1200000000001, "text": " A massive conflict of interest.", "tokens": [51462, 316, 5994, 6596, 295, 1179, 13, 51536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1211538314819336, "compression_ratio": 1.66, "no_speech_prob": 1.662134622645861e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 171470, "start": 1738.28, "end": 1741.7, "text": " The protocol literally forbids this at a cryptographic level.", "tokens": [51544, 440, 10336, 3736, 16603, 3742, 341, 412, 257, 9844, 12295, 1496, 13, 51715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1211538314819336, "compression_ratio": 1.66, "no_speech_prob": 1.662134622645861e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 171470, "start": 1741.96, "end": 1742.4, "text": " Oh, really?", "tokens": [51728, 876, 11, 534, 30, 51750], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1211538314819336, "compression_ratio": 1.66, "no_speech_prob": 1.662134622645861e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 174240, "start": 1742.4, "end": 1755.7800000000002, "text": " It explicitly states, No manifest entry may be interpreted as satisfying more than one of the assertion, verification, and transformation attestation rules unless it carries the corresponding distinct signature for each.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 20803, 4368, 11, 883, 10067, 8729, 815, 312, 26749, 382, 18348, 544, 813, 472, 295, 264, 19810, 313, 11, 30206, 11, 293, 9887, 951, 377, 399, 4474, 5969, 309, 16402, 264, 11760, 10644, 13397, 337, 1184, 13, 51034], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13026514649391174, "compression_ratio": 1.6458333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.184787940839872e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 174240, "start": 1755.98, "end": 1756.44, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51044, 3153, 13, 51067], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13026514649391174, "compression_ratio": 1.6458333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.184787940839872e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 174240, "start": 1756.72, "end": 1767.3400000000001, "text": " If a single cryptographic key tries to claim authorship and verification simultaneously without explicit separate cryptographic steps, the protocol's logic engine flags it as invalid.", "tokens": [51081, 759, 257, 2167, 9844, 12295, 2141, 9898, 281, 3932, 6979, 14752, 293, 30206, 16561, 1553, 13691, 4994, 9844, 12295, 4439, 11, 264, 10336, 311, 9952, 2848, 23265, 309, 382, 34702, 13, 51612], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13026514649391174, "compression_ratio": 1.6458333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.184787940839872e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 174240, "start": 1767.5600000000002, "end": 1769.7800000000002, "text": " It physically prevents the conflation of powers.", "tokens": [51623, 467, 9762, 22367, 264, 1497, 24278, 295, 8674, 13, 51734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13026514649391174, "compression_ratio": 1.6458333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.184787940839872e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 174240, "start": 1769.94, "end": 1770.5600000000002, "text": " That's amazing.", "tokens": [51742, 663, 311, 2243, 13, 51773], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13026514649391174, "compression_ratio": 1.6458333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.184787940839872e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 177056, "start": 1770.56, "end": 1774.2, "text": " And you mentioned earlier that this manifest is append-only.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 291, 2835, 3071, 300, 341, 10067, 307, 34116, 12, 25202, 13, 50547], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17477774620056152, "compression_ratio": 1.632398753894081, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324757943694037e-12}, {"id": 460, "seek": 177056, "start": 1774.46, "end": 1774.7, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50560, 1079, 13, 50572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17477774620056152, "compression_ratio": 1.632398753894081, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324757943694037e-12}, {"id": 461, "seek": 177056, "start": 1774.84, "end": 1777.5, "text": " Let's dive into what that means for the life cycle of a claim.", "tokens": [50579, 961, 311, 9192, 666, 437, 300, 1355, 337, 264, 993, 6586, 295, 257, 3932, 13, 50712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17477774620056152, "compression_ratio": 1.632398753894081, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324757943694037e-12}, {"id": 462, "seek": 177056, "start": 1777.6, "end": 1778.4199999999998, "text": " Why is that important?", "tokens": [50717, 1545, 307, 300, 1021, 30, 50758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17477774620056152, "compression_ratio": 1.632398753894081, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324757943694037e-12}, {"id": 463, "seek": 177056, "start": 1778.7, "end": 1780.4199999999998, "text": " It means you can never erase the past.", "tokens": [50772, 467, 1355, 291, 393, 1128, 23525, 264, 1791, 13, 50858], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17477774620056152, "compression_ratio": 1.632398753894081, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324757943694037e-12}, {"id": 464, "seek": 177056, "start": 1780.52, "end": 1781.8999999999999, "text": " Which happens all the time on the web.", "tokens": [50863, 3013, 2314, 439, 264, 565, 322, 264, 3670, 13, 50932], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17477774620056152, "compression_ratio": 1.632398753894081, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324757943694037e-12}, {"id": 465, "seek": 177056, "start": 1782.12, "end": 1782.56, "text": " Constantly.", "tokens": [50943, 8574, 3627, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17477774620056152, "compression_ratio": 1.632398753894081, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324757943694037e-12}, {"id": 466, "seek": 177056, "start": 1782.86, "end": 1788.0, "text": " In our current web infrastructure, if an article is wrong, a publisher might just stealth edit the web page.", "tokens": [50980, 682, 527, 2190, 3670, 6896, 11, 498, 364, 7222, 307, 2085, 11, 257, 25088, 1062, 445, 25756, 8129, 264, 3670, 3028, 13, 51237], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17477774620056152, "compression_ratio": 1.632398753894081, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324757943694037e-12}, {"id": 467, "seek": 177056, "start": 1788.3, "end": 1790.1599999999999, "text": " The error just vanishes into the ether.", "tokens": [51252, 440, 6713, 445, 3161, 16423, 666, 264, 37096, 13, 51345], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17477774620056152, "compression_ratio": 1.632398753894081, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324757943694037e-12}, {"id": 468, "seek": 177056, "start": 1790.3, "end": 1791.24, "text": " Like it never happened.", "tokens": [51352, 1743, 309, 1128, 2011, 13, 51399], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17477774620056152, "compression_ratio": 1.632398753894081, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324757943694037e-12}, {"id": 469, "seek": 177056, "start": 1791.56, "end": 1793.24, "text": " The manifest protocol forbids this.", "tokens": [51415, 440, 10067, 10336, 16603, 3742, 341, 13, 51499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17477774620056152, "compression_ratio": 1.632398753894081, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324757943694037e-12}, {"id": 470, "seek": 177056, "start": 1794.1, "end": 1796.52, "text": " The paper provides a fantastic scenario.", "tokens": [51542, 440, 3035, 6417, 257, 5456, 9005, 13, 51663], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17477774620056152, "compression_ratio": 1.632398753894081, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324757943694037e-12}, {"id": 471, "seek": 177056, "start": 1796.94, "end": 1797.6, "text": " Example one.", "tokens": [51684, 24755, 781, 472, 13, 51717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17477774620056152, "compression_ratio": 1.632398753894081, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324757943694037e-12}, {"id": 472, "seek": 177056, "start": 1797.72, "end": 1798.3999999999999, "text": " Walk me through it.", "tokens": [51723, 10818, 385, 807, 309, 13, 51757], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17477774620056152, "compression_ratio": 1.632398753894081, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324757943694037e-12}, {"id": 473, "seek": 179840, "start": 1798.4, "end": 1802.98, "text": " Let's say a complex mathematical claim is published simply as a conjecture.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 311, 584, 257, 3997, 18894, 3932, 307, 6572, 2935, 382, 257, 416, 1020, 540, 13, 50594], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21635779415268497, "compression_ratio": 1.5311004784688995, "no_speech_prob": 1.472224360650476e-12}, {"id": 474, "seek": 179840, "start": 1803.26, "end": 1805.92, "text": " It'd have an assertion signature, but no verification.", "tokens": [50608, 467, 1116, 362, 364, 19810, 313, 13397, 11, 457, 572, 30206, 13, 50741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21635779415268497, "compression_ratio": 1.5311004784688995, "no_speech_prob": 1.472224360650476e-12}, {"id": 475, "seek": 179840, "start": 1806.2800000000002, "end": 1807.8600000000001, "text": " It's just an idea out in the wild.", "tokens": [50759, 467, 311, 445, 364, 1558, 484, 294, 264, 4868, 13, 50838], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21635779415268497, "compression_ratio": 1.5311004784688995, "no_speech_prob": 1.472224360650476e-12}, {"id": 476, "seek": 179840, "start": 1808.0400000000002, "end": 1808.3000000000002, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50847, 1033, 13, 50860], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21635779415268497, "compression_ratio": 1.5311004784688995, "no_speech_prob": 1.472224360650476e-12}, {"id": 477, "seek": 179840, "start": 1808.7, "end": 1812.8600000000001, "text": " Six months later, a brilliant mathematician formally proves it.", "tokens": [50880, 11678, 2493, 1780, 11, 257, 10248, 48281, 25983, 25019, 309, 13, 51088], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21635779415268497, "compression_ratio": 1.5311004784688995, "no_speech_prob": 1.472224360650476e-12}, {"id": 478, "seek": 179840, "start": 1812.96, "end": 1813.16, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51093, 865, 13, 51103], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21635779415268497, "compression_ratio": 1.5311004784688995, "no_speech_prob": 1.472224360650476e-12}, {"id": 479, "seek": 179840, "start": 1813.16, "end": 1818.2, "text": " A verification signature with the status accepted is appended to the manifest.", "tokens": [51103, 316, 30206, 13397, 365, 264, 6558, 9035, 307, 724, 3502, 281, 264, 10067, 13, 51355], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21635779415268497, "compression_ratio": 1.5311004784688995, "no_speech_prob": 1.472224360650476e-12}, {"id": 480, "seek": 181820, "start": 1818.2, "end": 1820.18, "text": " So now the world sees it as verified.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 586, 264, 1002, 8194, 309, 382, 31197, 13, 50464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17086288050601356, "compression_ratio": 1.5530973451327434, "no_speech_prob": 1.3460516338700823e-12}, {"id": 481, "seek": 181820, "start": 1820.56, "end": 1820.8, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50483, 1079, 13, 50495], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17086288050601356, "compression_ratio": 1.5530973451327434, "no_speech_prob": 1.3460516338700823e-12}, {"id": 482, "seek": 181820, "start": 1821.38, "end": 1826.5, "text": " But let's say a year later, a different researcher finds a fatal, subtle flaw in that proof.", "tokens": [50524, 583, 718, 311, 584, 257, 1064, 1780, 11, 257, 819, 21751, 10704, 257, 24069, 11, 13743, 13717, 294, 300, 8177, 13, 50780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17086288050601356, "compression_ratio": 1.5530973451327434, "no_speech_prob": 1.3460516338700823e-12}, {"id": 483, "seek": 181820, "start": 1826.66, "end": 1827.02, "text": " Uh-oh.", "tokens": [50788, 4019, 12, 1445, 13, 50806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17086288050601356, "compression_ratio": 1.5530973451327434, "no_speech_prob": 1.3460516338700823e-12}, {"id": 484, "seek": 181820, "start": 1827.52, "end": 1830.32, "text": " Under the current system, we might try to just delete the old proof.", "tokens": [50831, 6974, 264, 2190, 1185, 11, 321, 1062, 853, 281, 445, 12097, 264, 1331, 8177, 13, 50971], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17086288050601356, "compression_ratio": 1.5530973451327434, "no_speech_prob": 1.3460516338700823e-12}, {"id": 485, "seek": 181820, "start": 1830.8400000000001, "end": 1834.92, "text": " Under the manifest protocol, you cannot go into manifest and delete the accepted signature.", "tokens": [50997, 6974, 264, 10067, 10336, 11, 291, 2644, 352, 666, 10067, 293, 12097, 264, 9035, 13397, 13, 51201], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17086288050601356, "compression_ratio": 1.5530973451327434, "no_speech_prob": 1.3460516338700823e-12}, {"id": 486, "seek": 181820, "start": 1835.2, "end": 1837.02, "text": " Because that would be erasing history.", "tokens": [51215, 1436, 300, 576, 312, 1189, 3349, 2503, 13, 51306], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17086288050601356, "compression_ratio": 1.5530973451327434, "no_speech_prob": 1.3460516338700823e-12}, {"id": 487, "seek": 181820, "start": 1837.22, "end": 1837.5800000000002, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51316, 7587, 13, 51334], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17086288050601356, "compression_ratio": 1.5530973451327434, "no_speech_prob": 1.3460516338700823e-12}, {"id": 488, "seek": 183758, "start": 1837.58, "end": 1846.02, "text": " Instead, a new superseding verification signature with the status rejected is appended to the end of the cryptographic log, citing the flaw.", "tokens": [50365, 7156, 11, 257, 777, 37906, 9794, 30206, 13397, 365, 264, 6558, 15749, 307, 724, 3502, 281, 264, 917, 295, 264, 9844, 12295, 3565, 11, 48749, 264, 13717, 13, 50787], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10203643143177032, "compression_ratio": 1.2727272727272727, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144777351291163e-12}, {"id": 489, "seek": 184602, "start": 1846.02, "end": 1849.94, "text": " So the history of the claim is completely visible to anyone who queries the manifest.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 264, 2503, 295, 264, 3932, 307, 2584, 8974, 281, 2878, 567, 24109, 264, 10067, 13, 50561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10663028096043786, "compression_ratio": 1.6682926829268292, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182054169549322e-12}, {"id": 490, "seek": 184602, "start": 1850.34, "end": 1854.1, "text": " You see the birth, the false validation, and the eventual refutation.", "tokens": [50581, 509, 536, 264, 3965, 11, 264, 7908, 24071, 11, 293, 264, 33160, 1895, 11380, 13, 50769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10663028096043786, "compression_ratio": 1.6682926829268292, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182054169549322e-12}, {"id": 491, "seek": 184602, "start": 1854.54, "end": 1854.94, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50791, 7587, 13, 50811], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10663028096043786, "compression_ratio": 1.6682926829268292, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182054169549322e-12}, {"id": 492, "seek": 184602, "start": 1855.6399999999999, "end": 1859.18, "text": " The manifest retains an epistemic history, not a single mutable verdict.", "tokens": [50846, 440, 10067, 1533, 2315, 364, 2388, 468, 3438, 2503, 11, 406, 257, 2167, 5839, 712, 33957, 13, 51023], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10663028096043786, "compression_ratio": 1.6682926829268292, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182054169549322e-12}, {"id": 493, "seek": 184602, "start": 1859.52, "end": 1864.76, "text": " You can see exactly when it was proposed, when it was believed to be true, and when it was proven false.", "tokens": [51040, 509, 393, 536, 2293, 562, 309, 390, 10348, 11, 562, 309, 390, 7847, 281, 312, 2074, 11, 293, 562, 309, 390, 12785, 7908, 13, 51302], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10663028096043786, "compression_ratio": 1.6682926829268292, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182054169549322e-12}, {"id": 494, "seek": 186476, "start": 1864.76, "end": 1869.78, "text": " It treats truth as a process occurring over time, not a static badge.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 19566, 3494, 382, 257, 1399, 18386, 670, 565, 11, 406, 257, 13437, 25797, 13, 50616], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13989543914794922, "compression_ratio": 1.5349794238683128, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112910260201232e-12}, {"id": 495, "seek": 186476, "start": 1870.0, "end": 1870.28, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50627, 1079, 13, 50641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13989543914794922, "compression_ratio": 1.5349794238683128, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112910260201232e-12}, {"id": 496, "seek": 186476, "start": 1870.3799999999999, "end": 1875.3799999999999, "text": " This sounds incredibly robust, but it raises a massive practical caution.", "tokens": [50646, 639, 3263, 6252, 13956, 11, 457, 309, 19658, 257, 5994, 8496, 23585, 13, 50896], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13989543914794922, "compression_ratio": 1.5349794238683128, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112910260201232e-12}, {"id": 497, "seek": 186476, "start": 1875.78, "end": 1876.2, "text": " Let's hear it.", "tokens": [50916, 961, 311, 1568, 309, 13, 50937], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13989543914794922, "compression_ratio": 1.5349794238683128, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112910260201232e-12}, {"id": 498, "seek": 186476, "start": 1876.36, "end": 1880.84, "text": " We have all these signatures flying around, assertions, verifications, attestations.", "tokens": [50945, 492, 362, 439, 613, 32322, 7137, 926, 11, 19810, 626, 11, 1306, 7833, 11, 951, 377, 763, 13, 51169], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13989543914794922, "compression_ratio": 1.5349794238683128, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112910260201232e-12}, {"id": 499, "seek": 186476, "start": 1881.24, "end": 1884.48, "text": " Why should the reader trust the people or the machines signing them?", "tokens": [51189, 1545, 820, 264, 15149, 3361, 264, 561, 420, 264, 8379, 13393, 552, 30, 51351], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13989543914794922, "compression_ratio": 1.5349794238683128, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112910260201232e-12}, {"id": 500, "seek": 186476, "start": 1884.62, "end": 1887.1, "text": " That is the million-dollar question for the web.", "tokens": [51358, 663, 307, 264, 2459, 12, 40485, 1168, 337, 264, 3670, 13, 51482], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13989543914794922, "compression_ratio": 1.5349794238683128, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112910260201232e-12}, {"id": 501, "seek": 186476, "start": 1887.24, "end": 1887.52, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51489, 1779, 13, 51503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13989543914794922, "compression_ratio": 1.5349794238683128, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112910260201232e-12}, {"id": 502, "seek": 188752, "start": 1887.52, "end": 1902.06, "text": " If anyone can mathematically append a verification signature to the manifest, what stops a bad actor, or just a hallucinating AI, from verifying their own false claims using a bogus pseudoscientific method?", "tokens": [50365, 759, 2878, 393, 44003, 34116, 257, 30206, 13397, 281, 264, 10067, 11, 437, 10094, 257, 1578, 8747, 11, 420, 445, 257, 35212, 8205, 7318, 11, 490, 1306, 5489, 641, 1065, 7908, 9441, 1228, 257, 26132, 301, 25505, 35063, 5412, 1089, 3170, 30, 51092], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10563326781650759, "compression_ratio": 1.5986622073578596, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674023494047229e-12}, {"id": 503, "seek": 188752, "start": 1902.24, "end": 1907.06, "text": " That is the exact vulnerability that Section 6 of Paper 2 addresses through the policy layer.", "tokens": [51101, 663, 307, 264, 1900, 24210, 300, 21804, 1386, 295, 24990, 568, 16862, 807, 264, 3897, 4583, 13, 51342], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10563326781650759, "compression_ratio": 1.5986622073578596, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674023494047229e-12}, {"id": 504, "seek": 188752, "start": 1907.1399999999999, "end": 1908.02, "text": " The policy layer, okay.", "tokens": [51346, 440, 3897, 4583, 11, 1392, 13, 51390], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10563326781650759, "compression_ratio": 1.5986622073578596, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674023494047229e-12}, {"id": 505, "seek": 188752, "start": 1908.26, "end": 1913.76, "text": " Having a valid cryptographic signature on a transformation attestation is completely meaningless on its own.", "tokens": [51402, 10222, 257, 7363, 9844, 12295, 13397, 322, 257, 9887, 951, 377, 399, 307, 2584, 33232, 322, 1080, 1065, 13, 51677], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10563326781650759, "compression_ratio": 1.5986622073578596, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674023494047229e-12}, {"id": 506, "seek": 188752, "start": 1914.02, "end": 1916.18, "text": " Yeah, it just proves that someone signed it.", "tokens": [51690, 865, 11, 309, 445, 25019, 300, 1580, 8175, 309, 13, 51798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10563326781650759, "compression_ratio": 1.5986622073578596, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674023494047229e-12}, {"id": 507, "seek": 191618, "start": 1916.18, "end": 1921.92, "text": " The software rendering the document to the reader has to ask a fundamental question.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 4722, 22407, 264, 4166, 281, 264, 15149, 575, 281, 1029, 257, 8088, 1168, 13, 50652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11048257491167854, "compression_ratio": 1.6337448559670782, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252654824923773e-12}, {"id": 508, "seek": 191618, "start": 1923.18, "end": 1934.3, "text": " Was the entity who signed this actually authorized by the reader's trusted institutions to use that specific verification method for that specific type of claim?", "tokens": [50715, 3027, 264, 13977, 567, 8175, 341, 767, 28312, 538, 264, 15149, 311, 16034, 8142, 281, 764, 300, 2685, 30206, 3170, 337, 300, 2685, 2010, 295, 3932, 30, 51271], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11048257491167854, "compression_ratio": 1.6337448559670782, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252654824923773e-12}, {"id": 509, "seek": 191618, "start": 1934.48, "end": 1941.5600000000002, "text": " Okay, so the signature proves who did the checking and how they did it, but the policy layer checks if they were actually allowed to do it.", "tokens": [51280, 1033, 11, 370, 264, 13397, 25019, 567, 630, 264, 8568, 293, 577, 436, 630, 309, 11, 457, 264, 3897, 4583, 13834, 498, 436, 645, 767, 4350, 281, 360, 309, 13, 51634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11048257491167854, "compression_ratio": 1.6337448559670782, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252654824923773e-12}, {"id": 510, "seek": 191618, "start": 1941.64, "end": 1942.1200000000001, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51638, 48746, 736, 13, 51662], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11048257491167854, "compression_ratio": 1.6337448559670782, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252654824923773e-12}, {"id": 511, "seek": 194212, "start": 1942.12, "end": 1946.78, "text": " It cleanly separates trust delegation from the truth of what is delegated.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 2541, 356, 34149, 3361, 36602, 490, 264, 3494, 295, 437, 307, 15824, 770, 13, 50598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1689583220571842, "compression_ratio": 1.6923076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396473580595263e-12}, {"id": 512, "seek": 194212, "start": 1947.08, "end": 1947.82, "text": " How do they manage that?", "tokens": [50613, 1012, 360, 436, 3067, 300, 30, 50650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1689583220571842, "compression_ratio": 1.6923076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396473580595263e-12}, {"id": 513, "seek": 194212, "start": 1947.9199999999998, "end": 1952.5, "text": " To manage this, the paper formalizes what they call a claim-type policy.", "tokens": [50655, 1407, 3067, 341, 11, 264, 3035, 9860, 5660, 437, 436, 818, 257, 3932, 12, 20467, 3897, 13, 50884], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1689583220571842, "compression_ratio": 1.6923076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396473580595263e-12}, {"id": 514, "seek": 194212, "start": 1952.9399999999998, "end": 1956.04, "text": " Every claim in the manifest is tagged with an epistemic type.", "tokens": [50906, 2048, 3932, 294, 264, 10067, 307, 40239, 365, 364, 2388, 468, 3438, 2010, 13, 51061], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1689583220571842, "compression_ratio": 1.6923076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396473580595263e-12}, {"id": 515, "seek": 194212, "start": 1956.1799999999998, "end": 1957.1999999999998, "text": " An epistemic type.", "tokens": [51068, 1107, 2388, 468, 3438, 2010, 13, 51119], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1689583220571842, "compression_ratio": 1.6923076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396473580595263e-12}, {"id": 516, "seek": 194212, "start": 1957.36, "end": 1958.1999999999998, "text": " Give me some examples.", "tokens": [51127, 5303, 385, 512, 5110, 13, 51169], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1689583220571842, "compression_ratio": 1.6923076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396473580595263e-12}, {"id": 517, "seek": 194212, "start": 1958.4399999999998, "end": 1960.5, "text": " Is this an empirical claim about the physical world?", "tokens": [51181, 1119, 341, 364, 31886, 3932, 466, 264, 4001, 1002, 30, 51284], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1689583220571842, "compression_ratio": 1.6923076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396473580595263e-12}, {"id": 518, "seek": 194212, "start": 1960.9799999999998, "end": 1963.36, "text": " Is it a strictly logical mathematical claim?", "tokens": [51308, 1119, 309, 257, 20792, 14978, 18894, 3932, 30, 51427], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1689583220571842, "compression_ratio": 1.6923076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396473580595263e-12}, {"id": 519, "seek": 194212, "start": 1963.8999999999999, "end": 1965.12, "text": " Is it informal prose?", "tokens": [51454, 1119, 309, 24342, 12505, 30, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1689583220571842, "compression_ratio": 1.6923076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396473580595263e-12}, {"id": 520, "seek": 196512, "start": 1965.12, "end": 1972.08, "text": " For each type, the policy defines which adjudication regimes are accepted and which specific verifiers are trusted to use them.", "tokens": [50365, 1171, 1184, 2010, 11, 264, 3897, 23122, 597, 614, 9218, 8758, 45738, 366, 9035, 293, 597, 2685, 1306, 23463, 366, 16034, 281, 764, 552, 13, 50713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10700608825683594, "compression_ratio": 1.6440129449838188, "no_speech_prob": 1.4045094297657212e-12}, {"id": 521, "seek": 196512, "start": 1972.1799999999998, "end": 1974.54, "text": " How does that play out in a real-world scenario?", "tokens": [50718, 1012, 775, 300, 862, 484, 294, 257, 957, 12, 13217, 9005, 30, 50836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10700608825683594, "compression_ratio": 1.6440129449838188, "no_speech_prob": 1.4045094297657212e-12}, {"id": 522, "seek": 196512, "start": 1974.9599999999998, "end": 1977.36, "text": " Let's say you have a claim typed as informal prose.", "tokens": [50857, 961, 311, 584, 291, 362, 257, 3932, 33941, 382, 24342, 12505, 13, 50977], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10700608825683594, "compression_ratio": 1.6440129449838188, "no_speech_prob": 1.4045094297657212e-12}, {"id": 523, "seek": 196512, "start": 1977.5, "end": 1979.6, "text": " Let's say it's a summary of a historical event.", "tokens": [50984, 961, 311, 584, 309, 311, 257, 12691, 295, 257, 8584, 2280, 13, 51089], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10700608825683594, "compression_ratio": 1.6440129449838188, "no_speech_prob": 1.4045094297657212e-12}, {"id": 524, "seek": 196512, "start": 1979.7199999999998, "end": 1991.54, "text": " A university's policy engine might dictate that for informal prose, a single expert human attestation signature is sufficient to light the document up as verified for their students.", "tokens": [51095, 316, 5454, 311, 3897, 2848, 1062, 36071, 300, 337, 24342, 12505, 11, 257, 2167, 5844, 1952, 951, 377, 399, 13397, 307, 11563, 281, 1442, 264, 4166, 493, 382, 31197, 337, 641, 1731, 13, 51686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10700608825683594, "compression_ratio": 1.6440129449838188, "no_speech_prob": 1.4045094297657212e-12}, {"id": 525, "seek": 196512, "start": 1991.6799999999998, "end": 1991.9399999999998, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51693, 1779, 13, 51706], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10700608825683594, "compression_ratio": 1.6440129449838188, "no_speech_prob": 1.4045094297657212e-12}, {"id": 526, "seek": 196512, "start": 1992.04, "end": 1993.32, "text": " A professor signs off on it.", "tokens": [51711, 316, 8304, 7880, 766, 322, 309, 13, 51775], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10700608825683594, "compression_ratio": 1.6440129449838188, "no_speech_prob": 1.4045094297657212e-12}, {"id": 527, "seek": 196512, "start": 1993.4199999999998, "end": 1993.78, "text": " That's good.", "tokens": [51780, 663, 311, 665, 13, 51798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10700608825683594, "compression_ratio": 1.6440129449838188, "no_speech_prob": 1.4045094297657212e-12}, {"id": 528, "seek": 199378, "start": 1993.78, "end": 2006.52, "text": " But if the claim is typed as a mathematical theorem, that exact same university's policy might demand a formal, machine-checked proof using a specific, recognized proof assistant kernel like Lean 4.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 498, 264, 3932, 307, 33941, 382, 257, 18894, 20904, 11, 300, 1900, 912, 5454, 311, 3897, 1062, 4733, 257, 9860, 11, 3479, 12, 15723, 292, 8177, 1228, 257, 2685, 11, 9823, 8177, 10994, 28256, 411, 49303, 1017, 13, 51002], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.096822876528085, "compression_ratio": 1.5853658536585367, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858657703010648e-12}, {"id": 529, "seek": 199378, "start": 2007.54, "end": 2014.48, "text": " If a human professor tries to sign the mathematical claim using just human review, the policy layer will reject the verification.", "tokens": [51053, 759, 257, 1952, 8304, 9898, 281, 1465, 264, 18894, 3932, 1228, 445, 1952, 3131, 11, 264, 3897, 4583, 486, 8248, 264, 30206, 13, 51400], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.096822876528085, "compression_ratio": 1.5853658536585367, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858657703010648e-12}, {"id": 530, "seek": 199378, "start": 2015.22, "end": 2018.26, "text": " The human signature isn't authorized for that epistemic type.", "tokens": [51437, 440, 1952, 13397, 1943, 380, 28312, 337, 300, 2388, 468, 3438, 2010, 13, 51589], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.096822876528085, "compression_ratio": 1.5853658536585367, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858657703010648e-12}, {"id": 531, "seek": 201826, "start": 2018.26, "end": 2029.26, "text": " Ah, so different institutions like a university, a news organization, a financial regulator, they can literally enforce entirely different standards of truth on the exact same underlying manifest document.", "tokens": [50365, 2438, 11, 370, 819, 8142, 411, 257, 5454, 11, 257, 2583, 4475, 11, 257, 4669, 36250, 11, 436, 393, 3736, 24825, 7696, 819, 7787, 295, 3494, 322, 264, 1900, 912, 14217, 10067, 4166, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07897914006159856, "compression_ratio": 1.48, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211941507472295e-12}, {"id": 532, "seek": 201826, "start": 2029.8799999999999, "end": 2030.1, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50946, 1079, 13, 50957], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07897914006159856, "compression_ratio": 1.48, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211941507472295e-12}, {"id": 533, "seek": 201826, "start": 2030.3799999999999, "end": 2034.2, "text": " And the protocol treats this as a core intended feature, not a bug.", "tokens": [50971, 400, 264, 10336, 19566, 341, 382, 257, 4965, 10226, 4111, 11, 406, 257, 7426, 13, 51162], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07897914006159856, "compression_ratio": 1.48, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211941507472295e-12}, {"id": 534, "seek": 201826, "start": 2034.28, "end": 2034.92, "text": " That's brilliant.", "tokens": [51166, 663, 311, 10248, 13, 51198], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07897914006159856, "compression_ratio": 1.48, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211941507472295e-12}, {"id": 535, "seek": 203492, "start": 2034.92, "end": 2039.42, "text": " The manifest simply holds the objective, immutable history of who signed what and how.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 10067, 2935, 9190, 264, 10024, 11, 3397, 32148, 2503, 295, 567, 8175, 437, 293, 577, 13, 50590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08784210031682795, "compression_ratio": 1.5454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782118671480271e-12}, {"id": 536, "seek": 203492, "start": 2039.92, "end": 2047.9, "text": " The reader's software applies their chosen institution's policy layer to that manifest to determine what lights up green, what lights up yellow, and what lights up red.", "tokens": [50615, 440, 15149, 311, 4722, 13165, 641, 8614, 7818, 311, 3897, 4583, 281, 300, 10067, 281, 6997, 437, 5811, 493, 3092, 11, 437, 5811, 493, 5566, 11, 293, 437, 5811, 493, 2182, 13, 51014], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08784210031682795, "compression_ratio": 1.5454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782118671480271e-12}, {"id": 537, "seek": 204790, "start": 2047.9, "end": 2052.82, "text": " So it exposes trust assumptions as explicit, comparable objects.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 309, 1278, 4201, 3361, 17695, 382, 13691, 11, 25323, 6565, 13, 50611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1265157887965073, "compression_ratio": 1.4649122807017543, "no_speech_prob": 1.4490879199705042e-12}, {"id": 538, "seek": 204790, "start": 2052.94, "end": 2058.94, "text": " Rather than hiding them behind a universal, opaque, verified badge controlled by a single tech monopoly.", "tokens": [50617, 16571, 813, 10596, 552, 2261, 257, 11455, 11, 42687, 11, 31197, 25797, 10164, 538, 257, 2167, 7553, 37061, 13, 50917], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1265157887965073, "compression_ratio": 1.4649122807017543, "no_speech_prob": 1.4490879199705042e-12}, {"id": 539, "seek": 204790, "start": 2059.1600000000003, "end": 2061.46, "text": " Okay, so we've got the trust delegation sorted out.", "tokens": [50928, 1033, 11, 370, 321, 600, 658, 264, 3361, 36602, 25462, 484, 13, 51043], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1265157887965073, "compression_ratio": 1.4649122807017543, "no_speech_prob": 1.4490879199705042e-12}, {"id": 540, "seek": 204790, "start": 2061.6, "end": 2065.02, "text": " But documents aren't just isolated, floating sentences, right?", "tokens": [51050, 583, 8512, 3212, 380, 445, 14621, 11, 12607, 16579, 11, 558, 30, 51221], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1265157887965073, "compression_ratio": 1.4649122807017543, "no_speech_prob": 1.4490879199705042e-12}, {"id": 541, "seek": 204790, "start": 2065.7200000000003, "end": 2067.42, "text": " Claims build on other claims.", "tokens": [51256, 383, 10970, 82, 1322, 322, 661, 9441, 13, 51341], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1265157887965073, "compression_ratio": 1.4649122807017543, "no_speech_prob": 1.4490879199705042e-12}, {"id": 542, "seek": 204790, "start": 2067.6800000000003, "end": 2068.7400000000002, "text": " They absolutely do.", "tokens": [51354, 814, 3122, 360, 13, 51407], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1265157887965073, "compression_ratio": 1.4649122807017543, "no_speech_prob": 1.4490879199705042e-12}, {"id": 543, "seek": 206874, "start": 2068.74, "end": 2077.74, "text": " If claim C relies on claim B and claim B relies on claim A, what happens if claim A turns out to be mathematically false?", "tokens": [50365, 759, 3932, 383, 30910, 322, 3932, 363, 293, 3932, 363, 30910, 322, 3932, 316, 11, 437, 2314, 498, 3932, 316, 4523, 484, 281, 312, 44003, 7908, 30, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14051775204933295, "compression_ratio": 1.6180555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759271479956707e-12}, {"id": 544, "seek": 206874, "start": 2077.8599999999997, "end": 2078.7, "text": " It creates a cascade.", "tokens": [50821, 467, 7829, 257, 50080, 13, 50863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14051775204933295, "compression_ratio": 1.6180555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759271479956707e-12}, {"id": 545, "seek": 206874, "start": 2079.12, "end": 2079.3999999999996, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50884, 1779, 13, 50898], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14051775204933295, "compression_ratio": 1.6180555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759271479956707e-12}, {"id": 546, "seek": 206874, "start": 2079.72, "end": 2081.7999999999997, "text": " How many other claims go down with the ship?", "tokens": [50914, 1012, 867, 661, 9441, 352, 760, 365, 264, 5374, 30, 51018], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14051775204933295, "compression_ratio": 1.6180555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759271479956707e-12}, {"id": 547, "seek": 206874, "start": 2082.3599999999997, "end": 2089.7799999999997, "text": " If an AI summarizes a 50-page document and gets one foundational fact wrong, does the whole document lose verification?", "tokens": [51046, 759, 364, 7318, 14611, 5660, 257, 2625, 12, 15161, 4166, 293, 2170, 472, 32195, 1186, 2085, 11, 775, 264, 1379, 4166, 3624, 30206, 30, 51417], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14051775204933295, "compression_ratio": 1.6180555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759271479956707e-12}, {"id": 548, "seek": 206874, "start": 2090.4199999999996, "end": 2092.4399999999996, "text": " This is the domain of the dependency graph.", "tokens": [51449, 639, 307, 264, 9274, 295, 264, 33621, 4295, 13, 51550], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14051775204933295, "compression_ratio": 1.6180555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759271479956707e-12}, {"id": 549, "seek": 206874, "start": 2092.5, "end": 2092.72, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51553, 1033, 13, 51564], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14051775204933295, "compression_ratio": 1.6180555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759271479956707e-12}, {"id": 550, "seek": 206874, "start": 2092.72, "end": 2098.3999999999996, "text": " In version 1 of Flixie's protocol design, they track dependencies using what they called flat edges.", "tokens": [51564, 682, 3037, 502, 295, 3235, 970, 414, 311, 10336, 1715, 11, 436, 2837, 36606, 1228, 437, 436, 1219, 4962, 8819, 13, 51848], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14051775204933295, "compression_ratio": 1.6180555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759271479956707e-12}, {"id": 551, "seek": 209840, "start": 2098.4, "end": 2099.1600000000003, "text": " Flat edges.", "tokens": [50365, 36172, 8819, 13, 50403], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13624666504940744, "compression_ratio": 1.6006944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.325122516397271e-12}, {"id": 552, "seek": 209840, "start": 2099.34, "end": 2101.78, "text": " Basically, the system just made a simple binary note.", "tokens": [50412, 8537, 11, 264, 1185, 445, 1027, 257, 2199, 17434, 3637, 13, 50534], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13624666504940744, "compression_ratio": 1.6006944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.325122516397271e-12}, {"id": 553, "seek": 209840, "start": 2102.1, "end": 2103.9, "text": " Claim 15 depends on claim 7.", "tokens": [50550, 383, 10970, 2119, 5946, 322, 3932, 1614, 13, 50640], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13624666504940744, "compression_ratio": 1.6006944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.325122516397271e-12}, {"id": 554, "seek": 209840, "start": 2104.06, "end": 2104.42, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50648, 7587, 13, 50666], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13624666504940744, "compression_ratio": 1.6006944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.325122516397271e-12}, {"id": 555, "seek": 209840, "start": 2104.6, "end": 2105.64, "text": " That makes intuitive sense.", "tokens": [50675, 663, 1669, 21769, 2020, 13, 50727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13624666504940744, "compression_ratio": 1.6006944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.325122516397271e-12}, {"id": 556, "seek": 209840, "start": 2105.7400000000002, "end": 2106.92, "text": " It's a simple chain link.", "tokens": [50732, 467, 311, 257, 2199, 5021, 2113, 13, 50791], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13624666504940744, "compression_ratio": 1.6006944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.325122516397271e-12}, {"id": 557, "seek": 209840, "start": 2107.1800000000003, "end": 2112.1600000000003, "text": " It makes sense intuitively, but when they actually ran empirical testing, which we'll get into when we look at paper 3,", "tokens": [50804, 467, 1669, 2020, 46506, 11, 457, 562, 436, 767, 5872, 31886, 4997, 11, 597, 321, 603, 483, 666, 562, 321, 574, 412, 3035, 805, 11, 51053], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13624666504940744, "compression_ratio": 1.6006944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.325122516397271e-12}, {"id": 558, "seek": 209840, "start": 2112.52, "end": 2115.2400000000002, "text": " flat edges completely catastrophically failed.", "tokens": [51071, 4962, 8819, 2584, 28363, 984, 7612, 13, 51207], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13624666504940744, "compression_ratio": 1.6006944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.325122516397271e-12}, {"id": 559, "seek": 209840, "start": 2115.38, "end": 2115.6, "text": " Really?", "tokens": [51214, 4083, 30, 51225], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13624666504940744, "compression_ratio": 1.6006944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.325122516397271e-12}, {"id": 560, "seek": 209840, "start": 2115.8, "end": 2122.06, "text": " They led to massive false predictions and cascading verification failures that weren't actually real.", "tokens": [51235, 814, 4684, 281, 5994, 7908, 21264, 293, 3058, 66, 8166, 30206, 20774, 300, 4999, 380, 767, 957, 13, 51548], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13624666504940744, "compression_ratio": 1.6006944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.325122516397271e-12}, {"id": 561, "seek": 209840, "start": 2122.14, "end": 2123.3, "text": " But why would that happen?", "tokens": [51552, 583, 983, 576, 300, 1051, 30, 51610], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13624666504940744, "compression_ratio": 1.6006944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.325122516397271e-12}, {"id": 562, "seek": 212330, "start": 2123.3, "end": 2128.94, "text": " Because saying depends on conflates entirely different types of logical relationships.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 1566, 5946, 322, 1497, 75, 1024, 7696, 819, 3467, 295, 14978, 6159, 13, 50647], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16359573602676392, "compression_ratio": 1.5913043478260869, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007647460515196e-12}, {"id": 563, "seek": 212330, "start": 2129.78, "end": 2134.6400000000003, "text": " So, version 2 of the protocol introduces typed dependency edges.", "tokens": [50689, 407, 11, 3037, 568, 295, 264, 10336, 31472, 33941, 33621, 8819, 13, 50932], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16359573602676392, "compression_ratio": 1.5913043478260869, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007647460515196e-12}, {"id": 564, "seek": 212330, "start": 2134.98, "end": 2136.38, "text": " Typed dependency edges.", "tokens": [50949, 5569, 3452, 33621, 8819, 13, 51019], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16359573602676392, "compression_ratio": 1.5913043478260869, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007647460515196e-12}, {"id": 565, "seek": 212330, "start": 2136.42, "end": 2137.1000000000004, "text": " There are three types.", "tokens": [51021, 821, 366, 1045, 3467, 13, 51055], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16359573602676392, "compression_ratio": 1.5913043478260869, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007647460515196e-12}, {"id": 566, "seek": 212330, "start": 2137.5, "end": 2139.6600000000003, "text": " Semantic, interface, and proof term.", "tokens": [51075, 14421, 7128, 11, 9226, 11, 293, 8177, 1433, 13, 51183], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16359573602676392, "compression_ratio": 1.5913043478260869, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007647460515196e-12}, {"id": 567, "seek": 212330, "start": 2139.82, "end": 2140.78, "text": " Okay, let's break these down.", "tokens": [51191, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 1821, 613, 760, 13, 51239], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16359573602676392, "compression_ratio": 1.5913043478260869, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007647460515196e-12}, {"id": 568, "seek": 212330, "start": 2140.84, "end": 2143.6000000000004, "text": " Let me use a car building analogy to see if I have the mechanics of this right.", "tokens": [51242, 961, 385, 764, 257, 1032, 2390, 21663, 281, 536, 498, 286, 362, 264, 12939, 295, 341, 558, 13, 51380], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16359573602676392, "compression_ratio": 1.5913043478260869, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007647460515196e-12}, {"id": 569, "seek": 212330, "start": 2143.6800000000003, "end": 2144.38, "text": " Okay, let's hear it.", "tokens": [51384, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 1568, 309, 13, 51419], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16359573602676392, "compression_ratio": 1.5913043478260869, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007647460515196e-12}, {"id": 570, "seek": 214438, "start": 2144.38, "end": 2148.5, "text": " Let's say claim 15 is our fully assembled working car.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 311, 584, 3932, 2119, 307, 527, 4498, 24204, 1364, 1032, 13, 50571], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1743901102166427, "compression_ratio": 1.7118644067796611, "no_speech_prob": 1.853389186914911e-12}, {"id": 571, "seek": 214438, "start": 2149.1400000000003, "end": 2155.12, "text": " A semantic dependency means changing the underlying claim changes the actual truth or validity of the final claim.", "tokens": [50603, 316, 47982, 33621, 1355, 4473, 264, 14217, 3932, 2962, 264, 3539, 3494, 420, 40943, 295, 264, 2572, 3932, 13, 50902], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1743901102166427, "compression_ratio": 1.7118644067796611, "no_speech_prob": 1.853389186914911e-12}, {"id": 572, "seek": 214438, "start": 2155.38, "end": 2155.6, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50915, 1779, 13, 50926], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1743901102166427, "compression_ratio": 1.7118644067796611, "no_speech_prob": 1.853389186914911e-12}, {"id": 573, "seek": 214438, "start": 2155.92, "end": 2158.3, "text": " So, the semantic dependency is the engine schematic.", "tokens": [50942, 407, 11, 264, 47982, 33621, 307, 264, 2848, 44739, 13, 51061], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1743901102166427, "compression_ratio": 1.7118644067796611, "no_speech_prob": 1.853389186914911e-12}, {"id": 574, "seek": 214438, "start": 2158.7200000000003, "end": 2165.4, "text": " If the original schematic says the engine needs four cylinders and someone comes along and mutates that claim to say it only needs two cylinders,", "tokens": [51082, 759, 264, 3380, 44739, 1619, 264, 2848, 2203, 1451, 42166, 293, 1580, 1487, 2051, 293, 5839, 1024, 300, 3932, 281, 584, 309, 787, 2203, 732, 42166, 11, 51416], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1743901102166427, "compression_ratio": 1.7118644067796611, "no_speech_prob": 1.853389186914911e-12}, {"id": 575, "seek": 214438, "start": 2166.2200000000003, "end": 2167.1800000000003, "text": " the car won't run.", "tokens": [51457, 264, 1032, 1582, 380, 1190, 13, 51505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1743901102166427, "compression_ratio": 1.7118644067796611, "no_speech_prob": 1.853389186914911e-12}, {"id": 576, "seek": 214438, "start": 2167.4, "end": 2167.9, "text": " It fails.", "tokens": [51516, 467, 18199, 13, 51541], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1743901102166427, "compression_ratio": 1.7118644067796611, "no_speech_prob": 1.853389186914911e-12}, {"id": 577, "seek": 216790, "start": 2167.9, "end": 2173.28, "text": " The truth of the car depends entirely, fundamentally, on the semantic truth of the schematic.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3494, 295, 264, 1032, 5946, 7696, 11, 17879, 11, 322, 264, 47982, 3494, 295, 264, 44739, 13, 50634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15556960203209702, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.460976305212025e-12}, {"id": 578, "seek": 216790, "start": 2173.54, "end": 2173.84, "text": " Perfect.", "tokens": [50647, 10246, 13, 50662], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15556960203209702, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.460976305212025e-12}, {"id": 579, "seek": 216790, "start": 2174.04, "end": 2175.2400000000002, "text": " That is a semantic dependency.", "tokens": [50672, 663, 307, 257, 47982, 33621, 13, 50732], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15556960203209702, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.460976305212025e-12}, {"id": 580, "seek": 216790, "start": 2175.7000000000003, "end": 2177.54, "text": " It is load-bearing for the actual meaning.", "tokens": [50755, 467, 307, 3677, 12, 650, 1921, 337, 264, 3539, 3620, 13, 50847], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15556960203209702, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.460976305212025e-12}, {"id": 581, "seek": 216790, "start": 2178.3, "end": 2182.64, "text": " If the semantic dependency fails, the claim above it logically collapses.", "tokens": [50885, 759, 264, 47982, 33621, 18199, 11, 264, 3932, 3673, 309, 38887, 48765, 13, 51102], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15556960203209702, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.460976305212025e-12}, {"id": 582, "seek": 216790, "start": 2183.02, "end": 2185.0, "text": " Okay, so what's an interface dependency?", "tokens": [51121, 1033, 11, 370, 437, 311, 364, 9226, 33621, 30, 51220], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15556960203209702, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.460976305212025e-12}, {"id": 583, "seek": 216790, "start": 2185.9, "end": 2195.52, "text": " The paper defines this as when constructing the justification requires the signature of the other claim without depending on its internal justification.", "tokens": [51265, 440, 3035, 23122, 341, 382, 562, 39969, 264, 31591, 7029, 264, 13397, 295, 264, 661, 3932, 1553, 5413, 322, 1080, 6920, 31591, 13, 51746], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15556960203209702, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.460976305212025e-12}, {"id": 584, "seek": 219552, "start": 2195.52, "end": 2203.58, "text": " Okay, so an interface dependency is like the specific physical shape of the bolts connecting the engine to the chassis.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 370, 364, 9226, 33621, 307, 411, 264, 2685, 4001, 3909, 295, 264, 18127, 11015, 264, 2848, 281, 264, 28262, 13, 50768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11987614322018314, "compression_ratio": 1.6536585365853658, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170643363377373e-12}, {"id": 585, "seek": 219552, "start": 2203.9, "end": 2204.02, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50784, 1779, 13, 50790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11987614322018314, "compression_ratio": 1.6536585365853658, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170643363377373e-12}, {"id": 586, "seek": 219552, "start": 2204.32, "end": 2215.2, "text": " I need a specific bolt shape to connect the pieces together, but the car's overall speed and performance doesn't depend on the metallurgical purity of the bolt's internal structure.", "tokens": [50805, 286, 643, 257, 2685, 13436, 3909, 281, 1745, 264, 3755, 1214, 11, 457, 264, 1032, 311, 4787, 3073, 293, 3389, 1177, 380, 5672, 322, 264, 20866, 46736, 34382, 295, 264, 13436, 311, 6920, 3877, 13, 51349], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11987614322018314, "compression_ratio": 1.6536585365853658, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170643363377373e-12}, {"id": 587, "seek": 219552, "start": 2215.46, "end": 2216.92, "text": " It just needs to fit the slot.", "tokens": [51362, 467, 445, 2203, 281, 3318, 264, 14747, 13, 51435], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11987614322018314, "compression_ratio": 1.6536585365853658, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170643363377373e-12}, {"id": 588, "seek": 221692, "start": 2216.92, "end": 2217.56, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50397], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10851825532459078, "compression_ratio": 1.7188612099644127, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884353736171029e-12}, {"id": 589, "seek": 221692, "start": 2217.76, "end": 2225.84, "text": " It's a structural syntactic requirement to connect the logical pieces in the software, but the semantic truth isn't drawn from its internal proof.", "tokens": [50407, 467, 311, 257, 15067, 23980, 19892, 11695, 281, 1745, 264, 14978, 3755, 294, 264, 4722, 11, 457, 264, 47982, 3494, 1943, 380, 10117, 490, 1080, 6920, 8177, 13, 50811], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10851825532459078, "compression_ratio": 1.7188612099644127, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884353736171029e-12}, {"id": 590, "seek": 221692, "start": 2225.98, "end": 2226.16, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50818, 1033, 13, 50827], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10851825532459078, "compression_ratio": 1.7188612099644127, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884353736171029e-12}, {"id": 591, "seek": 221692, "start": 2226.4, "end": 2228.6800000000003, "text": " And the third, the proof-term dependency.", "tokens": [50839, 400, 264, 2636, 11, 264, 8177, 12, 7039, 33621, 13, 50953], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10851825532459078, "compression_ratio": 1.7188612099644127, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884353736171029e-12}, {"id": 592, "seek": 221692, "start": 2229.2000000000003, "end": 2237.6800000000003, "text": " The paper says this is when a specific certified justification happens to reference another claim, independent of whether the underlying statement even mentions it.", "tokens": [50979, 440, 3035, 1619, 341, 307, 562, 257, 2685, 18580, 31591, 2314, 281, 6408, 1071, 3932, 11, 6695, 295, 1968, 264, 14217, 5629, 754, 23844, 309, 13, 51403], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10851825532459078, "compression_ratio": 1.7188612099644127, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884353736171029e-12}, {"id": 593, "seek": 221692, "start": 2237.8, "end": 2243.34, "text": " So the proof-term dependency is the specific brand of wrench the mechanic used to tighten the bolts on the engine.", "tokens": [51409, 407, 264, 8177, 12, 7039, 33621, 307, 264, 2685, 3360, 295, 25406, 264, 23860, 1143, 281, 17041, 264, 18127, 322, 264, 2848, 13, 51686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10851825532459078, "compression_ratio": 1.7188612099644127, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884353736171029e-12}, {"id": 594, "seek": 224334, "start": 2243.34, "end": 2250.6000000000004, "text": " And taking your car building analogy a step further, the system doesn't just record the wrench, it records exactly how the wrench was used.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 1940, 428, 1032, 2390, 21663, 257, 1823, 3052, 11, 264, 1185, 1177, 380, 445, 2136, 264, 25406, 11, 309, 7724, 2293, 577, 264, 25406, 390, 1143, 13, 50728], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10216466522216797, "compression_ratio": 1.7737704918032786, "no_speech_prob": 1.579119430702991e-12}, {"id": 595, "seek": 224334, "start": 2250.82, "end": 2251.3, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50739, 1779, 13, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10216466522216797, "compression_ratio": 1.7737704918032786, "no_speech_prob": 1.579119430702991e-12}, {"id": 596, "seek": 224334, "start": 2251.44, "end": 2259.7000000000003, "text": " So if the company that made the wrench issues a massive recall because the wrenches are defective, the mechanic's specific wrench is technically invalidated.", "tokens": [50770, 407, 498, 264, 2237, 300, 1027, 264, 25406, 2663, 257, 5994, 9901, 570, 264, 261, 1095, 3781, 366, 16445, 488, 11, 264, 23860, 311, 2685, 25406, 307, 12120, 34702, 770, 13, 51183], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10216466522216797, "compression_ratio": 1.7737704918032786, "no_speech_prob": 1.579119430702991e-12}, {"id": 597, "seek": 224334, "start": 2259.7400000000002, "end": 2260.04, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51185, 1079, 13, 51200], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10216466522216797, "compression_ratio": 1.7737704918032786, "no_speech_prob": 1.579119430702991e-12}, {"id": 598, "seek": 224334, "start": 2260.2200000000003, "end": 2262.4, "text": " But the car's engine is still perfectly fine.", "tokens": [51209, 583, 264, 1032, 311, 2848, 307, 920, 6239, 2489, 13, 51318], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10216466522216797, "compression_ratio": 1.7737704918032786, "no_speech_prob": 1.579119430702991e-12}, {"id": 599, "seek": 224334, "start": 2262.6400000000003, "end": 2267.56, "text": " The car doesn't break down on the highway just because the wrench used to build it was recalled months later.", "tokens": [51330, 440, 1032, 1177, 380, 1821, 760, 322, 264, 17205, 445, 570, 264, 25406, 1143, 281, 1322, 309, 390, 39301, 2493, 1780, 13, 51576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10216466522216797, "compression_ratio": 1.7737704918032786, "no_speech_prob": 1.579119430702991e-12}, {"id": 600, "seek": 224334, "start": 2267.6800000000003, "end": 2271.7400000000002, "text": " And that is exactly why typed edges are so revolutionary for this protocol.", "tokens": [51582, 400, 300, 307, 2293, 983, 33941, 8819, 366, 370, 22687, 337, 341, 10336, 13, 51785], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10216466522216797, "compression_ratio": 1.7737704918032786, "no_speech_prob": 1.579119430702991e-12}, {"id": 601, "seek": 227174, "start": 2271.74, "end": 2285.68, "text": " Before typed edges, if the wrench was recalled, the flat-edge system would look at the graph, see a simple link that says car depends on wrench, and flag the entire car, the entire document, as unverified.", "tokens": [50365, 4546, 33941, 8819, 11, 498, 264, 25406, 390, 39301, 11, 264, 4962, 12, 12203, 1185, 576, 574, 412, 264, 4295, 11, 536, 257, 2199, 2113, 300, 1619, 1032, 5946, 322, 25406, 11, 293, 7166, 264, 2302, 1032, 11, 264, 2302, 4166, 11, 382, 517, 331, 2587, 13, 51062], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09097077369689942, "compression_ratio": 1.640495867768595, "no_speech_prob": 1.7082113718328018e-12}, {"id": 602, "seek": 227174, "start": 2285.7999999999997, "end": 2287.06, "text": " It overcounted the damage.", "tokens": [51068, 467, 670, 26050, 292, 264, 4344, 13, 51131], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09097077369689942, "compression_ratio": 1.640495867768595, "no_speech_prob": 1.7082113718328018e-12}, {"id": 603, "seek": 227174, "start": 2287.24, "end": 2287.7999999999997, "text": " Massively.", "tokens": [51140, 10482, 3413, 13, 51168], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09097077369689942, "compression_ratio": 1.640495867768595, "no_speech_prob": 1.7082113718328018e-12}, {"id": 604, "seek": 227174, "start": 2287.9199999999996, "end": 2292.1, "text": " It would revoke verification for thousands of claims that were actually totally fine.", "tokens": [51174, 467, 576, 3698, 2949, 30206, 337, 5383, 295, 9441, 300, 645, 767, 3879, 2489, 13, 51383], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09097077369689942, "compression_ratio": 1.640495867768595, "no_speech_prob": 1.7082113718328018e-12}, {"id": 605, "seek": 227174, "start": 2292.3799999999997, "end": 2294.68, "text": " Imagine what that does to a scientific database.", "tokens": [51397, 11739, 437, 300, 775, 281, 257, 8134, 8149, 13, 51512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09097077369689942, "compression_ratio": 1.640495867768595, "no_speech_prob": 1.7082113718328018e-12}, {"id": 606, "seek": 227174, "start": 2294.8199999999997, "end": 2295.58, "text": " It would be chaos.", "tokens": [51519, 467, 576, 312, 14158, 13, 51557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09097077369689942, "compression_ratio": 1.640495867768595, "no_speech_prob": 1.7082113718328018e-12}, {"id": 607, "seek": 229558, "start": 2295.58, "end": 2303.58, "text": " One foundational paper gets a minor retraction on a proof method, and suddenly 10,000 downstream papers lose their verification status instantly.", "tokens": [50365, 1485, 32195, 3035, 2170, 257, 6696, 1533, 26766, 322, 257, 8177, 3170, 11, 293, 5800, 1266, 11, 1360, 30621, 10577, 3624, 641, 30206, 6558, 13518, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10713128610090776, "compression_ratio": 1.575875486381323, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810483548737823e-12}, {"id": 608, "seek": 229558, "start": 2304.54, "end": 2307.02, "text": " It would bring the speed of science to a grinding halt.", "tokens": [50813, 467, 576, 1565, 264, 3073, 295, 3497, 281, 257, 25300, 12479, 13, 50937], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10713128610090776, "compression_ratio": 1.575875486381323, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810483548737823e-12}, {"id": 609, "seek": 229558, "start": 2307.7799999999997, "end": 2317.94, "text": " If we connect this to the bigger picture, the paper gives a brilliant scenario, example two, to illustrate how policy-qualified queries use these typed edges to prevent that.", "tokens": [50975, 759, 321, 1745, 341, 281, 264, 3801, 3036, 11, 264, 3035, 2709, 257, 10248, 9005, 11, 1365, 732, 11, 281, 23221, 577, 3897, 12, 46094, 24109, 764, 613, 33941, 8819, 281, 4871, 300, 13, 51483], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10713128610090776, "compression_ratio": 1.575875486381323, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810483548737823e-12}, {"id": 610, "seek": 229558, "start": 2318.06, "end": 2319.64, "text": " Walk me through example two.", "tokens": [51489, 10818, 385, 807, 1365, 732, 13, 51568], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10713128610090776, "compression_ratio": 1.575875486381323, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810483548737823e-12}, {"id": 611, "seek": 231964, "start": 2319.64, "end": 2322.58, "text": " Imagine an intermediate mathematical proof.", "tokens": [50365, 11739, 364, 19376, 18894, 8177, 13, 50512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17200054945769133, "compression_ratio": 1.6477732793522266, "no_speech_prob": 1.432514480301239e-12}, {"id": 612, "seek": 231964, "start": 2322.68, "end": 2323.74, "text": " Let's call it Claim 7.", "tokens": [50517, 961, 311, 818, 309, 383, 10970, 1614, 13, 50570], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17200054945769133, "compression_ratio": 1.6477732793522266, "no_speech_prob": 1.432514480301239e-12}, {"id": 613, "seek": 231964, "start": 2324.18, "end": 2331.3599999999997, "text": " Let's say Claim 7's formal verification is revoked because someone found a flaw in the specific proof term used.", "tokens": [50592, 961, 311, 584, 383, 10970, 1614, 311, 9860, 30206, 307, 3698, 9511, 570, 1580, 1352, 257, 13717, 294, 264, 2685, 8177, 1433, 1143, 13, 50951], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17200054945769133, "compression_ratio": 1.6477732793522266, "no_speech_prob": 1.432514480301239e-12}, {"id": 614, "seek": 231964, "start": 2331.62, "end": 2333.1, "text": " The wrench was recalled.", "tokens": [50964, 440, 25406, 390, 39301, 13, 51038], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17200054945769133, "compression_ratio": 1.6477732793522266, "no_speech_prob": 1.432514480301239e-12}, {"id": 615, "seek": 231964, "start": 2333.48, "end": 2333.8799999999997, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51057, 7587, 13, 51077], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17200054945769133, "compression_ratio": 1.6477732793522266, "no_speech_prob": 1.432514480301239e-12}, {"id": 616, "seek": 231964, "start": 2334.42, "end": 2335.58, "text": " The system runs a query.", "tokens": [51104, 440, 1185, 6676, 257, 14581, 13, 51162], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17200054945769133, "compression_ratio": 1.6477732793522266, "no_speech_prob": 1.432514480301239e-12}, {"id": 617, "seek": 231964, "start": 2336.2599999999998, "end": 2342.06, "text": " It looks at the massive closure of claims that depend on Claim 7, but it only looks along the semantic edges.", "tokens": [51196, 467, 1542, 412, 264, 5994, 24653, 295, 9441, 300, 5672, 322, 383, 10970, 1614, 11, 457, 309, 787, 1542, 2051, 264, 47982, 8819, 13, 51486], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17200054945769133, "compression_ratio": 1.6477732793522266, "no_speech_prob": 1.432514480301239e-12}, {"id": 618, "seek": 231964, "start": 2342.22, "end": 2344.54, "text": " It only looks for the engine schematics, not the wrenches.", "tokens": [51494, 467, 787, 1542, 337, 264, 2848, 956, 37541, 11, 406, 264, 261, 1095, 3781, 13, 51610], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17200054945769133, "compression_ratio": 1.6477732793522266, "no_speech_prob": 1.432514480301239e-12}, {"id": 619, "seek": 234454, "start": 2344.54, "end": 2345.1, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50393], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11685866879341297, "compression_ratio": 1.5943396226415094, "no_speech_prob": 1.782761546893774e-12}, {"id": 620, "seek": 234454, "start": 2345.24, "end": 2351.62, "text": " So the system queries the graph and sees that Claims 15, 18, and 22 depend on Claim 7 semantically.", "tokens": [50400, 407, 264, 1185, 24109, 264, 4295, 293, 8194, 300, 383, 10970, 82, 2119, 11, 2443, 11, 293, 5853, 5672, 322, 383, 10970, 1614, 4361, 49505, 13, 50719], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11685866879341297, "compression_ratio": 1.5943396226415094, "no_speech_prob": 1.782761546893774e-12}, {"id": 621, "seek": 234454, "start": 2352.58, "end": 2357.24, "text": " Therefore, those three specific claims instantly lose their verified status.", "tokens": [50767, 7504, 11, 729, 1045, 2685, 9441, 13518, 3624, 641, 31197, 6558, 13, 51000], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11685866879341297, "compression_ratio": 1.5943396226415094, "no_speech_prob": 1.782761546893774e-12}, {"id": 622, "seek": 234454, "start": 2357.4, "end": 2358.72, "text": " The blast radius is contained.", "tokens": [51008, 440, 12035, 15845, 307, 16212, 13, 51074], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11685866879341297, "compression_ratio": 1.5943396226415094, "no_speech_prob": 1.782761546893774e-12}, {"id": 623, "seek": 234454, "start": 2358.94, "end": 2359.2599999999998, "text": " Completely.", "tokens": [51085, 39978, 13, 51101], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11685866879341297, "compression_ratio": 1.5943396226415094, "no_speech_prob": 1.782761546893774e-12}, {"id": 624, "seek": 234454, "start": 2359.64, "end": 2366.12, "text": " But any claim, let's say Claim 50, that only depended on Claim 7 via an interface or proof term edge is safely untouched.", "tokens": [51120, 583, 604, 3932, 11, 718, 311, 584, 383, 10970, 2625, 11, 300, 787, 1367, 3502, 322, 383, 10970, 1614, 5766, 364, 9226, 420, 8177, 1433, 4691, 307, 11750, 1701, 36740, 13, 51444], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11685866879341297, "compression_ratio": 1.5943396226415094, "no_speech_prob": 1.782761546893774e-12}, {"id": 625, "seek": 234454, "start": 2366.38, "end": 2368.06, "text": " The revocation is surgically precise.", "tokens": [51457, 440, 3698, 27943, 307, 19560, 984, 13600, 13, 51541], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11685866879341297, "compression_ratio": 1.5943396226415094, "no_speech_prob": 1.782761546893774e-12}, {"id": 626, "seek": 234454, "start": 2368.36, "end": 2368.62, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51556, 7587, 13, 51569], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11685866879341297, "compression_ratio": 1.5943396226415094, "no_speech_prob": 1.782761546893774e-12}, {"id": 627, "seek": 234454, "start": 2368.72, "end": 2374.06, "text": " You don't have to throw out an entire 50-page document just because one auxiliary lemma used a recalled wrench.", "tokens": [51574, 509, 500, 380, 362, 281, 3507, 484, 364, 2302, 2625, 12, 15161, 4166, 445, 570, 472, 43741, 7495, 1696, 1143, 257, 39301, 25406, 13, 51841], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11685866879341297, "compression_ratio": 1.5943396226415094, "no_speech_prob": 1.782761546893774e-12}, {"id": 628, "seek": 237406, "start": 2374.06, "end": 2375.5, "text": " That is so elegant.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 370, 21117, 13, 50437], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13356163745790017, "compression_ratio": 1.6246153846153846, "no_speech_prob": 1.9201086033648895e-12}, {"id": 629, "seek": 237406, "start": 2375.74, "end": 2381.12, "text": " It perfectly balances rigorous truth checking with the practical reality that systems need to be resilient.", "tokens": [50449, 467, 6239, 33993, 29882, 3494, 8568, 365, 264, 8496, 4103, 300, 3652, 643, 281, 312, 23699, 13, 50718], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13356163745790017, "compression_ratio": 1.6246153846153846, "no_speech_prob": 1.9201086033648895e-12}, {"id": 630, "seek": 237406, "start": 2381.32, "end": 2381.96, "text": " It really does.", "tokens": [50728, 467, 534, 775, 13, 50760], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13356163745790017, "compression_ratio": 1.6246153846153846, "no_speech_prob": 1.9201086033648895e-12}, {"id": 631, "seek": 237406, "start": 2382.2599999999998, "end": 2384.34, "text": " But again, this is all theory on a whiteboard.", "tokens": [50775, 583, 797, 11, 341, 307, 439, 5261, 322, 257, 2418, 3787, 13, 50879], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13356163745790017, "compression_ratio": 1.6246153846153846, "no_speech_prob": 1.9201086033648895e-12}, {"id": 632, "seek": 237406, "start": 2385.2999999999997, "end": 2387.7999999999997, "text": " Did they actually test this to see if it works in the real world?", "tokens": [50927, 2589, 436, 767, 1500, 341, 281, 536, 498, 309, 1985, 294, 264, 957, 1002, 30, 51052], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13356163745790017, "compression_ratio": 1.6246153846153846, "no_speech_prob": 1.9201086033648895e-12}, {"id": 633, "seek": 237406, "start": 2388.02, "end": 2392.06, "text": " Or is this just a really beautiful mathematical thought experiment?", "tokens": [51063, 1610, 307, 341, 445, 257, 534, 2238, 18894, 1194, 5120, 30, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13356163745790017, "compression_ratio": 1.6246153846153846, "no_speech_prob": 1.9201086033648895e-12}, {"id": 634, "seek": 237406, "start": 2392.36, "end": 2397.04, "text": " This is where the deep dive gets incredibly practical and, frankly, kind of thrilling.", "tokens": [51280, 639, 307, 689, 264, 2452, 9192, 2170, 6252, 8496, 293, 11, 11939, 11, 733, 295, 39347, 13, 51514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13356163745790017, "compression_ratio": 1.6246153846153846, "no_speech_prob": 1.9201086033648895e-12}, {"id": 635, "seek": 237406, "start": 2397.34, "end": 2398.58, "text": " They absolutely tested it.", "tokens": [51529, 814, 3122, 8246, 309, 13, 51591], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13356163745790017, "compression_ratio": 1.6246153846153846, "no_speech_prob": 1.9201086033648895e-12}, {"id": 636, "seek": 237406, "start": 2398.66, "end": 2398.94, "text": " Awesome.", "tokens": [51595, 10391, 13, 51609], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13356163745790017, "compression_ratio": 1.6246153846153846, "no_speech_prob": 1.9201086033648895e-12}, {"id": 637, "seek": 237406, "start": 2399.16, "end": 2403.36, "text": " This brings us to Paper 3, which documents the Claim Shift repository on GitHub.", "tokens": [51620, 639, 5607, 505, 281, 24990, 805, 11, 597, 8512, 264, 383, 10970, 28304, 25841, 322, 23331, 13, 51830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13356163745790017, "compression_ratio": 1.6246153846153846, "no_speech_prob": 1.9201086033648895e-12}, {"id": 638, "seek": 240336, "start": 2403.36, "end": 2404.26, "text": " What did they do?", "tokens": [50365, 708, 630, 436, 360, 30, 50410], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15645758310953775, "compression_ratio": 1.5253456221198156, "no_speech_prob": 1.8601279370977775e-12}, {"id": 639, "seek": 240336, "start": 2404.48, "end": 2412.8, "text": " They built a pristine mathematical specimen and then systematically, viciously tried to break it using automated mutations.", "tokens": [50421, 814, 3094, 257, 582, 42745, 18894, 34204, 293, 550, 39531, 11, 30093, 356, 3031, 281, 1821, 309, 1228, 18473, 29243, 13, 50837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15645758310953775, "compression_ratio": 1.5253456221198156, "no_speech_prob": 1.8601279370977775e-12}, {"id": 640, "seek": 240336, "start": 2413.06, "end": 2413.6400000000003, "text": " I love this.", "tokens": [50850, 286, 959, 341, 13, 50879], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15645758310953775, "compression_ratio": 1.5253456221198156, "no_speech_prob": 1.8601279370977775e-12}, {"id": 641, "seek": 240336, "start": 2413.7000000000003, "end": 2414.46, "text": " Let's get into the code.", "tokens": [50882, 961, 311, 483, 666, 264, 3089, 13, 50920], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15645758310953775, "compression_ratio": 1.5253456221198156, "no_speech_prob": 1.8601279370977775e-12}, {"id": 642, "seek": 240336, "start": 2414.54, "end": 2416.48, "text": " What exactly did they build in this repository?", "tokens": [50924, 708, 2293, 630, 436, 1322, 294, 341, 25841, 30, 51021], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15645758310953775, "compression_ratio": 1.5253456221198156, "no_speech_prob": 1.8601279370977775e-12}, {"id": 643, "seek": 240336, "start": 2416.76, "end": 2424.58, "text": " They built a formal verification artifact using a highly respected proof assistant called Lean 4.9 0.0.", "tokens": [51035, 814, 3094, 257, 9860, 30206, 34806, 1228, 257, 5405, 20020, 8177, 10994, 1219, 49303, 1017, 13, 24, 1958, 13, 15, 13, 51426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15645758310953775, "compression_ratio": 1.5253456221198156, "no_speech_prob": 1.8601279370977775e-12}, {"id": 644, "seek": 242458, "start": 2424.58, "end": 2431.9, "text": " Specifically, they created a frozen mathematical specimen named admissibilitytransitionsystem.lean.", "tokens": [50365, 26058, 11, 436, 2942, 257, 12496, 18894, 34204, 4926, 5910, 891, 2841, 24999, 2451, 9321, 13, 28499, 13, 50731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1949713120766736, "compression_ratio": 1.568840579710145, "no_speech_prob": 1.825318542147958e-12}, {"id": 645, "seek": 242458, "start": 2432.2, "end": 2433.12, "text": " Why does it need to be frozen?", "tokens": [50746, 1545, 775, 309, 643, 281, 312, 12496, 30, 50792], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1949713120766736, "compression_ratio": 1.568840579710145, "no_speech_prob": 1.825318542147958e-12}, {"id": 646, "seek": 242458, "start": 2433.4, "end": 2438.4, "text": " Because in strict scientific testing, your control group has to be perfectly, unalterably stable.", "tokens": [50806, 1436, 294, 10910, 8134, 4997, 11, 428, 1969, 1594, 575, 281, 312, 6239, 11, 517, 43420, 1188, 8351, 13, 51056], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1949713120766736, "compression_ratio": 1.568840579710145, "no_speech_prob": 1.825318542147958e-12}, {"id": 647, "seek": 242458, "start": 2438.52, "end": 2438.74, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51062, 1033, 13, 51073], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1949713120766736, "compression_ratio": 1.568840579710145, "no_speech_prob": 1.825318542147958e-12}, {"id": 648, "seek": 242458, "start": 2438.86, "end": 2439.3199999999997, "text": " That makes sense.", "tokens": [51079, 663, 1669, 2020, 13, 51102], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1949713120766736, "compression_ratio": 1.568840579710145, "no_speech_prob": 1.825318542147958e-12}, {"id": 649, "seek": 242458, "start": 2439.48, "end": 2440.88, "text": " This specimen is beautifully minimal.", "tokens": [51110, 639, 34204, 307, 16525, 13206, 13, 51180], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1949713120766736, "compression_ratio": 1.568840579710145, "no_speech_prob": 1.825318542147958e-12}, {"id": 650, "seek": 242458, "start": 2441.12, "end": 2442.74, "text": " It has absolutely zero dependencies.", "tokens": [51192, 467, 575, 3122, 4018, 36606, 13, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1949713120766736, "compression_ratio": 1.568840579710145, "no_speech_prob": 1.825318542147958e-12}, {"id": 651, "seek": 242458, "start": 2443.2799999999997, "end": 2445.34, "text": " There is no external mathlib imported.", "tokens": [51300, 821, 307, 572, 8320, 5221, 38270, 25524, 13, 51403], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1949713120766736, "compression_ratio": 1.568840579710145, "no_speech_prob": 1.825318542147958e-12}, {"id": 652, "seek": 242458, "start": 2445.7799999999997, "end": 2447.96, "text": " It uses just pure Lean core code.", "tokens": [51425, 467, 4960, 445, 6075, 49303, 4965, 3089, 13, 51534], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1949713120766736, "compression_ratio": 1.568840579710145, "no_speech_prob": 1.825318542147958e-12}, {"id": 653, "seek": 242458, "start": 2448.14, "end": 2449.5, "text": " It is completely self-contained.", "tokens": [51543, 467, 307, 2584, 2698, 12, 9000, 3563, 13, 51611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1949713120766736, "compression_ratio": 1.568840579710145, "no_speech_prob": 1.825318542147958e-12}, {"id": 654, "seek": 244950, "start": 2449.5, "end": 2451.24, "text": " And what's the structure of it?", "tokens": [50365, 400, 437, 311, 264, 3877, 295, 309, 30, 50452], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14791659012581537, "compression_ratio": 1.5965665236051503, "no_speech_prob": 2.0429426379753313e-12}, {"id": 655, "seek": 244950, "start": 2451.5, "end": 2454.32, "text": " Logically, it's designed with an asymmetric dependency graph.", "tokens": [50465, 10824, 984, 11, 309, 311, 4761, 365, 364, 37277, 17475, 33621, 4295, 13, 50606], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14791659012581537, "compression_ratio": 1.5965665236051503, "no_speech_prob": 2.0429426379753313e-12}, {"id": 656, "seek": 244950, "start": 2455.24, "end": 2456.66, "text": " It looks a bit like a Y shape.", "tokens": [50652, 467, 1542, 257, 857, 411, 257, 398, 3909, 13, 50723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14791659012581537, "compression_ratio": 1.5965665236051503, "no_speech_prob": 2.0429426379753313e-12}, {"id": 657, "seek": 244950, "start": 2456.7, "end": 2457.58, "text": " A Y shape?", "tokens": [50725, 316, 398, 3909, 30, 50769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14791659012581537, "compression_ratio": 1.5965665236051503, "no_speech_prob": 2.0429426379753313e-12}, {"id": 658, "seek": 244950, "start": 2457.64, "end": 2457.82, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50772, 865, 13, 50781], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14791659012581537, "compression_ratio": 1.5965665236051503, "no_speech_prob": 2.0429426379753313e-12}, {"id": 659, "seek": 244950, "start": 2457.92, "end": 2463.02, "text": " It has two separate logical branches of proofs that happen to share one common dependency right", "tokens": [50786, 467, 575, 732, 4994, 14978, 14770, 295, 8177, 82, 300, 1051, 281, 2073, 472, 2689, 33621, 558, 51041], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14791659012581537, "compression_ratio": 1.5965665236051503, "no_speech_prob": 2.0429426379753313e-12}, {"id": 660, "seek": 244950, "start": 2463.02, "end": 2464.84, "text": " in the middle, which they call D2.", "tokens": [51041, 294, 264, 2808, 11, 597, 436, 818, 413, 17, 13, 51132], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14791659012581537, "compression_ratio": 1.5965665236051503, "no_speech_prob": 2.0429426379753313e-12}, {"id": 661, "seek": 244950, "start": 2465.02, "end": 2468.08, "text": " Why design it like a Y shape with a shared middle node?", "tokens": [51141, 1545, 1715, 309, 411, 257, 398, 3909, 365, 257, 5507, 2808, 9984, 30, 51294], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14791659012581537, "compression_ratio": 1.5965665236051503, "no_speech_prob": 2.0429426379753313e-12}, {"id": 662, "seek": 244950, "start": 2468.44, "end": 2471.04, "text": " To enable highly targeted mutation testing.", "tokens": [51312, 1407, 9528, 5405, 15045, 27960, 4997, 13, 51442], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14791659012581537, "compression_ratio": 1.5965665236051503, "no_speech_prob": 2.0429426379753313e-12}, {"id": 663, "seek": 247104, "start": 2471.04, "end": 2477.66, "text": " If you mutate that shared dependency, D2, you should theoretically see the failure propagate", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 5839, 473, 300, 5507, 33621, 11, 413, 17, 11, 291, 820, 29400, 536, 264, 7763, 48256, 50696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10649267832438152, "compression_ratio": 1.6644736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213558715420183e-12}, {"id": 664, "seek": 247104, "start": 2477.66, "end": 2479.34, "text": " down both branches of the Y.", "tokens": [50696, 760, 1293, 14770, 295, 264, 398, 13, 50780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10649267832438152, "compression_ratio": 1.6644736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213558715420183e-12}, {"id": 665, "seek": 247104, "start": 2479.5, "end": 2479.7599999999998, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50788, 1779, 13, 50801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10649267832438152, "compression_ratio": 1.6644736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213558715420183e-12}, {"id": 666, "seek": 247104, "start": 2479.94, "end": 2484.52, "text": " But if you mutate a node higher up on just one branch, the other branch should remain", "tokens": [50810, 583, 498, 291, 5839, 473, 257, 9984, 2946, 493, 322, 445, 472, 9819, 11, 264, 661, 9819, 820, 6222, 51039], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10649267832438152, "compression_ratio": 1.6644736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213558715420183e-12}, {"id": 667, "seek": 247104, "start": 2484.52, "end": 2487.2799999999997, "text": " perfectly verified and completely unaffected.", "tokens": [51039, 6239, 31197, 293, 2584, 2002, 11259, 292, 13, 51177], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10649267832438152, "compression_ratio": 1.6644736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213558715420183e-12}, {"id": 668, "seek": 247104, "start": 2487.34, "end": 2487.6, "text": " Ah.", "tokens": [51180, 2438, 13, 51193], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10649267832438152, "compression_ratio": 1.6644736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213558715420183e-12}, {"id": 669, "seek": 247104, "start": 2487.7599999999998, "end": 2491.98, "text": " It's a way to prove that the type dependency edges actually track the blast radius of a", "tokens": [51201, 467, 311, 257, 636, 281, 7081, 300, 264, 2010, 33621, 8819, 767, 2837, 264, 12035, 15845, 295, 257, 51412], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10649267832438152, "compression_ratio": 1.6644736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213558715420183e-12}, {"id": 670, "seek": 247104, "start": 2491.98, "end": 2493.7599999999998, "text": " failure correctly in real time.", "tokens": [51412, 7763, 8944, 294, 957, 565, 13, 51501], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10649267832438152, "compression_ratio": 1.6644736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213558715420183e-12}, {"id": 671, "seek": 247104, "start": 2493.88, "end": 2494.38, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51507, 7587, 13, 51532], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10649267832438152, "compression_ratio": 1.6644736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213558715420183e-12}, {"id": 672, "seek": 247104, "start": 2494.68, "end": 2494.92, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51547, 1033, 13, 51559], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10649267832438152, "compression_ratio": 1.6644736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213558715420183e-12}, {"id": 673, "seek": 247104, "start": 2495.06, "end": 2499.02, "text": " So they have this perfect, pristine mathematical crystal in the shape of a Y.", "tokens": [51566, 407, 436, 362, 341, 2176, 11, 582, 42745, 18894, 13662, 294, 264, 3909, 295, 257, 398, 13, 51764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10649267832438152, "compression_ratio": 1.6644736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213558715420183e-12}, {"id": 674, "seek": 247104, "start": 2499.16, "end": 2500.6, "text": " How do they try to break it?", "tokens": [51771, 1012, 360, 436, 853, 281, 1821, 309, 30, 51843], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10649267832438152, "compression_ratio": 1.6644736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213558715420183e-12}, {"id": 675, "seek": 250060, "start": 2500.6, "end": 2504.42, "text": " They developed a framework containing 20 pre-registered mutants.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 4743, 257, 8388, 19273, 945, 659, 12, 3375, 1964, 292, 5839, 1719, 13, 50556], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15687701576634458, "compression_ratio": 1.5971731448763251, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920756466641928e-12}, {"id": 676, "seek": 250060, "start": 2504.56, "end": 2505.02, "text": " Mutants.", "tokens": [50563, 18517, 1719, 13, 50586], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15687701576634458, "compression_ratio": 1.5971731448763251, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920756466641928e-12}, {"id": 677, "seek": 250060, "start": 2505.2999999999997, "end": 2507.02, "text": " Like injecting a virus into the code.", "tokens": [50600, 1743, 10711, 278, 257, 5752, 666, 264, 3089, 13, 50686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15687701576634458, "compression_ratio": 1.5971731448763251, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920756466641928e-12}, {"id": 678, "seek": 250060, "start": 2507.24, "end": 2508.12, "text": " Essentially, yes.", "tokens": [50697, 23596, 11, 2086, 13, 50741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15687701576634458, "compression_ratio": 1.5971731448763251, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920756466641928e-12}, {"id": 679, "seek": 250060, "start": 2508.7999999999997, "end": 2515.3199999999997, "text": " A mutant is a deliberate, specific, logical error injected into the code to see if the", "tokens": [50775, 316, 47198, 307, 257, 30515, 11, 2685, 11, 14978, 6713, 36967, 666, 264, 3089, 281, 536, 498, 264, 51101], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15687701576634458, "compression_ratio": 1.5971731448763251, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920756466641928e-12}, {"id": 680, "seek": 250060, "start": 2515.3199999999997, "end": 2517.2, "text": " Lean4 verification system catches it.", "tokens": [51101, 49303, 19, 30206, 1185, 25496, 309, 13, 51195], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15687701576634458, "compression_ratio": 1.5971731448763251, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920756466641928e-12}, {"id": 681, "seek": 250060, "start": 2517.2999999999997, "end": 2520.88, "text": " And more importantly, to see how the protocol maps the failure.", "tokens": [51200, 400, 544, 8906, 11, 281, 536, 577, 264, 10336, 11317, 264, 7763, 13, 51379], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15687701576634458, "compression_ratio": 1.5971731448763251, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920756466641928e-12}, {"id": 682, "seek": 250060, "start": 2521.04, "end": 2521.2999999999997, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51387, 1033, 13, 51400], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15687701576634458, "compression_ratio": 1.5971731448763251, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920756466641928e-12}, {"id": 683, "seek": 250060, "start": 2521.74, "end": 2526.7, "text": " But here is the most crucial scientific principle of the entire claim shift experiment.", "tokens": [51422, 583, 510, 307, 264, 881, 11462, 8134, 8665, 295, 264, 2302, 3932, 5513, 5120, 13, 51670], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15687701576634458, "compression_ratio": 1.5971731448763251, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920756466641928e-12}, {"id": 684, "seek": 250060, "start": 2526.96, "end": 2530.04, "text": " The paper emphasizes this in bold text.", "tokens": [51683, 440, 3035, 48856, 341, 294, 11928, 2487, 13, 51837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15687701576634458, "compression_ratio": 1.5971731448763251, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920756466641928e-12}, {"id": 685, "seek": 253060, "start": 2530.6, "end": 2533.86, "text": " Ground truth first, then observation.", "tokens": [50365, 28371, 3494, 700, 11, 550, 14816, 13, 50528], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.4409050660974839, "compression_ratio": 0.9491525423728814, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396417202082294e-12}, {"id": 686, "seek": 253060, "start": 2534.64, "end": 2535.5, "text": " Never the reverse.", "tokens": [50567, 7344, 264, 9943, 13, 50610], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.4409050660974839, "compression_ratio": 0.9491525423728814, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396417202082294e-12}, {"id": 687, "seek": 253550, "start": 2535.5, "end": 2538.52, "text": " So they pre-registered the exact mutants.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 436, 659, 12, 3375, 1964, 292, 264, 1900, 5839, 1719, 13, 50516], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11277422829279823, "compression_ratio": 1.7188612099644127, "no_speech_prob": 1.636227178053451e-12}, {"id": 688, "seek": 253550, "start": 2538.82, "end": 2541.48, "text": " Why is it so vitally important that they pre-registered them?", "tokens": [50531, 1545, 307, 309, 370, 9467, 379, 1021, 300, 436, 659, 12, 3375, 1964, 292, 552, 30, 50664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11277422829279823, "compression_ratio": 1.7188612099644127, "no_speech_prob": 1.636227178053451e-12}, {"id": 689, "seek": 253550, "start": 2541.92, "end": 2546.38, "text": " Couldn't they just run the code, mutate it randomly a thousand times, and see what failed?", "tokens": [50686, 35800, 380, 436, 445, 1190, 264, 3089, 11, 5839, 473, 309, 16979, 257, 4714, 1413, 11, 293, 536, 437, 7612, 30, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11277422829279823, "compression_ratio": 1.7188612099644127, "no_speech_prob": 1.636227178053451e-12}, {"id": 690, "seek": 253550, "start": 2546.64, "end": 2551.54, "text": " If you don't predict the exact failure sets beforehand, you fall victim to the trap of", "tokens": [50922, 759, 291, 500, 380, 6069, 264, 1900, 7763, 6352, 22893, 11, 291, 2100, 6760, 281, 264, 11487, 295, 51167], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11277422829279823, "compression_ratio": 1.7188612099644127, "no_speech_prob": 1.636227178053451e-12}, {"id": 691, "seek": 253550, "start": 2551.54, "end": 2552.38, "text": " hindsight bias.", "tokens": [51167, 44357, 12577, 13, 51209], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11277422829279823, "compression_ratio": 1.7188612099644127, "no_speech_prob": 1.636227178053451e-12}, {"id": 692, "seek": 253550, "start": 2552.6, "end": 2553.68, "text": " Which is a huge issue.", "tokens": [51220, 3013, 307, 257, 2603, 2734, 13, 51274], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11277422829279823, "compression_ratio": 1.7188612099644127, "no_speech_prob": 1.636227178053451e-12}, {"id": 693, "seek": 253550, "start": 2554.02, "end": 2556.74, "text": " It is a massive persistent problem in software verification.", "tokens": [51291, 467, 307, 257, 5994, 24315, 1154, 294, 4722, 30206, 13, 51427], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11277422829279823, "compression_ratio": 1.7188612099644127, "no_speech_prob": 1.636227178053451e-12}, {"id": 694, "seek": 253550, "start": 2557.14, "end": 2560.68, "text": " If you just inject a random error and the system crashes, you might pat yourself on the back and say,", "tokens": [51447, 759, 291, 445, 10711, 257, 4974, 6713, 293, 264, 1185, 28642, 11, 291, 1062, 1947, 1803, 322, 264, 646, 293, 584, 11, 51624], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11277422829279823, "compression_ratio": 1.7188612099644127, "no_speech_prob": 1.636227178053451e-12}, {"id": 695, "seek": 256068, "start": 2560.68, "end": 2562.4199999999996, "text": " great, the system got the error, it's secure.", "tokens": [50365, 869, 11, 264, 1185, 658, 264, 6713, 11, 309, 311, 7144, 13, 50452], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12166435773982558, "compression_ratio": 1.5429864253393666, "no_speech_prob": 3.2541311225514624e-12}, {"id": 696, "seek": 256068, "start": 2562.58, "end": 2562.7799999999997, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50460, 1779, 13, 50470], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12166435773982558, "compression_ratio": 1.5429864253393666, "no_speech_prob": 3.2541311225514624e-12}, {"id": 697, "seek": 256068, "start": 2563.1, "end": 2564.8799999999997, "text": " But what if it crashed for the wrong reason?", "tokens": [50486, 583, 437, 498, 309, 24190, 337, 264, 2085, 1778, 30, 50575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12166435773982558, "compression_ratio": 1.5429864253393666, "no_speech_prob": 3.2541311225514624e-12}, {"id": 698, "seek": 256068, "start": 2565.14, "end": 2569.4199999999996, "text": " What if it crashed because of a simple syntax error, like a missing comma, rather than actually", "tokens": [50588, 708, 498, 309, 24190, 570, 295, 257, 2199, 28431, 6713, 11, 411, 257, 5361, 22117, 11, 2831, 813, 767, 50802], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12166435773982558, "compression_ratio": 1.5429864253393666, "no_speech_prob": 3.2541311225514624e-12}, {"id": 699, "seek": 256068, "start": 2569.4199999999996, "end": 2572.3799999999997, "text": " detecting the deep semantic lie you tried to inject?", "tokens": [50802, 40237, 264, 2452, 47982, 4544, 291, 3031, 281, 10711, 30, 50950], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12166435773982558, "compression_ratio": 1.5429864253393666, "no_speech_prob": 3.2541311225514624e-12}, {"id": 700, "seek": 256068, "start": 2572.58, "end": 2577.8399999999997, "text": " By pre-registering, Flixion forced themselves to mathematically predict exactly which theorems", "tokens": [50960, 3146, 659, 12, 3375, 1964, 278, 11, 3235, 970, 313, 7579, 2969, 281, 44003, 6069, 2293, 597, 10299, 2592, 51223], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12166435773982558, "compression_ratio": 1.5429864253393666, "no_speech_prob": 3.2541311225514624e-12}, {"id": 701, "seek": 257784, "start": 2577.84, "end": 2583.7400000000002, "text": " should fail, exactly which edges should break, and exactly which branches the failure should", "tokens": [50365, 820, 3061, 11, 2293, 597, 8819, 820, 1821, 11, 293, 2293, 597, 14770, 264, 7763, 820, 50660], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10835620825239223, "compression_ratio": 1.7580645161290323, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485370790160104e-12}, {"id": 702, "seek": 257784, "start": 2583.7400000000002, "end": 2587.44, "text": " propagate down, all before the computer ever executed the code.", "tokens": [50660, 48256, 760, 11, 439, 949, 264, 3820, 1562, 17577, 264, 3089, 13, 50845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10835620825239223, "compression_ratio": 1.7580645161290323, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485370790160104e-12}, {"id": 703, "seek": 257784, "start": 2587.5, "end": 2590.28, "text": " It's like calling your exact shot in a game of pool.", "tokens": [50848, 467, 311, 411, 5141, 428, 1900, 3347, 294, 257, 1216, 295, 7005, 13, 50987], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10835620825239223, "compression_ratio": 1.7580645161290323, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485370790160104e-12}, {"id": 704, "seek": 257784, "start": 2590.54, "end": 2590.98, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51000, 7587, 13, 51022], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10835620825239223, "compression_ratio": 1.7580645161290323, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485370790160104e-12}, {"id": 705, "seek": 257784, "start": 2591.1200000000003, "end": 2594.6800000000003, "text": " You have to point and say, eight ball, off the rail, corner pocket.", "tokens": [51029, 509, 362, 281, 935, 293, 584, 11, 3180, 2594, 11, 766, 264, 8765, 11, 4538, 8963, 13, 51207], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10835620825239223, "compression_ratio": 1.7580645161290323, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485370790160104e-12}, {"id": 706, "seek": 257784, "start": 2594.94, "end": 2598.94, "text": " If you just hit the ball and it happens to go in the side pocket by accident, it doesn't count.", "tokens": [51220, 759, 291, 445, 2045, 264, 2594, 293, 309, 2314, 281, 352, 294, 264, 1252, 8963, 538, 6398, 11, 309, 1177, 380, 1207, 13, 51420], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10835620825239223, "compression_ratio": 1.7580645161290323, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485370790160104e-12}, {"id": 707, "seek": 257784, "start": 2599.36, "end": 2601.88, "text": " You didn't prove you know how the physics work, you just got lucky.", "tokens": [51441, 509, 994, 380, 7081, 291, 458, 577, 264, 10649, 589, 11, 291, 445, 658, 6356, 13, 51567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10835620825239223, "compression_ratio": 1.7580645161290323, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485370790160104e-12}, {"id": 708, "seek": 257784, "start": 2602.2000000000003, "end": 2603.1600000000003, "text": " That's a great way to put it.", "tokens": [51583, 663, 311, 257, 869, 636, 281, 829, 309, 13, 51631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10835620825239223, "compression_ratio": 1.7580645161290323, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485370790160104e-12}, {"id": 709, "seek": 257784, "start": 2603.4, "end": 2606.7000000000003, "text": " You have to prove you understand the exact logical relationship.", "tokens": [51643, 509, 362, 281, 7081, 291, 1223, 264, 1900, 14978, 2480, 13, 51808], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10835620825239223, "compression_ratio": 1.7580645161290323, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485370790160104e-12}, {"id": 710, "seek": 260670, "start": 2606.7, "end": 2614.3399999999997, "text": " Will the mutant make the claim mathematically stronger, weaker, incompatible, or completely", "tokens": [50365, 3099, 264, 47198, 652, 264, 3932, 44003, 7249, 11, 24286, 11, 40393, 267, 964, 11, 420, 2584, 50747], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10427188873291016, "compression_ratio": 1.6655052264808363, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860671066444954e-12}, {"id": 711, "seek": 260670, "start": 2614.3399999999997, "end": 2615.2999999999997, "text": " logically refuted?", "tokens": [50747, 38887, 1895, 4866, 30, 50795], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10427188873291016, "compression_ratio": 1.6655052264808363, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860671066444954e-12}, {"id": 712, "seek": 260670, "start": 2615.48, "end": 2617.7599999999998, "text": " Okay, let's look at the actual mutants they threw at this thing.", "tokens": [50804, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 574, 412, 264, 3539, 5839, 1719, 436, 11918, 412, 341, 551, 13, 50918], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10427188873291016, "compression_ratio": 1.6655052264808363, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860671066444954e-12}, {"id": 713, "seek": 260670, "start": 2618.0, "end": 2621.2599999999998, "text": " The outline mentions some flagship mutants that really proved the concept.", "tokens": [50930, 440, 16387, 23844, 512, 30400, 5839, 1719, 300, 534, 14617, 264, 3410, 13, 51093], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10427188873291016, "compression_ratio": 1.6655052264808363, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860671066444954e-12}, {"id": 714, "seek": 260670, "start": 2621.68, "end": 2625.8799999999997, "text": " So if they are trying to break the interface, what exactly did they inject into the code?", "tokens": [51114, 407, 498, 436, 366, 1382, 281, 1821, 264, 9226, 11, 437, 2293, 630, 436, 10711, 666, 264, 3089, 30, 51324], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10427188873291016, "compression_ratio": 1.6655052264808363, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860671066444954e-12}, {"id": 715, "seek": 260670, "start": 2626.02, "end": 2627.08, "text": " Did they just delete a line?", "tokens": [51331, 2589, 436, 445, 12097, 257, 1622, 30, 51384], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10427188873291016, "compression_ratio": 1.6655052264808363, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860671066444954e-12}, {"id": 716, "seek": 260670, "start": 2627.3999999999996, "end": 2630.2999999999997, "text": " Well, let's start with M09, which tests a different mechanic.", "tokens": [51400, 1042, 11, 718, 311, 722, 365, 376, 13811, 11, 597, 6921, 257, 819, 23860, 13, 51545], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10427188873291016, "compression_ratio": 1.6655052264808363, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860671066444954e-12}, {"id": 717, "seek": 260670, "start": 2631.22, "end": 2632.8799999999997, "text": " M09 is a constant mutation.", "tokens": [51591, 376, 13811, 307, 257, 5754, 27960, 13, 51674], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10427188873291016, "compression_ratio": 1.6655052264808363, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860671066444954e-12}, {"id": 718, "seek": 260670, "start": 2632.9399999999996, "end": 2633.5, "text": " What does that do?", "tokens": [51677, 708, 775, 300, 360, 30, 51705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10427188873291016, "compression_ratio": 1.6655052264808363, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860671066444954e-12}, {"id": 719, "seek": 263350, "start": 2633.5, "end": 2639.22, "text": " They went to the very root of one of the branches, let's call it node D1, and simply changed a", "tokens": [50365, 814, 1437, 281, 264, 588, 5593, 295, 472, 295, 264, 14770, 11, 718, 311, 818, 309, 9984, 413, 16, 11, 293, 2935, 3105, 257, 50651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12361939748128255, "compression_ratio": 1.664516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.1201839152444326e-12}, {"id": 720, "seek": 263350, "start": 2639.22, "end": 2640.64, "text": " constant numerical value.", "tokens": [50651, 5754, 29054, 2158, 13, 50722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12361939748128255, "compression_ratio": 1.664516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.1201839152444326e-12}, {"id": 721, "seek": 263350, "start": 2640.86, "end": 2641.14, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50733, 1033, 13, 50747], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12361939748128255, "compression_ratio": 1.664516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.1201839152444326e-12}, {"id": 722, "seek": 263350, "start": 2641.84, "end": 2647.4, "text": " Based on the type dependency graph, they pre-registered the prediction that this should cause the semantic", "tokens": [50782, 18785, 322, 264, 2010, 33621, 4295, 11, 436, 659, 12, 3375, 1964, 292, 264, 17630, 300, 341, 820, 3082, 264, 47982, 51060], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12361939748128255, "compression_ratio": 1.664516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.1201839152444326e-12}, {"id": 723, "seek": 263350, "start": 2647.4, "end": 2652.48, "text": " theorems on branch one to fail, but the theorems on branch two should remain perfectly valid.", "tokens": [51060, 10299, 2592, 322, 9819, 472, 281, 3061, 11, 457, 264, 10299, 2592, 322, 9819, 732, 820, 6222, 6239, 7363, 13, 51314], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12361939748128255, "compression_ratio": 1.664516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.1201839152444326e-12}, {"id": 724, "seek": 263350, "start": 2652.7, "end": 2653.54, "text": " And did it work?", "tokens": [51325, 400, 630, 309, 589, 30, 51367], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12361939748128255, "compression_ratio": 1.664516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.1201839152444326e-12}, {"id": 725, "seek": 263350, "start": 2653.84, "end": 2656.56, "text": " When they ran the lean kernel, that's exactly what happened.", "tokens": [51382, 1133, 436, 5872, 264, 11659, 28256, 11, 300, 311, 2293, 437, 2011, 13, 51518], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12361939748128255, "compression_ratio": 1.664516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.1201839152444326e-12}, {"id": 726, "seek": 263350, "start": 2656.8, "end": 2659.52, "text": " It isolated the branch root propagation perfectly.", "tokens": [51530, 467, 14621, 264, 9819, 5593, 38377, 6239, 13, 51666], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12361939748128255, "compression_ratio": 1.664516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.1201839152444326e-12}, {"id": 727, "seek": 263350, "start": 2659.94, "end": 2662.36, "text": " The protocol didn't panic and shut down the whole document.", "tokens": [51687, 440, 10336, 994, 380, 14783, 293, 5309, 760, 264, 1379, 4166, 13, 51808], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12361939748128255, "compression_ratio": 1.664516129032258, "no_speech_prob": 1.1201839152444326e-12}, {"id": 728, "seek": 266236, "start": 2662.36, "end": 2662.8, "text": " Awesome.", "tokens": [50365, 10391, 13, 50387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17733466271126624, "compression_ratio": 1.525, "no_speech_prob": 1.1028187911488185e-12}, {"id": 729, "seek": 266236, "start": 2662.98, "end": 2663.7400000000002, "text": " What about M15?", "tokens": [50396, 708, 466, 376, 5211, 30, 50434], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17733466271126624, "compression_ratio": 1.525, "no_speech_prob": 1.1028187911488185e-12}, {"id": 730, "seek": 266236, "start": 2664.2200000000003, "end": 2665.44, "text": " Ah, M15.", "tokens": [50458, 2438, 11, 376, 5211, 13, 50519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17733466271126624, "compression_ratio": 1.525, "no_speech_prob": 1.1028187911488185e-12}, {"id": 731, "seek": 266236, "start": 2665.84, "end": 2667.86, "text": " This answers your question about deleting a line.", "tokens": [50539, 639, 6338, 428, 1168, 466, 48946, 257, 1622, 13, 50640], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17733466271126624, "compression_ratio": 1.525, "no_speech_prob": 1.1028187911488185e-12}, {"id": 732, "seek": 266236, "start": 2668.48, "end": 2671.1200000000003, "text": " M15 is hypothesis deletion.", "tokens": [50671, 376, 5211, 307, 17291, 1103, 302, 313, 13, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17733466271126624, "compression_ratio": 1.525, "no_speech_prob": 1.1028187911488185e-12}, {"id": 733, "seek": 266236, "start": 2671.36, "end": 2671.6400000000003, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50815, 1033, 13, 50829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17733466271126624, "compression_ratio": 1.525, "no_speech_prob": 1.1028187911488185e-12}, {"id": 734, "seek": 266236, "start": 2671.82, "end": 2675.34, "text": " They systematically deleted a required hypothesis from a central proof.", "tokens": [50838, 814, 39531, 22981, 257, 4739, 17291, 490, 257, 5777, 8177, 13, 51014], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17733466271126624, "compression_ratio": 1.525, "no_speech_prob": 1.1028187911488185e-12}, {"id": 735, "seek": 266236, "start": 2676.2000000000003, "end": 2680.7200000000003, "text": " The fascinating, almost beautiful thing here is that the system didn't just fail passively.", "tokens": [51057, 440, 10343, 11, 1920, 2238, 551, 510, 307, 300, 264, 1185, 994, 380, 445, 3061, 1320, 3413, 13, 51283], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17733466271126624, "compression_ratio": 1.525, "no_speech_prob": 1.1028187911488185e-12}, {"id": 736, "seek": 266236, "start": 2681.08, "end": 2684.42, "text": " It became actively self-refuting via an existing witness.", "tokens": [51301, 467, 3062, 13022, 2698, 12, 33115, 10861, 5766, 364, 6741, 7286, 13, 51468], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17733466271126624, "compression_ratio": 1.525, "no_speech_prob": 1.1028187911488185e-12}, {"id": 737, "seek": 266236, "start": 2684.58, "end": 2685.5, "text": " Wait, what does that mean?", "tokens": [51476, 3802, 11, 437, 775, 300, 914, 30, 51522], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17733466271126624, "compression_ratio": 1.525, "no_speech_prob": 1.1028187911488185e-12}, {"id": 738, "seek": 268550, "start": 2685.5, "end": 2690.62, "text": " The kernel-checked code actually contained the mathematical counterexample that proved the", "tokens": [50365, 440, 28256, 12, 15723, 292, 3089, 767, 16212, 264, 18894, 1207, 323, 87, 335, 781, 300, 14617, 264, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16162051937796854, "compression_ratio": 1.5726141078838174, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691689042573233e-12}, {"id": 739, "seek": 268550, "start": 2690.62, "end": 2693.46, "text": " newly mutated theorem was completely universally false.", "tokens": [50621, 15109, 5839, 770, 20904, 390, 2584, 43995, 7908, 13, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16162051937796854, "compression_ratio": 1.5726141078838174, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691689042573233e-12}, {"id": 740, "seek": 268550, "start": 2694.0, "end": 2697.48, "text": " It actively destroyed the false claim using its own internal logic.", "tokens": [50790, 467, 13022, 8937, 264, 7908, 3932, 1228, 1080, 1065, 6920, 9952, 13, 50964], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16162051937796854, "compression_ratio": 1.5726141078838174, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691689042573233e-12}, {"id": 741, "seek": 268550, "start": 2697.84, "end": 2698.56, "text": " That's incredible.", "tokens": [50982, 663, 311, 4651, 13, 51018], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16162051937796854, "compression_ratio": 1.5726141078838174, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691689042573233e-12}, {"id": 742, "seek": 268550, "start": 2698.68, "end": 2703.52, "text": " It's like a mathematical immune system recognizing the virus and immediately producing the exact", "tokens": [51024, 467, 311, 411, 257, 18894, 11992, 1185, 18538, 264, 5752, 293, 4258, 10501, 264, 1900, 51266], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16162051937796854, "compression_ratio": 1.5726141078838174, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691689042573233e-12}, {"id": 743, "seek": 268550, "start": 2703.52, "end": 2704.96, "text": " antibody to destroy it.", "tokens": [51266, 34507, 281, 5293, 309, 13, 51338], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16162051937796854, "compression_ratio": 1.5726141078838174, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691689042573233e-12}, {"id": 744, "seek": 268550, "start": 2705.04, "end": 2705.46, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51342, 7587, 13, 51363], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16162051937796854, "compression_ratio": 1.5726141078838174, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691689042573233e-12}, {"id": 745, "seek": 268550, "start": 2705.7, "end": 2706.42, "text": " What about M13?", "tokens": [51375, 708, 466, 376, 7668, 30, 51411], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16162051937796854, "compression_ratio": 1.5726141078838174, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691689042573233e-12}, {"id": 746, "seek": 270642, "start": 2706.42, "end": 2712.96, "text": " M13 is a quantifier mutation, and the results from this one yield a deeply counterintuitive", "tokens": [50365, 376, 7668, 307, 257, 4426, 9902, 27960, 11, 293, 264, 3542, 490, 341, 472, 11257, 257, 8760, 5682, 686, 48314, 50692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15725182427300347, "compression_ratio": 1.2647058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.6548928026549614e-12}, {"id": 747, "seek": 270642, "start": 2712.96, "end": 2716.44, "text": " insight that AI developers really need to pay attention to.", "tokens": [50692, 11269, 300, 7318, 8849, 534, 643, 281, 1689, 3202, 281, 13, 50866], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15725182427300347, "compression_ratio": 1.2647058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.6548928026549614e-12}, {"id": 748, "seek": 270642, "start": 2716.6, "end": 2717.4, "text": " Okay, I'm listening.", "tokens": [50874, 1033, 11, 286, 478, 4764, 13, 50914], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15725182427300347, "compression_ratio": 1.2647058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.6548928026549614e-12}, {"id": 749, "seek": 271740, "start": 2717.4, "end": 2723.2400000000002, "text": " Often, people intuitively assume that if you make a hypothesis weaker, if you make the starting", "tokens": [50365, 20043, 11, 561, 46506, 6552, 300, 498, 291, 652, 257, 17291, 24286, 11, 498, 291, 652, 264, 2891, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13883999188741047, "compression_ratio": 1.6503496503496504, "no_speech_prob": 1.832461482900727e-12}, {"id": 750, "seek": 271740, "start": 2723.2400000000002, "end": 2728.88, "text": " assumptions less strict or more vague, it should make the downstream proofs easier to", "tokens": [50657, 17695, 1570, 10910, 420, 544, 24247, 11, 309, 820, 652, 264, 30621, 8177, 82, 3571, 281, 50939], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13883999188741047, "compression_ratio": 1.6503496503496504, "no_speech_prob": 1.832461482900727e-12}, {"id": 751, "seek": 271740, "start": 2728.88, "end": 2729.2400000000002, "text": " prove.", "tokens": [50939, 7081, 13, 50957], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13883999188741047, "compression_ratio": 1.6503496503496504, "no_speech_prob": 1.832461482900727e-12}, {"id": 752, "seek": 271740, "start": 2729.46, "end": 2730.94, "text": " The bar is lower, right?", "tokens": [50968, 440, 2159, 307, 3126, 11, 558, 30, 51042], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13883999188741047, "compression_ratio": 1.6503496503496504, "no_speech_prob": 1.832461482900727e-12}, {"id": 753, "seek": 271740, "start": 2731.06, "end": 2731.2200000000003, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51048, 1779, 13, 51056], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13883999188741047, "compression_ratio": 1.6503496503496504, "no_speech_prob": 1.832461482900727e-12}, {"id": 754, "seek": 271740, "start": 2731.26, "end": 2736.86, "text": " If I say, find me a vehicle instead of, find me a red 2015 Honda Civic, it should be easier", "tokens": [51058, 759, 286, 584, 11, 915, 385, 257, 5864, 2602, 295, 11, 915, 385, 257, 2182, 7546, 26989, 46237, 11, 309, 820, 312, 3571, 51338], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13883999188741047, "compression_ratio": 1.6503496503496504, "no_speech_prob": 1.832461482900727e-12}, {"id": 755, "seek": 271740, "start": 2736.86, "end": 2737.46, "text": " to fulfill.", "tokens": [51338, 281, 13875, 13, 51368], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13883999188741047, "compression_ratio": 1.6503496503496504, "no_speech_prob": 1.832461482900727e-12}, {"id": 756, "seek": 271740, "start": 2737.78, "end": 2742.96, "text": " But M13 proved mathematically that weakening hypotheses can actually make downstream formal", "tokens": [51384, 583, 376, 7668, 14617, 44003, 300, 5336, 4559, 49969, 393, 767, 652, 30621, 9860, 51643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13883999188741047, "compression_ratio": 1.6503496503496504, "no_speech_prob": 1.832461482900727e-12}, {"id": 757, "seek": 271740, "start": 2742.96, "end": 2745.92, "text": " proof harder or even impossible to verify.", "tokens": [51643, 8177, 6081, 420, 754, 6243, 281, 16888, 13, 51791], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13883999188741047, "compression_ratio": 1.6503496503496504, "no_speech_prob": 1.832461482900727e-12}, {"id": 758, "seek": 271740, "start": 2746.1800000000003, "end": 2746.5, "text": " Really?", "tokens": [51804, 4083, 30, 51820], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13883999188741047, "compression_ratio": 1.6503496503496504, "no_speech_prob": 1.832461482900727e-12}, {"id": 759, "seek": 271740, "start": 2746.5, "end": 2747.0, "text": " Why?", "tokens": [51820, 1545, 30, 51845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13883999188741047, "compression_ratio": 1.6503496503496504, "no_speech_prob": 1.832461482900727e-12}, {"id": 760, "seek": 274740, "start": 2747.4, "end": 2749.6800000000003, "text": " By making it weaker, you break the interface dependencies.", "tokens": [50365, 3146, 1455, 309, 24286, 11, 291, 1821, 264, 9226, 36606, 13, 50479], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17289307361512674, "compression_ratio": 1.5844594594594594, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211890549970188e-12}, {"id": 761, "seek": 274740, "start": 2750.1800000000003, "end": 2754.6600000000003, "text": " You no longer have the strict, precise, logical tools you need to finish the complex construction", "tokens": [50504, 509, 572, 2854, 362, 264, 10910, 11, 13600, 11, 14978, 3873, 291, 643, 281, 2413, 264, 3997, 6435, 50728], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17289307361512674, "compression_ratio": 1.5844594594594594, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211890549970188e-12}, {"id": 762, "seek": 274740, "start": 2754.6600000000003, "end": 2755.26, "text": " later on.", "tokens": [50728, 1780, 322, 13, 50758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17289307361512674, "compression_ratio": 1.5844594594594594, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211890549970188e-12}, {"id": 763, "seek": 274740, "start": 2755.7000000000003, "end": 2757.7400000000002, "text": " The proof collapses because it lacks traction.", "tokens": [50780, 440, 8177, 48765, 570, 309, 31132, 23558, 13, 50882], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17289307361512674, "compression_ratio": 1.5844594594594594, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211890549970188e-12}, {"id": 764, "seek": 274740, "start": 2758.26, "end": 2761.3, "text": " So being vaguer doesn't make it easier for the AI to prove it.", "tokens": [50908, 407, 885, 13501, 5486, 1177, 380, 652, 309, 3571, 337, 264, 7318, 281, 7081, 309, 13, 51060], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17289307361512674, "compression_ratio": 1.5844594594594594, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211890549970188e-12}, {"id": 765, "seek": 274740, "start": 2761.62, "end": 2766.8, "text": " It deprives the system of the precise gears it needs to turn to reach the semantic truth.", "tokens": [51076, 467, 27095, 977, 264, 1185, 295, 264, 13600, 20915, 309, 2203, 281, 1261, 281, 2524, 264, 47982, 3494, 13, 51335], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17289307361512674, "compression_ratio": 1.5844594594594594, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211890549970188e-12}, {"id": 766, "seek": 274740, "start": 2766.96, "end": 2767.34, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51343, 7587, 13, 51362], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17289307361512674, "compression_ratio": 1.5844594594594594, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211890549970188e-12}, {"id": 767, "seek": 274740, "start": 2767.34, "end": 2768.62, "text": " You lose your grip on the logic.", "tokens": [51362, 509, 3624, 428, 12007, 322, 264, 9952, 13, 51426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17289307361512674, "compression_ratio": 1.5844594594594594, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211890549970188e-12}, {"id": 768, "seek": 274740, "start": 2769.2200000000003, "end": 2771.1600000000003, "text": " And finally, we arrive at M12.", "tokens": [51456, 400, 2721, 11, 321, 8881, 412, 376, 4762, 13, 51553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17289307361512674, "compression_ratio": 1.5844594594594594, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211890549970188e-12}, {"id": 769, "seek": 274740, "start": 2771.42, "end": 2771.9, "text": " M12.", "tokens": [51566, 376, 4762, 13, 51590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17289307361512674, "compression_ratio": 1.5844594594594594, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211890549970188e-12}, {"id": 770, "seek": 274740, "start": 2772.1800000000003, "end": 2773.44, "text": " I cannot overstate this.", "tokens": [51604, 286, 2644, 670, 15406, 341, 13, 51667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17289307361512674, "compression_ratio": 1.5844594594594594, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211890549970188e-12}, {"id": 771, "seek": 277344, "start": 2773.44, "end": 2780.32, "text": " M12 is perhaps the most important mutant for the entire AI industry to understand right", "tokens": [50365, 376, 4762, 307, 4317, 264, 881, 1021, 47198, 337, 264, 2302, 7318, 3518, 281, 1223, 558, 50709], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16075246087436018, "compression_ratio": 1.4849785407725322, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080645708586473e-12}, {"id": 772, "seek": 277344, "start": 2780.32, "end": 2780.54, "text": " now.", "tokens": [50709, 586, 13, 50720], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16075246087436018, "compression_ratio": 1.4849785407725322, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080645708586473e-12}, {"id": 773, "seek": 277344, "start": 2780.7000000000003, "end": 2780.86, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50728, 1033, 13, 50736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16075246087436018, "compression_ratio": 1.4849785407725322, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080645708586473e-12}, {"id": 774, "seek": 277344, "start": 2780.94, "end": 2781.78, "text": " Build the suspense.", "tokens": [50740, 11875, 264, 47803, 13, 50782], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16075246087436018, "compression_ratio": 1.4849785407725322, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080645708586473e-12}, {"id": 775, "seek": 277344, "start": 2781.96, "end": 2782.4, "text": " What is it?", "tokens": [50791, 708, 307, 309, 30, 50813], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16075246087436018, "compression_ratio": 1.4849785407725322, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080645708586473e-12}, {"id": 776, "seek": 277344, "start": 2782.58, "end": 2788.04, "text": " M12 showed conclusively that checking the parity of a state, meaning just checking the", "tokens": [50822, 376, 4762, 4712, 18646, 3413, 300, 8568, 264, 44747, 295, 257, 1785, 11, 3620, 445, 8568, 264, 51095], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16075246087436018, "compression_ratio": 1.4849785407725322, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080645708586473e-12}, {"id": 777, "seek": 277344, "start": 2788.04, "end": 2793.9, "text": " superficial structural count of variables or nodes in a syntax tree, is way, way too", "tokens": [51095, 34622, 15067, 1207, 295, 9102, 420, 13891, 294, 257, 28431, 4230, 11, 307, 636, 11, 636, 886, 51388], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16075246087436018, "compression_ratio": 1.4849785407725322, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080645708586473e-12}, {"id": 778, "seek": 277344, "start": 2793.9, "end": 2796.34, "text": " coarse to detect profound semantic changes.", "tokens": [51388, 39312, 281, 5531, 14382, 47982, 2962, 13, 51510], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16075246087436018, "compression_ratio": 1.4849785407725322, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080645708586473e-12}, {"id": 779, "seek": 279634, "start": 2796.34, "end": 2800.6000000000004, "text": " Let's really break down what checking the parity of a state means, because this feels", "tokens": [50365, 961, 311, 534, 1821, 760, 437, 8568, 264, 44747, 295, 257, 1785, 1355, 11, 570, 341, 3417, 50578], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11037027332144723, "compression_ratio": 1.4060913705583757, "no_speech_prob": 1.4378131931586102e-12}, {"id": 780, "seek": 279634, "start": 2800.6000000000004, "end": 2803.6000000000004, "text": " like the absolute crux of the issue with AI summarizers.", "tokens": [50578, 411, 264, 8236, 5140, 87, 295, 264, 2734, 365, 7318, 14611, 22525, 13, 50728], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11037027332144723, "compression_ratio": 1.4060913705583757, "no_speech_prob": 1.4378131931586102e-12}, {"id": 781, "seek": 279634, "start": 2803.82, "end": 2803.88, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50739, 1033, 13, 50742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11037027332144723, "compression_ratio": 1.4060913705583757, "no_speech_prob": 1.4378131931586102e-12}, {"id": 782, "seek": 279634, "start": 2804.36, "end": 2809.0, "text": " When M12 was injected, it perfectly matched the superficial mathematical invariance of", "tokens": [50766, 1133, 376, 4762, 390, 36967, 11, 309, 6239, 21447, 264, 34622, 18894, 33270, 719, 295, 50998], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11037027332144723, "compression_ratio": 1.4060913705583757, "no_speech_prob": 1.4378131931586102e-12}, {"id": 783, "seek": 279634, "start": 2809.0, "end": 2809.8, "text": " the original code.", "tokens": [50998, 264, 3380, 3089, 13, 51038], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11037027332144723, "compression_ratio": 1.4060913705583757, "no_speech_prob": 1.4378131931586102e-12}, {"id": 784, "seek": 279634, "start": 2809.9, "end": 2810.7000000000003, "text": " So it looked the same.", "tokens": [51043, 407, 309, 2956, 264, 912, 13, 51083], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11037027332144723, "compression_ratio": 1.4060913705583757, "no_speech_prob": 1.4378131931586102e-12}, {"id": 785, "seek": 281070, "start": 2810.7, "end": 2813.98, "text": " If you just counted the variables, if you just looked at the structural shape of the", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 445, 20150, 264, 9102, 11, 498, 291, 445, 2956, 412, 264, 15067, 3909, 295, 264, 50529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17484870709870992, "compression_ratio": 1.5925925925925926, "no_speech_prob": 1.56129156912016e-12}, {"id": 786, "seek": 281070, "start": 2813.98, "end": 2815.98, "text": " formula, it looked identical to the original.", "tokens": [50529, 8513, 11, 309, 2956, 14800, 281, 264, 3380, 13, 50629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17484870709870992, "compression_ratio": 1.5925925925925926, "no_speech_prob": 1.56129156912016e-12}, {"id": 787, "seek": 281070, "start": 2816.52, "end": 2817.2799999999997, "text": " The parity matched.", "tokens": [50656, 440, 44747, 21447, 13, 50694], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17484870709870992, "compression_ratio": 1.5925925925925926, "no_speech_prob": 1.56129156912016e-12}, {"id": 788, "seek": 281070, "start": 2817.7599999999998, "end": 2821.7599999999998, "text": " But internally, the logical meaning was completely corrupted and reversed.", "tokens": [50718, 583, 19501, 11, 264, 14978, 3620, 390, 2584, 39480, 293, 30563, 13, 50918], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17484870709870992, "compression_ratio": 1.5925925925925926, "no_speech_prob": 1.56129156912016e-12}, {"id": 789, "seek": 281070, "start": 2822.0, "end": 2822.3599999999997, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50930, 3153, 13, 50948], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17484870709870992, "compression_ratio": 1.5925925925925926, "no_speech_prob": 1.56129156912016e-12}, {"id": 790, "seek": 281070, "start": 2822.58, "end": 2825.0, "text": " Let me put this into a visceral real world narrative.", "tokens": [50959, 961, 385, 829, 341, 666, 257, 1452, 47879, 957, 1002, 9977, 13, 51080], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17484870709870992, "compression_ratio": 1.5925925925925926, "no_speech_prob": 1.56129156912016e-12}, {"id": 791, "seek": 281070, "start": 2825.18, "end": 2831.22, "text": " Imagine an AI summarizer is looking at a dense 100 page financial report from a major bank.", "tokens": [51089, 11739, 364, 7318, 14611, 6545, 307, 1237, 412, 257, 18011, 2319, 3028, 4669, 2275, 490, 257, 2563, 3765, 13, 51391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17484870709870992, "compression_ratio": 1.5925925925925926, "no_speech_prob": 1.56129156912016e-12}, {"id": 792, "seek": 281070, "start": 2831.64, "end": 2837.7999999999997, "text": " The original report has a very specific, deeply verified semantic claim buried on page 40.", "tokens": [51412, 440, 3380, 2275, 575, 257, 588, 2685, 11, 8760, 31197, 47982, 3932, 14101, 322, 3028, 3356, 13, 51720], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17484870709870992, "compression_ratio": 1.5925925925925926, "no_speech_prob": 1.56129156912016e-12}, {"id": 793, "seek": 281070, "start": 2837.96, "end": 2838.24, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51728, 1033, 13, 51742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17484870709870992, "compression_ratio": 1.5925925925925926, "no_speech_prob": 1.56129156912016e-12}, {"id": 794, "seek": 283824, "start": 2838.24, "end": 2843.9399999999996, "text": " It says, based on complex risk models, do not short this specific tech stock.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1619, 11, 2361, 322, 3997, 3148, 5245, 11, 360, 406, 2099, 341, 2685, 7553, 4127, 13, 50650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15818517010911068, "compression_ratio": 1.6433566433566433, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851325424596338e-12}, {"id": 795, "seek": 283824, "start": 2844.1, "end": 2844.9599999999996, "text": " Very important advice.", "tokens": [50658, 4372, 1021, 5192, 13, 50701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15818517010911068, "compression_ratio": 1.6433566433566433, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851325424596338e-12}, {"id": 796, "seek": 283824, "start": 2845.18, "end": 2845.3799999999997, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50712, 1779, 13, 50722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15818517010911068, "compression_ratio": 1.6433566433566433, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851325424596338e-12}, {"id": 797, "seek": 283824, "start": 2845.74, "end": 2850.52, "text": " Now, the AI reads this, and in the process of condensing it for a one-page executive summary,", "tokens": [50740, 823, 11, 264, 7318, 15700, 341, 11, 293, 294, 264, 1399, 295, 2224, 22481, 309, 337, 257, 472, 12, 15161, 10140, 12691, 11, 50979], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15818517010911068, "compression_ratio": 1.6433566433566433, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851325424596338e-12}, {"id": 798, "seek": 283824, "start": 2850.66, "end": 2851.8399999999997, "text": " it mutates the claim.", "tokens": [50986, 309, 5839, 1024, 264, 3932, 13, 51045], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15818517010911068, "compression_ratio": 1.6433566433566433, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851325424596338e-12}, {"id": 799, "seek": 283824, "start": 2852.04, "end": 2853.62, "text": " It drops a single negative.", "tokens": [51055, 467, 11438, 257, 2167, 3671, 13, 51134], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15818517010911068, "compression_ratio": 1.6433566433566433, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851325424596338e-12}, {"id": 800, "seek": 283824, "start": 2853.9599999999996, "end": 2854.52, "text": " Oh, no.", "tokens": [51151, 876, 11, 572, 13, 51179], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15818517010911068, "compression_ratio": 1.6433566433566433, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851325424596338e-12}, {"id": 801, "seek": 283824, "start": 2854.7, "end": 2858.5, "text": " The summary now reads, short this specific tech stock.", "tokens": [51188, 440, 12691, 586, 15700, 11, 2099, 341, 2685, 7553, 4127, 13, 51378], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15818517010911068, "compression_ratio": 1.6433566433566433, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851325424596338e-12}, {"id": 802, "seek": 283824, "start": 2858.58, "end": 2859.7799999999997, "text": " A total semantic reversal.", "tokens": [51382, 316, 3217, 47982, 42778, 13, 51442], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15818517010911068, "compression_ratio": 1.6433566433566433, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851325424596338e-12}, {"id": 803, "seek": 283824, "start": 2859.9599999999996, "end": 2860.2, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51451, 1779, 13, 51463], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15818517010911068, "compression_ratio": 1.6433566433566433, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851325424596338e-12}, {"id": 804, "seek": 283824, "start": 2860.62, "end": 2865.3399999999997, "text": " Now, imagine we are using the tech industry's current favorite tool, the digital watermark.", "tokens": [51484, 823, 11, 3811, 321, 366, 1228, 264, 7553, 3518, 311, 2190, 2954, 2290, 11, 264, 4562, 1281, 5638, 13, 51720], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15818517010911068, "compression_ratio": 1.6433566433566433, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851325424596338e-12}, {"id": 805, "seek": 283824, "start": 2865.58, "end": 2866.4799999999996, "text": " Which checks parity.", "tokens": [51732, 3013, 13834, 44747, 13, 51777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15818517010911068, "compression_ratio": 1.6433566433566433, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851325424596338e-12}, {"id": 806, "seek": 283824, "start": 2866.66, "end": 2867.08, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51786, 7587, 13, 51807], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15818517010911068, "compression_ratio": 1.6433566433566433, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851325424596338e-12}, {"id": 807, "seek": 286708, "start": 2867.08, "end": 2868.6, "text": " The system checks the parity.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1185, 13834, 264, 44747, 13, 50441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.186498340807463, "compression_ratio": 1.7180327868852459, "no_speech_prob": 1.6776770944693098e-12}, {"id": 808, "seek": 286708, "start": 2868.7799999999997, "end": 2869.86, "text": " It looks at the AI summary.", "tokens": [50450, 467, 1542, 412, 264, 7318, 12691, 13, 50504], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.186498340807463, "compression_ratio": 1.7180327868852459, "no_speech_prob": 1.6776770944693098e-12}, {"id": 809, "seek": 286708, "start": 2870.04, "end": 2871.56, "text": " It sees the same financial vocabulary.", "tokens": [50513, 467, 8194, 264, 912, 4669, 19864, 13, 50589], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.186498340807463, "compression_ratio": 1.7180327868852459, "no_speech_prob": 1.6776770944693098e-12}, {"id": 810, "seek": 286708, "start": 2871.9, "end": 2873.38, "text": " It sees the same company names.", "tokens": [50606, 467, 8194, 264, 912, 2237, 5288, 13, 50680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.186498340807463, "compression_ratio": 1.7180327868852459, "no_speech_prob": 1.6776770944693098e-12}, {"id": 811, "seek": 286708, "start": 2873.7999999999997, "end": 2876.4, "text": " The superficial structural metadata is identical.", "tokens": [50701, 440, 34622, 15067, 26603, 307, 14800, 13, 50831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.186498340807463, "compression_ratio": 1.7180327868852459, "no_speech_prob": 1.6776770944693098e-12}, {"id": 812, "seek": 286708, "start": 2876.64, "end": 2876.7999999999997, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50843, 1079, 13, 50851], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.186498340807463, "compression_ratio": 1.7180327868852459, "no_speech_prob": 1.6776770944693098e-12}, {"id": 813, "seek": 286708, "start": 2877.0, "end": 2880.3199999999997, "text": " The cryptographic pointer traces perfectly back to the original bank report.", "tokens": [50861, 440, 9844, 12295, 23918, 26076, 6239, 646, 281, 264, 3380, 3765, 2275, 13, 51027], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.186498340807463, "compression_ratio": 1.7180327868852459, "no_speech_prob": 1.6776770944693098e-12}, {"id": 814, "seek": 286708, "start": 2880.74, "end": 2883.7999999999997, "text": " The system blindly slaps a green verified badge on the summary.", "tokens": [51048, 440, 1185, 47744, 1061, 2382, 257, 3092, 31197, 25797, 322, 264, 12691, 13, 51201], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.186498340807463, "compression_ratio": 1.7180327868852459, "no_speech_prob": 1.6776770944693098e-12}, {"id": 815, "seek": 286708, "start": 2884.2999999999997, "end": 2887.6, "text": " An investor reads it, shorts the stock, and loses millions of dollars.", "tokens": [51226, 1107, 18479, 15700, 309, 11, 19848, 264, 4127, 11, 293, 18293, 6803, 295, 3808, 13, 51391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.186498340807463, "compression_ratio": 1.7180327868852459, "no_speech_prob": 1.6776770944693098e-12}, {"id": 816, "seek": 286708, "start": 2888.06, "end": 2891.66, "text": " The watermark perfectly certified a lie because it was blind to M12.", "tokens": [51414, 440, 1281, 5638, 6239, 18580, 257, 4544, 570, 309, 390, 6865, 281, 376, 4762, 13, 51594], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.186498340807463, "compression_ratio": 1.7180327868852459, "no_speech_prob": 1.6776770944693098e-12}, {"id": 817, "seek": 286708, "start": 2891.8199999999997, "end": 2892.18, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51602, 1079, 13, 51620], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.186498340807463, "compression_ratio": 1.7180327868852459, "no_speech_prob": 1.6776770944693098e-12}, {"id": 818, "seek": 286708, "start": 2892.58, "end": 2894.18, "text": " That is the exact nightmare scenario.", "tokens": [51640, 663, 307, 264, 1900, 18724, 9005, 13, 51720], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.186498340807463, "compression_ratio": 1.7180327868852459, "no_speech_prob": 1.6776770944693098e-12}, {"id": 819, "seek": 286708, "start": 2894.54, "end": 2895.5, "text": " It's terrifying.", "tokens": [51738, 467, 311, 18106, 13, 51786], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.186498340807463, "compression_ratio": 1.7180327868852459, "no_speech_prob": 1.6776770944693098e-12}, {"id": 820, "seek": 289550, "start": 2895.5, "end": 2901.32, "text": " If a verification system only checks superficial metadata, provenance chains, or lexical parity,", "tokens": [50365, 759, 257, 30206, 1185, 787, 13834, 34622, 26603, 11, 12785, 719, 12626, 11, 420, 476, 87, 804, 44747, 11, 50656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1260264176588792, "compression_ratio": 1.435, "no_speech_prob": 2.1173971864046903e-12}, {"id": 821, "seek": 289550, "start": 2901.32, "end": 2908.0, "text": " which is exactly what our current digital watermarks do, it will be completely blind to M12-style mutations.", "tokens": [50656, 597, 307, 2293, 437, 527, 2190, 4562, 1281, 37307, 360, 11, 309, 486, 312, 2584, 6865, 281, 376, 4762, 12, 15014, 29243, 13, 50990], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1260264176588792, "compression_ratio": 1.435, "no_speech_prob": 2.1173971864046903e-12}, {"id": 822, "seek": 289550, "start": 2908.78, "end": 2914.16, "text": " It will proudly cryptographically certify a corrupted document as absolute truth.", "tokens": [51029, 467, 486, 33522, 9844, 3108, 984, 5351, 2505, 257, 39480, 4166, 382, 8236, 3494, 13, 51298], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1260264176588792, "compression_ratio": 1.435, "no_speech_prob": 2.1173971864046903e-12}, {"id": 823, "seek": 291416, "start": 2914.16, "end": 2918.22, "text": " This is terrifying, but it is also incredibly clarifying.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 307, 18106, 11, 457, 309, 307, 611, 6252, 6093, 5489, 13, 50568], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1425212174654007, "compression_ratio": 1.0178571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.861334220434885e-12}, {"id": 824, "seek": 291822, "start": 2918.22, "end": 2921.3999999999996, "text": " It slices right through the hype of digital provenance.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 19793, 558, 807, 264, 24144, 295, 4562, 12785, 719, 13, 50524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23355305989583333, "compression_ratio": 0.9016393442622951, "no_speech_prob": 2.2014156990379785e-12}, {"id": 825, "seek": 292140, "start": 2921.4, "end": 2923.32, "text": " So, what does this all mean?", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 437, 775, 341, 439, 914, 30, 50461], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1463418873873624, "compression_ratio": 1.5083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.325721429677352e-12}, {"id": 826, "seek": 292140, "start": 2923.78, "end": 2925.92, "text": " Let's bring this all the way back up to the surface.", "tokens": [50484, 961, 311, 1565, 341, 439, 264, 636, 646, 493, 281, 264, 3753, 13, 50591], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1463418873873624, "compression_ratio": 1.5083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.325721429677352e-12}, {"id": 827, "seek": 292140, "start": 2926.1, "end": 2927.96, "text": " We've gone incredibly deep today.", "tokens": [50600, 492, 600, 2780, 6252, 2452, 965, 13, 50693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1463418873873624, "compression_ratio": 1.5083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.325721429677352e-12}, {"id": 828, "seek": 292140, "start": 2928.2200000000003, "end": 2932.3, "text": " It means that the infrastructure we are currently rushing to build to verify truth on the internet,", "tokens": [50706, 467, 1355, 300, 264, 6896, 321, 366, 4362, 25876, 281, 1322, 281, 16888, 3494, 322, 264, 4705, 11, 50910], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1463418873873624, "compression_ratio": 1.5083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.325721429677352e-12}, {"id": 829, "seek": 292140, "start": 2932.76, "end": 2936.28, "text": " the billions of dollars being poured into C2PA and steganography,", "tokens": [50933, 264, 17375, 295, 3808, 885, 23270, 666, 383, 17, 10297, 293, 342, 43118, 5820, 11, 51109], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1463418873873624, "compression_ratio": 1.5083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.325721429677352e-12}, {"id": 830, "seek": 292140, "start": 2936.54, "end": 2940.36, "text": " is fundamentally flawed if it does not account for deep semantic correspondence.", "tokens": [51122, 307, 17879, 38823, 498, 309, 775, 406, 2696, 337, 2452, 47982, 38135, 13, 51313], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1463418873873624, "compression_ratio": 1.5083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.325721429677352e-12}, {"id": 831, "seek": 294036, "start": 2940.36, "end": 2942.32, "text": " We can't just rely on pointers.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 393, 380, 445, 10687, 322, 44548, 13, 50463], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14513183852373543, "compression_ratio": 1.6383763837638377, "no_speech_prob": 1.8326358226100625e-12}, {"id": 832, "seek": 294036, "start": 2942.6400000000003, "end": 2946.76, "text": " We cannot rely solely on robust locators, watermarks, or provenance chains.", "tokens": [50479, 492, 2644, 10687, 23309, 322, 13956, 1628, 3391, 11, 1281, 37307, 11, 420, 12785, 719, 12626, 13, 50685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14513183852373543, "compression_ratio": 1.6383763837638377, "no_speech_prob": 1.8326358226100625e-12}, {"id": 833, "seek": 294036, "start": 2947.02, "end": 2948.6, "text": " They are pointers, not payloads.", "tokens": [50698, 814, 366, 44548, 11, 406, 30918, 82, 13, 50777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14513183852373543, "compression_ratio": 1.6383763837638377, "no_speech_prob": 1.8326358226100625e-12}, {"id": 834, "seek": 294036, "start": 2948.76, "end": 2951.7000000000003, "text": " If I can try to synthesize the massive journey we've just been on,", "tokens": [50785, 759, 286, 393, 853, 281, 26617, 1125, 264, 5994, 4671, 321, 600, 445, 668, 322, 11, 50932], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14513183852373543, "compression_ratio": 1.6383763837638377, "no_speech_prob": 1.8326358226100625e-12}, {"id": 835, "seek": 294036, "start": 2952.1400000000003, "end": 2956.28, "text": " the next time you, the listener, see a little sparkly verified badge,", "tokens": [50954, 264, 958, 565, 291, 11, 264, 31569, 11, 536, 257, 707, 9908, 356, 31197, 25797, 11, 51161], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14513183852373543, "compression_ratio": 1.6383763837638377, "no_speech_prob": 1.8326358226100625e-12}, {"id": 836, "seek": 294036, "start": 2956.34, "end": 2960.4, "text": " or an AI watermark on a summarized news article, or a translated document,", "tokens": [51164, 420, 364, 7318, 1281, 5638, 322, 257, 14611, 1602, 2583, 7222, 11, 420, 257, 16805, 4166, 11, 51367], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14513183852373543, "compression_ratio": 1.6383763837638377, "no_speech_prob": 1.8326358226100625e-12}, {"id": 837, "seek": 294036, "start": 2960.96, "end": 2964.1600000000003, "text": " you have to remember that truth does not automatically travel with the pixels.", "tokens": [51395, 291, 362, 281, 1604, 300, 3494, 775, 406, 6772, 3147, 365, 264, 18668, 13, 51555], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14513183852373543, "compression_ratio": 1.6383763837638377, "no_speech_prob": 1.8326358226100625e-12}, {"id": 838, "seek": 294036, "start": 2964.6, "end": 2965.36, "text": " It does not.", "tokens": [51577, 467, 775, 406, 13, 51615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14513183852373543, "compression_ratio": 1.6383763837638377, "no_speech_prob": 1.8326358226100625e-12}, {"id": 839, "seek": 296536, "start": 2965.36, "end": 2971.0, "text": " Just because the digital signatures survive the AI rewriting the paragraph does not mean the truth survived.", "tokens": [50365, 1449, 570, 264, 4562, 32322, 7867, 264, 7318, 319, 19868, 264, 18865, 775, 406, 914, 264, 3494, 14433, 13, 50647], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1476297990991435, "compression_ratio": 1.6901408450704225, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109986608614513e-12}, {"id": 840, "seek": 296536, "start": 2971.6600000000003, "end": 2975.44, "text": " To truly verify a transformed document in a generative world,", "tokens": [50680, 1407, 4908, 16888, 257, 16894, 4166, 294, 257, 1337, 1166, 1002, 11, 50869], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1476297990991435, "compression_ratio": 1.6901408450704225, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109986608614513e-12}, {"id": 841, "seek": 296536, "start": 2975.6400000000003, "end": 2978.1, "text": " we need a radically more rigorous structure.", "tokens": [50879, 321, 643, 257, 35508, 544, 29882, 3877, 13, 51002], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1476297990991435, "compression_ratio": 1.6901408450704225, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109986608614513e-12}, {"id": 842, "seek": 296536, "start": 2978.6400000000003, "end": 2980.32, "text": " We need Fliction's manifest protocol.", "tokens": [51029, 492, 643, 3235, 4105, 311, 10067, 10336, 13, 51113], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1476297990991435, "compression_ratio": 1.6901408450704225, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109986608614513e-12}, {"id": 843, "seek": 296536, "start": 2980.58, "end": 2984.6200000000003, "text": " We need strict cryptographic separation between who asserted the claim,", "tokens": [51126, 492, 643, 10910, 9844, 12295, 14634, 1296, 567, 19810, 292, 264, 3932, 11, 51328], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1476297990991435, "compression_ratio": 1.6901408450704225, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109986608614513e-12}, {"id": 844, "seek": 296536, "start": 2984.76, "end": 2987.46, "text": " who verified it, and who is attesting to the transformation.", "tokens": [51335, 567, 31197, 309, 11, 293, 567, 307, 951, 8714, 281, 264, 9887, 13, 51470], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1476297990991435, "compression_ratio": 1.6901408450704225, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109986608614513e-12}, {"id": 845, "seek": 296536, "start": 2988.28, "end": 2993.7000000000003, "text": " We need typed dependency edges so one recalled wrench doesn't condemn the whole car.", "tokens": [51511, 492, 643, 33941, 33621, 8819, 370, 472, 39301, 25406, 1177, 380, 30733, 264, 1379, 1032, 13, 51782], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1476297990991435, "compression_ratio": 1.6901408450704225, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109986608614513e-12}, {"id": 846, "seek": 296536, "start": 2994.02, "end": 2994.46, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51798, 7587, 13, 51820], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1476297990991435, "compression_ratio": 1.6901408450704225, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109986608614513e-12}, {"id": 847, "seek": 299446, "start": 2994.46, "end": 2999.4, "text": " And above all, we need to accept the hard mathematical reality of Church's theorem.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 3673, 439, 11, 321, 643, 281, 3241, 264, 1152, 18894, 4103, 295, 7882, 311, 20904, 13, 50612], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09903616865142052, "compression_ratio": 1.6827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298364567679524e-12}, {"id": 848, "seek": 299446, "start": 3000.18, "end": 3003.0, "text": " A machine can only perfectly certify that meaning is preserved", "tokens": [50651, 316, 3479, 393, 787, 6239, 5351, 2505, 300, 3620, 307, 22242, 50792], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09903616865142052, "compression_ratio": 1.6827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298364567679524e-12}, {"id": 849, "seek": 299446, "start": 3003.0, "end": 3007.14, "text": " if it operates inside a tiny, strict, algebraic safe zone.", "tokens": [50792, 498, 309, 22577, 1854, 257, 5870, 11, 10910, 11, 21989, 299, 3273, 6668, 13, 50999], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09903616865142052, "compression_ratio": 1.6827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298364567679524e-12}, {"id": 850, "seek": 299446, "start": 3007.32, "end": 3010.2200000000003, "text": " And outside of that safe zone, the machine must be honest.", "tokens": [51008, 400, 2380, 295, 300, 3273, 6668, 11, 264, 3479, 1633, 312, 3245, 13, 51153], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09903616865142052, "compression_ratio": 1.6827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298364567679524e-12}, {"id": 851, "seek": 299446, "start": 3010.38, "end": 3010.66, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51161, 1779, 13, 51175], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09903616865142052, "compression_ratio": 1.6827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298364567679524e-12}, {"id": 852, "seek": 299446, "start": 3010.78, "end": 3012.7400000000002, "text": " It must say outside certified fragment.", "tokens": [51181, 467, 1633, 584, 2380, 18580, 26424, 13, 51279], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09903616865142052, "compression_ratio": 1.6827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298364567679524e-12}, {"id": 853, "seek": 299446, "start": 3012.86, "end": 3014.94, "text": " It must act as a routing mechanism, not a judge.", "tokens": [51285, 467, 1633, 605, 382, 257, 32722, 7513, 11, 406, 257, 6995, 13, 51389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09903616865142052, "compression_ratio": 1.6827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298364567679524e-12}, {"id": 854, "seek": 299446, "start": 3015.32, "end": 3019.38, "text": " It must never silently promote its own mathematical confusion into a false positive,", "tokens": [51408, 467, 1633, 1128, 40087, 9773, 1080, 1065, 18894, 15075, 666, 257, 7908, 3353, 11, 51611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09903616865142052, "compression_ratio": 1.6827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298364567679524e-12}, {"id": 855, "seek": 299446, "start": 3019.92, "end": 3021.68, "text": " just to give the user a smooth experience.", "tokens": [51638, 445, 281, 976, 264, 4195, 257, 5508, 1752, 13, 51726], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09903616865142052, "compression_ratio": 1.6827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298364567679524e-12}, {"id": 856, "seek": 302168, "start": 3021.68, "end": 3024.9199999999996, "text": " It takes us right back to that medical x-ray we talked about at the very beginning.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 2516, 505, 558, 646, 281, 300, 4625, 2031, 12, 3458, 321, 2825, 466, 412, 264, 588, 2863, 13, 50527], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13277017929974724, "compression_ratio": 1.5355450236966826, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924238904040937e-12}, {"id": 857, "seek": 302168, "start": 3024.9199999999996, "end": 3029.52, "text": " We so desperately want the clean, binary, broken, or not broken x-ray.", "tokens": [50527, 492, 370, 23726, 528, 264, 2541, 11, 17434, 11, 5463, 11, 420, 406, 5463, 2031, 12, 3458, 13, 50757], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13277017929974724, "compression_ratio": 1.5355450236966826, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924238904040937e-12}, {"id": 858, "seek": 302168, "start": 3029.8399999999997, "end": 3033.4199999999996, "text": " We want the AI to just give us a green checkmark so we don't have to think about it.", "tokens": [50773, 492, 528, 264, 7318, 281, 445, 976, 505, 257, 3092, 1520, 5638, 370, 321, 500, 380, 362, 281, 519, 466, 309, 13, 50952], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13277017929974724, "compression_ratio": 1.5355450236966826, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924238904040937e-12}, {"id": 859, "seek": 302168, "start": 3033.7599999999998, "end": 3038.8399999999997, "text": " But we are actually operating in the deep, muddy waters of complex semantic meaning.", "tokens": [50969, 583, 321, 366, 767, 7447, 294, 264, 2452, 11, 38540, 12975, 295, 3997, 47982, 3620, 13, 51223], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13277017929974724, "compression_ratio": 1.5355450236966826, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924238904040937e-12}, {"id": 860, "seek": 303884, "start": 3038.84, "end": 3057.56, "text": " It is an epistemic safety net for a world that is about to drown in generative text.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 364, 2388, 468, 3438, 4514, 2533, 337, 257, 1002, 300, 307, 466, 281, 20337, 294, 1337, 1166, 2487, 13, 51301], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21740785598754883, "compression_ratio": 1.105263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182134400510086e-12}, {"id": 861, "seek": 305756, "start": 3057.56, "end": 3060.72, "text": " Which leaves us with a final, slightly haunting thought.", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 5510, 505, 365, 257, 2572, 11, 4748, 44512, 1194, 13, 50523], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08710126157076854, "compression_ratio": 1.6486486486486487, "no_speech_prob": 2.254137198079431e-12}, {"id": 862, "seek": 305756, "start": 3061.48, "end": 3066.68, "text": " The researchers conclusively mathematically proved that a machine can never universally guarantee", "tokens": [50561, 440, 10309, 18646, 3413, 44003, 14617, 300, 257, 3479, 393, 1128, 43995, 10815, 50821], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08710126157076854, "compression_ratio": 1.6486486486486487, "no_speech_prob": 2.254137198079431e-12}, {"id": 863, "seek": 305756, "start": 3066.68, "end": 3069.7799999999997, "text": " that a paraphrased text means exactly the same thing as the original.", "tokens": [50821, 300, 257, 36992, 1703, 1937, 2487, 1355, 2293, 264, 912, 551, 382, 264, 3380, 13, 50976], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08710126157076854, "compression_ratio": 1.6486486486486487, "no_speech_prob": 2.254137198079431e-12}, {"id": 864, "seek": 305756, "start": 3070.08, "end": 3075.08, "text": " Yet we are rapidly, almost blindly, accelerating into a future where almost all the news,", "tokens": [50991, 10890, 321, 366, 12910, 11, 1920, 47744, 11, 34391, 666, 257, 2027, 689, 1920, 439, 264, 2583, 11, 51241], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08710126157076854, "compression_ratio": 1.6486486486486487, "no_speech_prob": 2.254137198079431e-12}, {"id": 865, "seek": 305756, "start": 3075.44, "end": 3078.86, "text": " the scientific research, the financial data, and the legal analysis you consume", "tokens": [51259, 264, 8134, 2132, 11, 264, 4669, 1412, 11, 293, 264, 5089, 5215, 291, 14732, 51430], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08710126157076854, "compression_ratio": 1.6486486486486487, "no_speech_prob": 2.254137198079431e-12}, {"id": 866, "seek": 305756, "start": 3078.86, "end": 3083.54, "text": " is going to be filtered, summarized, or translated by an AI before it ever reaches your eyes.", "tokens": [51430, 307, 516, 281, 312, 37111, 11, 14611, 1602, 11, 420, 16805, 538, 364, 7318, 949, 309, 1562, 14235, 428, 2575, 13, 51664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08710126157076854, "compression_ratio": 1.6486486486486487, "no_speech_prob": 2.254137198079431e-12}, {"id": 867, "seek": 308354, "start": 3083.54, "end": 3089.2799999999997, "text": " If we don't implement the rigorous separation of semantics and policy that this protocol demands,", "tokens": [50365, 759, 321, 500, 380, 4445, 264, 29882, 14634, 295, 4361, 45298, 293, 3897, 300, 341, 10336, 15107, 11, 50652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11052784105626548, "compression_ratio": 1.5384615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 2.7510120917395575e-12}, {"id": 868, "seek": 308354, "start": 3089.7599999999998, "end": 3094.02, "text": " are we building a world of flawless, unbreakable digital watermarks", "tokens": [50676, 366, 321, 2390, 257, 1002, 295, 45693, 11, 517, 13225, 712, 4562, 1281, 37307, 50889], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11052784105626548, "compression_ratio": 1.5384615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 2.7510120917395575e-12}, {"id": 869, "seek": 308354, "start": 3094.02, "end": 3096.64, "text": " that do nothing but point to entirely altered truth?", "tokens": [50889, 300, 360, 1825, 457, 935, 281, 7696, 28783, 3494, 30, 51020], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11052784105626548, "compression_ratio": 1.5384615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 2.7510120917395575e-12}, {"id": 870, "seek": 308354, "start": 3096.92, "end": 3100.68, "text": " It's something to think very carefully about the next time you drop a complex document into an AI", "tokens": [51034, 467, 311, 746, 281, 519, 588, 7500, 466, 264, 958, 565, 291, 3270, 257, 3997, 4166, 666, 364, 7318, 51222], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11052784105626548, "compression_ratio": 1.5384615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 2.7510120917395575e-12}, {"id": 871, "seek": 308354, "start": 3100.68, "end": 3103.46, "text": " and casually ask it to just summarize this.", "tokens": [51222, 293, 34872, 1029, 309, 281, 445, 20858, 341, 13, 51361], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11052784105626548, "compression_ratio": 1.5384615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 2.7510120917395575e-12}, {"id": 872, "seek": 310346, "start": 3103.98, "end": 3109.4, "text": " To give a quick break, I just say, what you do if you don't use and for advice before you invest?", "tokens": [50391, 1407, 976, 257, 1702, 1821, 11, 286, 445, 584, 11, 437, 291, 360, 498, 291, 500, 380, 764, 293, 337, 5192, 949, 291, 1963, 30, 50662], "temperature": 1.0, "avg_logprob": -3.7729366136633833, "compression_ratio": 1.6775956284153006, "no_speech_prob": 2.9455781563880734e-11}, {"id": 873, "seek": 310346, "start": 3109.62, "end": 3110.14, "text": " To cover that, we want to watch this book.", "tokens": [50673, 1407, 2060, 300, 11, 321, 528, 281, 1159, 341, 1446, 13, 50699], "temperature": 1.0, "avg_logprob": -3.7729366136633833, "compression_ratio": 1.6775956284153006, "no_speech_prob": 2.9455781563880734e-11}, {"id": 874, "seek": 310346, "start": 3110.54, "end": 3112.14, "text": " Well, we can now go to a quick break.", "tokens": [50719, 1042, 11, 321, 393, 586, 352, 281, 257, 1702, 1821, 13, 50799], "temperature": 1.0, "avg_logprob": -3.7729366136633833, "compression_ratio": 1.6775956284153006, "no_speech_prob": 2.9455781563880734e-11}, {"id": 875, "seek": 310346, "start": 3112.2, "end": 3113.62, "te